he PHP Driver for Apache Cassandra. Use Cassandra::cluster() to build a cluster instance. Use Cassandra::ssl() to build SSL options instance. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"BatchStatement","fqn":"Cassandra\\BatchStatement","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cassandra","location":{"file":"cassandra/cassandra.php","range":{"start":78327,"end":78341}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Batch statements are used to execute a series of simple or prepared statements. There are 3 types of batch statements: * `Cassandra::BATCH_LOGGED`   - this is the default batch type. This batch guarantees that either all or none of its statements will be executed. This behavior is achieved by writing a batch log on the coordinator, which slows down the execution somewhat. * `Cassandra::BATCH_UNLOGGED` - this batch will not be verified when executed, which makes it faster than a `LOGGED` batch, but means that some of its statements might fail, while others - succeed. * `Cassandra::BATCH_COUNTER`  - this batch is used for counter updates, which are, unlike other writes, not idempotent. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Bigint","fqn":"Cassandra\\Bigint","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cassandra","location":{"file":"cassandra/cassandra.php","range":{"start":93649,"end":93655}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"A PHP representation of the CQL `bigint` datatype /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Blob","fqn":"Cassandra\\Blob","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cassandra","location":{"file":"cassandra/cassandra.php","range":{"sta