 is a new magic method __invoke, but Yaf is not only works with PHP 5.3+, Yaf choose another magic method execute), you must implement the abstract method \\Yaf\\Action_Abstract::execute() in your custom action class.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Application","fqn":"Yaf\\Application","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":1286,"end":1297}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"\\Yaf\\Application provides a bootstrapping facility for applications which provides reusable resources, common- and module-based bootstrap classes and dependency checking. <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p> \\Yaf\\Application implements the singleton pattern, and \\Yaf\\Application can not be serialized or un-serialized which will cause problem when you try to use PHPUnit to write some test case for Yaf.<br/> You may use &#64;backupGlobals annotation of PHPUnit to control the backup and restore operations for global variables. thus can solve this problem. </p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Bootstrap_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf\\Bootstrap_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":32062,"end":32080}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>Bootstrap is a mechanism used to do some initial config before a Application run.<br/><br/></p> <p>User may define their own Bootstrap class by inheriting <b>\\Yaf\\Bootstrap_Abstract</b><br/><br/></p> <p>Any method declared in Bootstrap class with leading \"_init\", will be called by \\Yaf\\Application::bootstrap() one by one according to their defined order<br/><br/></p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Ini","fqn":"Yaf\\Config\\Ini","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":70273,"end":70276}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>\\Yaf\\Config\\Ini enables developers to store configuration data in a familiar INI format and read them in the application by using nested object property syntax. The INI format is specialized to provide both the ability to have a hierarchy of configuration data keys and inheritance between configuration data sections. Configuration data hierarchies are supported by separating the keys with the dot or period character (\".\"). A section may extend or inherit from another section by following the section name with a colon character (\":\") and the name of the section from which data are to be inherited.</p><br/> <b>Note:</b> <p>\\Yaf\\Config\\Ini utilizes the » parse_ini_file() PHP function. Please review this documentation to be aware of its specific behaviors, which propagate to \\Yaf\\Config\\Ini, such as how the special values of \"TRUE\", \"FALSE\", \"yes\", \"no\", and \"NULL\" are handled.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Simple","fqn":"Yaf\\Config\\Simple","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":72464,"end":72470}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Config_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf\\Config_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":40538,"end":40553}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Controller_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf\\Controller_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":33220,"end":33239}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>\\Yaf\\Controller_Abstract</b> is the heart of Yaf's system. MVC stands for Model-View-Controller and is a design pattern targeted at separating application logic from display logic.</p> <br/> <p>Every custom controller shall inherit <b>\\Yaf\\Controller_Abstract</b>.</p> <br/> <p>You will find that you can not define __construct function for your custom controller, thus, <b>\\Yaf\\Controller_Abstract</b> provides a magic method: \\Yaf\\Controller_Abstract::init().</p> <br/> <p>If you have defined a init() method in your custom controller, it will be called as long as the controller was instantiated.</p> <br/> <p>Action may have arguments, when a request coming, if there are the same name variable in the request parameters(see \\Yaf\\Request_Abstract::getParam()) after routed, Yaf will pass them to the action method (see \\Yaf\\Action_Abstract::execute()).</p> <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p>These arguments are directly fetched without filtering, it should be carefully processed before use them.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Dispatcher","fqn":"Yaf\\Dispatcher","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":8415,"end":8425}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>\\Yaf\\Dispatcher</b> purpose is to initialize the request environment, route the incoming request, and then dispatch any discovered actions; it aggregates any responses and returns them when the process is complete.</p><br/> <p><b>\\Yaf\\Dispatcher</b> also implements the Singleton pattern, meaning only a single instance of it may be available at any given time. This allows it to also act as a registry on which the other objects in the dispatch process may draw.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Exception","fqn":"Yaf\\Exception","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":59063,"end":59072}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"DispatchFailed","fqn":"Yaf\\Exception\\DispatchFailed","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":88175,"end":88189}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"LoadFailed","fqn":"Yaf\\Exception\\LoadFailed","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":88305,"end":88315}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Action","fqn":"Yaf\\Exception\\LoadFailed\\Action","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":88766,"end":88772}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"