on":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":86652,"end":86655}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>\\Yaf\\Route\\Map</b> is a built-in route, it simply convert a URI endpoint (that part of the URI which comes after the base URI: see \\Yaf\\Request_Abstract::setBaseUri()) to a controller name or action name(depends on the parameter passed to \\Yaf\\Route\\Map::__construct()) in following rule: A => controller A. A/B/C => controller A_B_C. A/B/C/D/E => controller A_B_C_D_E.</p> <br/> <p>If the second parameter of \\Yaf\\Route\\Map::__construct() is specified, then only the part before delimiter of URI will used to routing, the part after it is used to routing request parameters (see the example section of \\Yaf\\Route\\Map::__construct()).</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Regex","fqn":"Yaf\\Route\\Regex","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":83994,"end":83999}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>\\Yaf\\Route\\Regex</b> is the most flexible route among the Yaf built-in routes.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Rewrite","fqn":"Yaf\\Route\\Rewrite","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":82300,"end":82307}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>For usage, please see the example section of \\Yaf\\Route\\Rewrite::__construct()</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Simple","fqn":"Yaf\\Route\\Simple","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":79443,"end":79449}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>\\Yaf\\Route\\Simple</b> will match the query string, and find the route info.</p> <br/> <p>all you need to do is tell <b>\\Yaf\\Route\\Simple</b> what key in the $_GET is module, what key is controller, and what key is action.</p> <br/> <p>\\Yaf\\Route\\Simple::route() will always return TRUE, so it is important put <b>\\Yaf\\Route\\Simple</b> in the front of the Route stack, otherwise all the other routes will not be called</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Supervar","fqn":"Yaf\\Route\\Supervar","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":80885,"end":80893}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Route_Static","fqn":"Yaf\\Route_Static","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":59620,"end":59632}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>by default, \\Yaf\\Router only have a <b>\\Yaf\\Route_Static</b> as its default route.</p> <br/> <p><b>\\Yaf\\Route_Static</b> is designed to handle 80% of normal requirements.</p> <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p> it is unnecessary to instance a <b>\\Yaf\\Route_Static</b>, also unnecessary to add it into \\Yaf\\Router's routes stack, since there is always be one in \\Yaf\\Router's routes stack, and always be called at the last time.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Router","fqn":"Yaf\\Router","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":28973,"end":28979}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>\\Yaf\\Router</b> is the standard framework router. Routing is the process of taking a URI endpoint (that part of the URI which comes after the base URI: see \\Yaf\\Request_Abstract::setBaseUri()) and decomposing it into parameters to determine which module, controller, and action of that controller should receive the request. This values of the module, controller, action and other parameters are packaged into a \\Yaf\\Request_Abstract object which is then processed by \\Yaf\\Dispatcher. Routing occurs only once: when the request is initially received and before the first controller is dispatched. \\Yaf\\Router is designed to allow for mod_rewrite-like functionality using pure PHP structures. It is very loosely based on Ruby on Rails routing and does not require any prior knowledge of webserver URL rewriting</p> <br/> <b>Default Route</b> <br/> <p><b>\\Yaf\\Router</b> comes pre-configured with a default route \\Yaf\\Route_Static, which will match URIs in the shape of controller/action. Additionally, a module name may be specified as the first path element, allowing URIs of the form module/controller/action. Finally, it will also match any additional parameters appended to the URI by default - controller/action/var1/value1/var2/value2.</p> <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p>Module name must be defined in config, considering application.module=\"Index,Foo,Bar\", in this case, only index, foo and bar can be considered as a module name. if doesn't config, there is only one module named \"Index\".</p> <br/> <p>** See examples by opening the external documentation</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Session","fqn":"Yaf\\Session","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":24194,"end":24201}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Simple","fqn":"Yaf\\View\\Simple","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf_namespace.php","range":{"start":74935,"end":74941}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<b>\\Yaf\\View\\Simple</b> is the built-in template engine in Yaf, it is a simple but fast template engine, and only support PHP script template. /","params":[{"name":"tpl_str","declared_type":"string","description":"string template"},{"name":"vars","declared_type":"array","description":null}],"return_type":"void|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Action_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf_Action_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":40983,"end":41002}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>A action can be defined in a separate file in Yaf(see Yaf_Controller_Abstract). that is a action method can also be a <b>Yaf_Action_Abstract</b> class.</P> <br/> <p>Since there should be a entry point which can be called by Yaf (as of PHP 5.3, there is a new magic method __invoke, but Yaf is not only works with PHP 5.3+, Yaf choose another magic method execute), you must implement the abstract method Yaf_Action_Abstract::execute() in your custom action class.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Application","fqn":"Yaf_Application","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":1509,"end":1524}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Yaf_Application provides a bootstrapping facility for applications which provides reusable resources, common- and module-based bootstrap classes and dependency checking. <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p> Yaf_Application implements the singleton pattern, and Yaf_Application can not be serialized or un-serialized which will cause problem when you try to use PHPUnit to write some test case for Yaf.<br/> You may use &#64;backupGlobals annotation of PHPUnit to control the backup and restore operations for global variables. thus can solve this problem. </p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Bootstrap_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf_Bootstrap_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":33487,"end":33509}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>Bootstrap is a mechanism used to do some initial config before a Application run.<br/><br/></p> <p>User may define their own Bootstrap class by inheriting <b>Yaf_Bootstrap_Abstract</b><br/><br/></p> <p>Any method declared in Bootstrap class with leading \"_init\", will be called by Yaf_Application::bootstrap() one by one according to their defined order<br/><br/></p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Config_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf_Config_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":42045,"end":42064}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Config_Ini","fqn":"Yaf_Config_Ini","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":68566,"end":68580}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>Yaf_Config_Ini enables developers to store configuration data in a familiar INI format and read them in the application by using nested object property syntax. The INI format is specialized to provide both the ability to have a hierarchy of configuration data keys and inheritance between configuration data sections. Configuration data hierarchies are supported by separating the keys with the dot or period character (\".\"). A section may extend or inherit from another section by following the section name with a colon character (\":\") and the name of the section from which data are to be inherited.</p><br/> <b>Note:</b> <p>Yaf_Config_Ini utilizes the » parse_ini_file() PHP function. Please review this documentation to be aware of its specific behaviors, which propagate to Yaf_Config_Ini, such as how the special values of \"TRUE\", \"FALSE\", \"yes\", \"no\", and \"NULL\" are handled.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Config_Simple","fqn":"Yaf_Config_Simple","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":71304,"end":71321}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Controller_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf_Controller_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":34645,"end":34668}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>Yaf_Controller_Abstract</b> is the heart of Yaf's system. MVC stands for Model-View-Controller and is a design pattern targeted at separating application logic from display logic.</p> <br/> <p>Every custom controller shall inherit <b>Yaf_Controller_Abstract</b>.</p> <br/> <p>You will find that you can not define __construct function for your custom controller, thus, <b>Yaf_Controller_Abstract</b> provides a magic method: Yaf_Controller_Abstract::init().</p> <br/> <p>If you have defined a init() method in your custom controller, it will be called as long as the controller was instantiated.</p> <br/> <p>Action may have arguments, when a request coming, if there are the same name variable in the request parameters(see Yaf_Request_Abstract::getParam()) after routed, Yaf will pass them to the action method (see Yaf_Action_Abstract::execute()).</p> <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p>These arguments are directly fetched without filtering, it should be carefully processed before use them.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Dispatcher","fqn":"Yaf_Dispatcher","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":8503,"end":8517}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>Yaf_Dispatcher</b> purpose is to initialize the request environment, route the incoming request, and then dispatch any discovered actions; it aggregates any responses and returns them when the process is complete.</p><br/> <p><b>Yaf_Dispatcher</b> also implements the Singleton pattern, meaning only a single instance of it may be available at any given time. This allows it to also act as a registry on which the other objects in the dispatch process may draw.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception","fqn":"Yaf_Exception","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":64143,"end":64156}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_DispatchFailed","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_DispatchFailed","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":89481,"end":89509}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":89626,"end":89650}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_Action","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_Action","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":90114,"end":90145}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_Controller","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_Controller","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":89944,"end":89979}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_Module","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_Module","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":89774,"end":89805}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_View","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_LoadFailed_View","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":90278,"end":90307}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_RouterFailed","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_RouterFailed","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":89334,"end":89360}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_StartupError","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_StartupError","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":89190,"end":89216}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Exception_TypeError","fqn":"Yaf_Exception_TypeError","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":89047,"end":89070}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Loader","fqn":"Yaf_Loader","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":18959,"end":18969}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>Yaf_Loader</b> introduces a comprehensive autoloading solution for Yaf.</p> <br/> <p>The first time an instance of Yaf_Application is retrieved, <b>Yaf_Loader</b> will instance a singleton, and registers itself with spl_autoload. You retrieve an instance using the Yaf_Loader::getInstance()</p> <br/> <p><b>Yaf_Loader</b> attempt to load a class only one shot, if failed, depend on yaf.use_spl_autoload, if this config is On Yaf_Loader::autoload() will return FALSE, thus give the chance to other autoload function. if it is Off (by default), Yaf_Loader::autoload() will return TRUE, and more important is that a very useful warning will be triggered (very useful to find out why a class could not be loaded).</p> <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p>Please keep yaf.use_spl_autoload Off unless there is some library have their own autoload mechanism and impossible to rewrite it.</p> <br/> <p>If you want <b>Yaf_Loader</b> search some classes(libraries) in the local class directory(which is defined in application.ini, and by default, it is application.directory . \"/library\"), you should register the class prefix using the Yaf_Loader::registerLocalNameSpace()</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Plugin_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf_Plugin_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":53805,"end":53824}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>Plugins allow for easy extensibility and customization of the framework.</p> <br/> <p>Plugins are classes. The actual class definition will vary based on the component -- you may need to implement this interface, but the fact remains that the plugin is itself a class.</p> <br/> <p>A plugin could be loaded into Yaf by using Yaf_Dispatcher::registerPlugin(), after registered, All the methods which the plugin implemented according to this interface, will be called at the proper time.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Registry","fqn":"Yaf_Registry","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":23761,"end":23773}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>All methods of <b>Yaf_Registry</b> declared as static, making it universally accessible. This provides the ability to get or set any custom data from anyway in your code as necessary.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Request_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf_Request_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":44519,"end":44539}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Request_Http","fqn":"Yaf_Request_Http","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":66203,"end":66219}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Request_Simple","fqn":"Yaf_Request_Simple","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":66689,"end":66707}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<b>Yaf_Request_Simple</b> is particularly used for test purpose. ie. simulate a spacial request under CLI mode. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Response_Abstract","fqn":"Yaf_Response_Abstract","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":56700,"end":56721}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Response_Cli","fqn":"Yaf_Response_Cli","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":65959,"end":65975}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":null,"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Response_Http","fqn":"Yaf_Response_Http","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":64363,"end":64380}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":null,"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Route_Map","fqn":"Yaf_Route_Map","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":87949,"end":87962}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>Yaf_Route_Map</b> is a built-in route, it simply convert a URI endpoint (that part of the URI which comes after the base URI: see Yaf_Request_Abstract::setBaseUri()) to a controller name or action name(depends on the parameter passed to Yaf_Route_Map::__construct()) in following rule: A => controller A. A/B/C => controller A_B_C. A/B/C/D/E => controller A_B_C_D_E.</p> <br/> <p>If the second parameter of Yaf_Route_Map::__construct() is specified, then only the part before delimiter of URI will used to routing, the part after it is used to routing request parameters (see the example section of Yaf_Route_Map::__construct()).</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Route_Regex","fqn":"Yaf_Route_Regex","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":85200,"end":85215}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>Yaf_Route_Regex</b> is the most flexible route among the Yaf built-in routes.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Route_Rewrite","fqn":"Yaf_Route_Rewrite","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":83410,"end":83427}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>For usage, please see the example section of Yaf_Route_Rewrite::__construct()</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Route_Simple","fqn":"Yaf_Route_Simple","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":80576,"end":80592}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>Yaf_Route_Simple</b> will match the query string, and find the route info.</p> <br/> <p>all you need to do is tell <b>Yaf_Route_Simple</b> what key in the $_GET is module, what key is controller, and what key is action.</p> <br/> <p>Yaf_Route_Simple::route() will always return TRUE, so it is important put <b>Yaf_Route_Simple</b> in the front of the Route stack, otherwise all the other routes will not be called</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Route_Static","fqn":"Yaf_Route_Static","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":79242,"end":79258}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>by default, Yaf_Router only have a <b>Yaf_Route_Static</b> as its default route.</p> <br/> <p><b>Yaf_Route_Static</b> is designed to handle 80% of normal requirements.</p> <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p> it is unnecessary to instance a <b>Yaf_Route_Static</b>, also unnecessary to add it into Yaf_Router's routes stack, since there is always be one in Yaf_Router's routes stack, and always be called at the last time.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Route_Supervar","fqn":"Yaf_Route_Supervar","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":82008,"end":82026}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Router","fqn":"Yaf_Router","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":30493,"end":30503}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p><b>Yaf_Router</b> is the standard framework router. Routing is the process of taking a URI endpoint (that part of the URI which comes after the base URI: see Yaf_Request_Abstract::setBaseUri()) and decomposing it into parameters to determine which module, controller, and action of that controller should receive the request. This values of the module, controller, action and other parameters are packaged into a Yaf_Request_Abstract object which is then processed by Yaf_Dispatcher. Routing occurs only once: when the request is initially received and before the first controller is dispatched. Yaf_Router is designed to allow for mod_rewrite-like functionality using pure PHP structures. It is very loosely based on Ruby on Rails routing and does not require any prior knowledge of webserver URL rewriting</p> <br/> <b>Default Route</b> <br/> <p><b>Yaf_Router</b> comes pre-configured with a default route Yaf_Route_Static, which will match URIs in the shape of controller/action. Additionally, a module name may be specified as the first path element, allowing URIs of the form module/controller/action. Finally, it will also match any additional parameters appended to the URI by default - controller/action/var1/value1/var2/value2.</p> <br/> <b>Note:</b> <p>Module name must be defined in config, considering application.module=\"Index,Foo,Bar\", in this case, only index, foo and bar can be considered as a module name. if doesn't config, there is only one module named \"Index\".</p> <br/> <p>** See examples by opening the external documentation</p> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_Session","fqn":"Yaf_Session","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":25137,"end":25148}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yaf_View_Simple","fqn":"Yaf_View_Simple","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yaf","location":{"file":"yaf/yaf.php","range":{"start":74146,"end":74161}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<b>Yaf_View_Simple</b> is the built-in template engine in Yaf, it is a simple but fast template engine, and only support PHP script template. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yar_Client","fqn":"Yar_Client","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yar","location":{"file":"yar/yar.php","range":{"start":1968,"end":1978}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":null,"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yar_Client_Exception","fqn":"Yar_Client_Exception","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yar","location":{"file":"yar/yar.php","range":{"start":5705,"end":5725}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Class Yar_Client_Exception Date 2018/6/9 下午3:05 /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yar_Client_Packager_Exception","fqn":"Yar_Client_Packager_Exception","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yar","location":{"file":"yar/yar.php","range":{"start":6305,"end":6334}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":null,"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yar_Client_Protocol_Exception","fqn":"Yar_Client_Protocol_Exception","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yar","location":{"file":"yar/yar.php","range":{"start":6374,"end":6403}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":null,"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yar_Client_Transport_Exception","fqn":"Yar_Client_Transport_Exception","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yar","location":{"file":"yar/yar.php","range":{"start":6235,"end":6265}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":null,"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"Yar_Concurrent_Client","fqn":"Yar_Concurrent_Client","kind":"Class","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"yar","location":{"fil