CUBRID CAS server (BROKER_PORT configured in $CUBRID/conf/cubrid_broker.conf). </p> Name of database. </p> User name for the database. Default value is 'PUBLIC'. </p> User password. Default value is empty string, i.e. no password is defined. </p> If a second call is made to cubrid_connect() with the same arguments, no new link will be established, but instead, the connection identifier of the already opened connection will be returned. The new_link parameter modifies this behavior and makes cubrid_connect() always open a new connection, even if cubrid_connect() was called before with the same parameters. </p> a CUBRID connection identifier on success or false on failure. </p> /","params":[{"name":"host","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"port","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"dbname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"userid","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"passwd","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"new_link","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_connect_with_url","fqn":"cubrid_connect_with_url","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":2628,"end":2651}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"conn_url","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"userid","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"passwd","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"new_link","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.1)<br/> Establish the environment for connecting to CUBRID server. A character string that contains server connection information.<br /> Syntax: 'CUBRID:&gt;host&lt;:&gt;port&lt;:&gt;dbname&lt;:&gt;username&lt;:&gt;password&lt;:?&gt;params&lt;'.<br /> E.g. <i>CUBRID:127.0.0.1:33088:demodb:dba:123456:?autocommit=off&althost=10.34.63.132:33088&rctime=100</i> </p> User name for the database. Default value is 'PUBLIC'. </p> User password. Default value is empty string, i.e. no password is defined. </p> If a second call is made to cubrid_connect() with the same arguments, no new link will be established, but instead, the connection identifier of the already opened connection will be returned. The new_link parameter modifies this behavior and makes cubrid_connect() always open a new connection, even if cubrid_connect() was called before with the same parameters. </p> a CUBRID connection identifier on success or false on failure. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_url","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"userid","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"passwd","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"new_link","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_current_oid","fqn":"cubrid_current_oid","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":40078,"end":40096}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"req_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Get OID of the current cursor location R