ed by cubrid_connect() is assumed. </p> the error number from the last CUBRID function, or 0 (zero) if no error occurred. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_error","fqn":"cubrid_error","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":12852,"end":12864}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.1)<br/> Get the error message. Same as cubrid_error_msg(); The CUBRID connection. </p> Error message that occurred. </p> /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_error_code","fqn":"cubrid_error_code","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":14080,"end":14097}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Get error code for the most recent function call. Same as cubrid_errno(); Error code of the error that occurred, or 0 (zero) if no error occurred. </p> /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_error_code_facility","fqn":"cubrid_error_code_facility","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":40898,"end":40924}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Get the facility code of error Facility code of the error code that occurred: CUBRID_FACILITY_DBMS, CUBRID_FACILITY_CAS, CUBRID_FACILITY_CCI, CUBRID_FACILITY_CLIENT </p> /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_error_msg","fqn":"cubrid_error_msg","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":13157,"end":13173}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Get last error message for the most recent function call. Same as cubrid_error(); Error message that occurred. </p> /","params":[],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_execute","fqn":"cubrid_execute","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":7420,"end":7434}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"sql","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"option","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Execute a prepared SQL statement Connection identifier. </p> SQL to be executed. </p> Query execution option CUBRID_INCLUDE_OID, CUBRID_ASYNC, CUBRID_EXEC_QUERY_ALL. </p> Request identifier, when process is successful, or FALSE, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"sql","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_fetch","fqn":"cubrid_fetch","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":19024,"end":19036}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"mixed"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Fetch the next row from a result set result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> Array type of the fetched result CUBRID_NUM, CUBRID_ASSOC, CUBRID_BOTH, CUBRID_OBJECT. If you want to operate the lob object, you can use CUBRID_LOB. </p> <ul> <li>array or object, when process is successful.</li> <li>FALSE, when there are no more rows;</li> <li>NULL, when process is unsuccessful.</li> </ul> <p> The result can be received either as an array or as an object, and you can decide which data type to use by setting the type argument. The type variable can be set to one of the following values: </p> <ul> <li>CUBRID_NUM : Numerical array (0-based)</li> <li>CUBRID_ASSOC : Associative array</li> <li>CUBRID_BOTH : Numerical & Associative array (default)</li> <li>CUBRID_OBJECT : object that has the attribute name as the column name of query result</li> </ul> <p> When type argument is omitted, the result will be received using CUBRID_BOTH option as default. When you want to receive query result in object data type, the column name of the result must obey the naming rules for identifiers in PHP. For example, column name such as \"count(*)\" cannot be received in object type. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"mixed","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_fetch_array","fqn":"cubrid_fetch_array","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":20792,"end":20810}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Fetch a result row as an associative array, a numeric array, or both The type of array that is to be fetched. It's a constant and can take the following values: CUBRID_ASSOC, CUBRID_NUM, and CUBRID_BOTH. </p> Returns an array of strings that corresponds to the fetched row, when process is successful. FALSE, when there are no more rows; NULL, when process is unsuccessful. </p> <p> The type of returned array depends on how result_type is defined. By using CUBRID_BOTH (default), you'll get an array with both associative and number indices, and you can decide which data type to use by setting the type argument. The type variable can be set to one of the following values: </p> <ul> <li>CUBRID_NUM : Numerical array (0-based)</li> <li>CUBRID_ASSOC : Associative array</li> <li>CUBRID_BOTH : Numerical & Associative array (default)</li> </ul> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":null},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_fetch_assoc","fqn":"cubrid_fetch_assoc","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":21429,"end":21447}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Return the associative array that corresponds to the fetched row result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> Type can only be CUBRID_LOB, this parameter will be used only when you need to operate the lob object. </p> Associative array, when process is successful. FALSE, when there are no more rows; NULL, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_fetch_field","fqn":"cubrid_fetch_field","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":24678,"end":24696}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"object"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.1)<br/> Get column information from a result and return as an object result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> The numerical field offset. If the field offset is not specified, the next field that was not yet retrieved by this function is retrieved. The field_offset starts at 0. </p> an object containing field information. The properties of the object are: </p> <ul> <li>name - column name</li> <li>table - name of the table the column belongs to</li> <li>def - default value of the column</li> <li>max_length - maximum length of the column</li> <li>not_null - 1 if the column cannot be NULL</li> <li>primary_key - 1 if the column is a primary key</li> <li>unique_key - 1 if the column is a unique key</li> <li>multiple_key - 1 if the column is a non-unique key</li> <li>numeric - 1 if the column is numeric</li> <li>blob - 1 if the column is a BLOB</li> <li>type - the type of the column</li> <li>unsigned - 1 if the column is unsigned</li> <li>zerofill - 1 if the column is zero-filled</li> </ul> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"object","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_fetch_lengths","fqn":"cubrid_fetch_lengths","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":23352,"end":23372}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Return an array with the lengths of the values of each field from the current row result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> A numerical array of lengths on success, or false on failure. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_fetch_object","fqn":"cubrid_fetch_object","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":22439,"end":22458}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"class_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"params","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"array","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"object"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Fetch the next row and return it as an object result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> The name of the class to instantiate. If not specified, a stdClass (stdClass is PHP's generic empty class that's used when casting other types to objects) object is returned. </p> An optional array of parameters to pass to the constructor for class_name objects. </p> Type can only be CUBRID_LOB, this parameter will be used only when you need to operate the lob object. </p> an object with string properties that correspond to the fetched row, or false if there are no more rows, or NULL, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"class_name","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"params","declared_type":"array","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"object","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_fetch_row","fqn":"cubrid_fetch_row","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":19637,"end":19653}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Return a numerical array with the values of the current row result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> Type can only be CUBRID_LOB, this parameter will be used only when you need to operate the lob object. </p> A numerical array, when process is successful. FALSE, when there are no more rows; NULL, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_field_flags","fqn":"cubrid_field_flags","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":29966,"end":29984}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Return a string with the flags of the given field offset result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> The numerical field offset. The field_offset starts at 0. If field_offset does not exist, an error of level E_WARNING is also issued. </p> a string of flags associated with the result, or FALSE when invalid field_offset value, or -1 if SQL sentence is not SELECT. </p> <p> The following flags are reported, if your version of CUBRID is current enough to support them: \"not_null\", \"primary_key\", \"unique_key\", \"foreign_key\", \"auto_increment\", \"shared\", \"reverse_index\", \"reverse_unique\", and \"timestamp\". </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_field_len","fqn":"cubrid_field_len","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":28305,"end":28321}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Get the maximum length of the specified field result comes from a call to cubrid_execute() </p> The field_offset starts at 0. If field_offset does not exist, an error of level E_WARNING is also issued. </p> Maximum length, when process is successful. FALSE on failure. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_s