). </p> Name of database. </p> User name for the database. Default value is 'PUBLIC'. </p> User password. Default value is empty string, i.e. no password is defined. </p> Connection identifier, when process is successful. FALSE, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"host","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"port","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"dbname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"userid","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"passwd","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_pconnect_with_url","fqn":"cubrid_pconnect_with_url","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":4488,"end":4512}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"conn_url","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"userid","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"passwd","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.1)<br/> Open a persistent connection to CUBRID server A character string that contains server connection information.<br /> Syntax: 'CUBRID:&gt;host&lt;:&gt;port&lt;:&gt;dbname&lt;:&gt;username&lt;:&gt;password&lt;:?&gt;params&lt;'.<br /> E.g. CUBRID:127.0.0.1:33088:demodb:dba:123456:?autocommit=off&althost=10.34.63.132:33088&rctime=100 </p> User name for the database. Default value is 'PUBLIC'. </p> User password. Default value is empty string, i.e. no password is defined. </p> Connection identifier, when process is successful. FALSE, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_url","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"userid","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"passwd","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_ping","fqn":"cubrid_ping","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":31694,"end":31705}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.1)<br/> Ping a server connection or reconnect if there is no connection The CUBRID connection identifier. If the connection identifier is not specified, the last connection opened by cubrid_connect() is assumed. </p> true if the connection to the server is working, otherwise false. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_prepare","fqn":"cubrid_prepare","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":53238,"end":53252}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"prepare_stmt","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"option","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Prepare an SQL statement for execution Connection identifier. </p> Prepare query. </p> OID return option CUBRID_INCLUDE_OID. </p> Request identifier, if process is successful; FALSE, if process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"prepare_stmt","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_put","fqn":"cubrid_put","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":53891,"end":53901}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"oid","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"attr","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"value","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Update a column using OID Connection identifier. </p> OID of the instance that you want to update. </p> Name of the attribute that you want to update. </p> New value that you want to assign to the attribute. </p> TRUE, when process is successful. FALSE, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"oid","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"attr","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"value","declared_type":"mixed","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_query","fqn":"cubrid_query","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":6825,"end":6837}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"query","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.1)<br/> Send a CUBRID query A SQL query. Data inside the query should be properly escaped. </p> The CUBRID connection. If the connection identifier is not specified, the last connection opened by cubrid_connect() is assumed. </p> For SELECT, SHOW, DESCRIBE, EXPLAIN and other statements returning resultset, cubrid_query() returns a resource on success, or false on error. </li> <li> For other type of SQL statements, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, etc, cubrid_query() returns true on success or false on error. </li> <p> The returned result resource should be passed to cubrid_fetch_array(), and other functions for dealing with result tables, to access the returned data. </p> <p> Use cubrid_num_rows() to find out how many rows were returned for a SELECT statement. </p> <p> Use cubrid_affected_rows() to find out how many rows were affected by a DELETE, INSERT, REPLACE, or UPDATE statement. </p> <li> cubrid_query() will also fail and return false if the user does not have permission to access the table(s) referenced by the query. </li> </ul> /","params":[{"name":"query","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_real_escape_string","fqn":"cubrid_real_escape_string","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":30598,"end":30623}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"unescaped_string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Escapes special characters in a string for use in an SQL statement The string that is to be escaped. </p> The CUBRID connection. If the connection identifier is not specified, the last connection opened by cubrid_connect() is assumed. </p> Escaped string version of the given string, on success. FALSE on failure. </p> /","params":[{"name":"unescaped_string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_result","fqn":"cubrid_result","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":16159,"end":16172}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Return the value of a specific field in a specific row The row number from the result that's being retrieved. Row numbers start at 0. </p> The name or offset of the field being retrieved. </p> <p> It can be the field's offset, the field's name, or the field's table dot field name (tablename.fieldname). If the column name has been aliased ('select foo as bar from...'), use the alias instead of the column name. If undefined, the first field is retrieved. </p> Value of a specific field, on success (NULL if value if null). FALSE on failure. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":null},{"name":"row","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field","declared_type":"mixed","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_rollback","fqn":"cubrid_rollback","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.php","range":{"start":39680,"end":39695}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, CUBRID &gt;= 8.3.0)<br/> Roll back a transaction Connection identifier. </p> TRUE, when process is successful. FALSE, when process is unsuccessful. </p> /","params":[{"name":"conn_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"cubrid_schema","fqn":"cubrid_schema","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"cubrid","location":{"file":"cubrid/cubrid.ph