tion about sunset/sunrise and twilight begin/end Timestamp. </p> Latitude in degrees. </p> Longitude in degrees. </p> sunrise: int|bool, sunset: int|bool, transit: int|bool, civil_twilight_begin: int|bool, civil_twilight_end: int|bool, nautical_twilight_begin: int|bool, nautical_twilight_end: int|bool, astronomical_twilight_begin: int|bool, astronomical_twilight_end: int|bool, }|false Returns array on success or <strong><code>false</code></strong> on failure. The structure of the array is detailed in the following list: <table> <tr><td>sunrise</td><td>The timestamp of the sunrise (zenith angle = 90°35&#039;).</td></tr> <tr><td>sunset</td><td>The timestamp of the sunset (zenith angle = 90°35&#039;).</td></tr> <tr><td>transit</td><td>The timestamp when the sun is at its zenith, i.e. has reached its topmost point.</td></tr> <tr><td>civil_twilight_begin</td><td>The start of the civil dawn (zenith angle = 96°). It ends at <code>sunrise</code>.</td></tr> <tr><td>civil_twilight_end</td><td>The end of the civil dusk (zenith angle = 96°). It starts at <code>sunset</code>.</td></tr> <tr><td>nautical_twilight_begin</td><td>The start of the nautical dawn (zenith angle = 102°). It ends at <code>civil_twilight_begin</code>.</td></tr> <tr><td>nautical_twilight_end</td><td>The end of the nautical dusk (zenith angle = 102°). It starts at <code>civil_twilight_end</code>.</td></tr> <tr><td>astronomical_twilight_begin</td><td>The start of the astronomical dawn (zenith angle = 108°). It ends at <code>nautical_twilight_begin</code>.</td></tr> <tr><td>astronomical_twilight_end</td><td>The end of the astronomical dusk (zenith angle = 108°). It starts at <code>nautical_twilight_end</code>.</td></tr> </table> <br> The values of the array elements are either UNIX timestamps, <strong><code>false</code></strong> if the sun is below the respective zenith for the whole day, or <strong><code>true</code></strong> if the sun is above the respective zenith for the whole day. /","params":[{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"latitude","declared_type":"float","description":"<p>"},{"name":"longitude","declared_type":"float","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array{","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"date_sunrise","fqn":"date_sunrise","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"date","location":{"file":"date/date.php","range":{"start":49468,"end":49480}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"returnFormat","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"latitude","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"longitude","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"zenith","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"utcOffset","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|int|float|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|int|float|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns time of sunrise for a given day and location The timestamp of the day from which the sunrise time is taken. </p> <table> format constants <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>constant</td> <td>description</td> <td>example</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>SUNFUNCS_RET_STRING</td> <td>returns the result as string</td> <td>16:46</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>SUNFUNCS_RET_DOUBLE</td> <td>returns the result as float</td> <td>16.78243132</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>SUNFUNCS_RET_TIMESTAMP</td> <td>returns the result as integer (timestamp)</td> <td>1095034606</td> </tr> </table> </p> Defaults to North, pass in a negative value for South. See also: date.default_latitude </p> Defaults to East, pass in a negative value for West. See also: date.default_longitude </p> Default: date.sunrise_zenith </p> success or false on failure. /","params":[{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"returnFormat","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"latitude","declared_type":"float|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"longitude","declared_type":"float|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"zenith","declared_type":"float|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"utcOffset","declared_type":"float|null","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"string|int|float|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"date_sunset","fqn":"date_sunset","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"date","location":{"file":"date/date.php","range":{"start":51096,"end":51107}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"returnFormat","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"latitude","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"longitude","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"zenith","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"utcOffset","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|int|float|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|int|float|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns time of sunset for a given day and loca