the columns matching the specified parameters. The rows are composed of the following columns: <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Column name</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>TABLE_CAT</td> <td>Name of the catalog. The value is NULL if this table does not have catalogs.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>TABLE_SCHEM</td> <td>Name of the schema.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>TABLE_NAME</td> <td>Name of the table or view.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>COLUMN_NAME</td> <td>Name of the column.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>DATA_TYPE</td> <td>The SQL data type for the column represented as an integer value.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>TYPE_NAME</td> <td>A string representing the data type for the column.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>COLUMN_SIZE</td> <td>An integer value representing the size of the column.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>BUFFER_LENGTH</td> <td> Maximum number of bytes necessary to store data from this column. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>DECIMAL_DIGITS</td> <td> The scale of the column, or null where scale is not applicable. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>NUM_PREC_RADIX</td> <td> An integer value of either 10 (representing an exact numeric data type), 2 (representing an approximate numeric data type), or null (representing a data type for which radix is not applicable). </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>NULLABLE</td> <td>An integer value representing whether the column is nullable or not.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>REMARKS</td> <td>Description of the column.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>COLUMN_DEF</td> <td>Default value for the column.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>SQL_DATA_TYPE</td> <td>An integer value representing the size of the column.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>SQL_DATETIME_SUB</td> <td> Returns an integer value representing a datetime subtype code, or null for SQL data types to which this does not apply. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>CHAR_OCTET_LENGTH</td> <td> Maximum length in octets for a character data type column, which matches COLUMN_SIZE for single-byte character set data, or null for non-character data types. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ORDINAL_POSITION</td> <td>The 1-indexed position of the column in the table.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IS_NULLABLE</td> <td> A string value where 'YES' means that the column is nullable and 'NO' means that the column is not nullable. </td> </tr> /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"qualifier","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"schema","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"table_name","declared_type":"string","description":null},{"name":"column_name","declared_type":"string","description":null}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_commit","fqn":"db2_commit","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":1963,"end":1973}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Commits a transaction A valid database connection resource variable as returned from db2_connect or db2_pconnect. </p> /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_conn_error","fqn":"db2_conn_error","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":40881,"end":40895}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns a string containing the SQLSTATE returned by the last connection attempt A connection resource associated with a connection that initially succeeded, but which over time became invalid. </p> Returns an empty string if there is no error associated with the last connection attempt. /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_conn_errormsg","fqn":"db2_conn_errormsg","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":40331,"end":40348}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the last connection error message and SQLCODE value A connection resource associated with a connection that initially succeeded, but which over time became invalid. </p> from a failed connection attempt. If there is no error associated with the last connection attempt, db2_conn_errormsg returns an empty string. /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_connect","fqn":"db2_connect","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":1529,"end":1540}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"database","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"username","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"password","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"options","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns a connection to a database For a cataloged connection to a database, this parameter represents the connection alias in the DB2 client catalog. </p> <p> For an uncataloged connection to a database, this parameter represents a complete DSN in the following format: DRIVER=driver;DATABASE=database;HOSTNAME=hostname;PORT=port;PROTOCOL=TCPIP;UID=username;PWD=password; </p> The username with which you are connecting to the database, or null if the $database parameter contains a DSN which already provides the username for the connection. </p> The password with which you are connecting to the database, or null if the $database parameter contains a DSN which already provides the password for the connection. </p> An associative array of connection options that affect the behavior of the connection, where valid array keys include: autocommit <p> Passing the DB2_AUTOCOMMIT_ON value turns autocommit on for this connection handle. </p> <p> Passing the DB2_AUTOCOMMIT_OFF value turns autocommit off for this connection handle. </p> successful. If the connection attempt fails, db2_connect returns false. /","params":[{"name":"database","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"username","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"password","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"options","declared_type":"array","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_cursor_type","fqn":"db2_cursor_type","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":47967,"end":47982}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stmt","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the cursor type used by a statement resource A valid statement resource. </p> resource uses a forward-only cursor or DB2_SCROLLABLE if the statement resource uses a scrollable cursor. /","params":[{"name":"stmt","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_escape_string","fqn":"db2_escape_string","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":56353,"end":56370}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string_literal","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Used to escape certain characters The string that contains special characters that need to be modified. Characters that are prepended with a backslash are \\x00, \\n, \\r, \\, ', \" and \\x1a. </p> noted above prepended with backslashes. /","params":[{"name":"string_literal","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_exec","fqn":"db2_exec","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":37367,"end":37375}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"statement","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"options","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Executes an SQL statement directly A valid database connection resource variable as returned from db2_connect or db2_pconnect. </p> An SQL statement. The statement cannot contain any parameter markers. </p> An associative array containing statement options. You can use this parameter to request a scrollable cursor on database servers that support this functionality. cursor </p> <p> Passing the DB2_FORWARD_ONLY value requests a forward-only cursor for this SQL statement. This is the default type of cursor, and it is supported by all database servers. It is also much faster than a scrollable cursor. </p> <p> Passing the DB2_SCROLLABLE value requests a scrollable cursor for this SQL statement. This type of cursor enables you to fetch rows non-sequentially from the database server. However, it is only supported by DB2 servers, and is much slower than forward-only cursors. </p> or false if the database failed to execute the SQL statement. /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"statement","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"options","declared_type":"array","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_execute","fqn":"db2_execute","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":39325,"end":39336}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stmt","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"parameters","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Executes a prepared SQL statement A prepared statement returned from db2_prepare. </p> An array of input parameters matching any parameter markers contained in the prepared statement. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stmt","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"parameters","declared_type":"array","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"db2_fetch_array","fqn":"db2_fetch_array","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"ibm_db2","location":{"file":"ibm_db2/ibm_db2.php","range":{"start":51272,"end":51287}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stmt","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row_number","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns an array, indexed by column position, representing a row in a result set A valid stmt resource containing a result set. </p> Requests a specific 1-indexed row from the result set. Passing this parameter results in a PHP warning if the result set uses a forward-only cursor. </p> representing the next or requested row in the result set. Returns false if there are no rows left in the result set, or if the row requested by row_number does not exist in the result set. /","params":[{"name":"stmt","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"row_number","declared_type":"int","descriptio