arameters":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"regs","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Regular expression match Case sensitive regular expression. </p> The input string. </p> If matches are found for parenthesized substrings of <i>pattern</i> and the function is called with the third argument <i>regs</i>, the matches will be stored in the elements of the array <i>regs</i>. </p> <p> $regs[1] will contain the substring which starts at the first left parenthesis; $regs[2] will contain the substring starting at the second, and so on. $regs[0] will contain a copy of the complete string matched. </p> <i>pattern</i> was found in <i>string</i>, or <b>FALSE</b> if no matches were found or an error occurred. </p> <p> If the optional parameter <i>regs</i> was not passed or the length of the matched string is 0, this function returns 1. /","params":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"ereg_replace","fqn":"ereg_replace","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"regex","location":{"file":"regex/ereg.php","range":{"start":2177,"end":2189}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"replacement","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Replace regular expression A POSIX extended regular expression. </p> If <i>pattern</i> contains parenthesized substrings, <i>replacement</i> may contain substrings of the form \\digit, which will be replaced by the text matching the digit'th parenthesized substring; \\0 will produce the entire contents of string. Up to nine substrings may be used. Parentheses may be nested, in which case they are counted by the opening parenthesis. </p> The input string. </p> <i>string</i>, then it will be returned unchanged. /","params":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"replacement","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"eregi","fqn":"eregi","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"regex","location":{"file":"regex/ereg.php","range":{"start":3399,"end":3404}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"regs","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Case insensitive regular expression match Case insensitive regular expression. </p> The input string. </p> If matches are found for parenthesized substrings of <i>pattern</i> and the function is called with the third argument <i>regs</i>, the matches will be stored in the elements of the array <i>regs</i>. </p> <p> $regs[1] will contain the substring which starts at the first left parenthesis; $regs[2] will contain the substring starting at the second, and so on. $regs[0] will contain a copy of the complete string matched. </p> <i>pattern</i> was found in <i>string</i>, or <b>FALSE</b> if no matches were found or an error occurred. </p> <p> If the optional parameter <i>regs</i> was not passed or the length of the matched string is 0, this function returns 1. /","params":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"eregi_replace","fqn":"eregi_replace","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"regex","location":{"file":"regex/ereg.php","range":{"start":4376,"end":4389}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"replacement","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Replace regular expression case insensitive A POSIX extended regular expression. </p> If <i>pattern</i> contains parenthesized substrings, <i>replacement</i> may contain substrings of the form \\digit, which will be replaced by the text matching the digit'th parenthesized substring; \\0 will produce the entire contents of string. Up to nine substrings may be used. Parentheses may be nested, in which case they are counted by the opening parenthesis. </p> The input string. </p> <i>string</i>, then it will be returned unchanged. /","params":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"replacement","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"error_clear_last","fqn":"error_clear_last","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/basic.php","range":{"start":3494,"end":3510}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"Clear the most recent error /","params":[],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"error_get_last","fqn":"error_get_last","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":653,"end":667}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"?array","phpdoc_return_type":"array|null"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the last occurred error \"message\", \"file\" and \"line\". Returns null if there hasn't been an error yet. /","params":[],"return_type":"array|null","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"error_log","fqn":"error_log","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_3.php","range":{"start":31448,"end":31457}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"message","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"message_type","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"destination","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"additional_headers","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Send an error message to the defined error handling routines The error message that should be logged. </p> Says where the error should go. The possible message types are as follows: </p> <p> <table> error_log log types <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>0</td> <td> message is sent to PHP's system logger, using the Operating System's system logging mechanism or a file, depending on what the error_log configuration directive is set to. This is the default option. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>1</td> <td> message is sent by email to the address in the destination parameter. This is the only message type where the fourth parameter, extra_headers is used. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>2</td> <td> No longer an option. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>3</td> <td> message is appended to the file destination. A newline is not automatically added to the end of the message string. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>4</td> <td> message is sent directly to the SAPI logging handler. </td> </tr> </table> </p> The destination. Its meaning depends on the message_type parameter as described above. </p> The extra headers. It's used when the message_type parameter is set to 1. This message type uses the same internal function as mail does. </p> /","params":[{"name":"message","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"message_type","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"destination","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"additional_headers","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"error_reporting","fqn":"error_reporting","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":8521,"end":8536}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"error_level","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Sets which PHP errors are reported The new error_reporting level. It takes on either a bitmask, or named constants. Using named constants is strongly encouraged to ensure compatibility for future versions. As error levels are added, the range of integers increases, so older integer-based error levels will not always behave as expected. </p> <p> The available error level constants and the actual meanings of these error levels are described in the predefined constants. <table> error_reporting level constants and bit values <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>value</td> <td>constant</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>1</td> <td> E_ERROR </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>2</td> <td> E_WARNING </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>4</td> <td> E_PARSE </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>8</td> <td> E_NOTICE </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>16</td> <td> E_CORE_ERROR </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>32</td> <td> E_CORE_WARNING </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>64</td> <td> E_COMPILE_ERROR </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>128</td> <td> E_COMPILE_WARNING </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>256</td> <td> E_USER_ERROR </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>512</td> <td> E_USER_WARNING </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>1024</td> <td> E_USER_NOTICE </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>32767</td> <td> E_ALL </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>2048</td> <td> E_STRICT </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>4096</td> <td> E_RECOVERABLE_ERROR </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>8192</td> <td> E_DEPRECATED </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>16384</td> <td> E_USER_DEPRECATED </td> </tr> </table> </p> level or the current level if no <i>level</i> parameter is given. /","params":[{"name":"error_level","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"escapeshellarg","fqn":"escapeshellarg","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_2.php","range":{"start":27753,"end":27767}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"arg","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Escape a string to be used as a shell argument The argument that will be escaped. </p> /","params":[{"name":"arg","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"escapeshellcmd","fqn":"escapeshellcmd","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_2.php","range":{"start":27461,"end":27475}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"command","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Escape shell metacharacters The command that will be escaped. </p> /","params":[{"name":"command","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_add","fqn":"event_add","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":9186,"end":9195}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Add an event to the set of monitored events</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Schedules the execution of the non-pending event (makes it pending in it's configured base) when the event specified in {@link event_set}() occurs or in at least the time specified by the timeout argument. If timeout was not specified, not timeout is set. The event must be already initialized by {@link event_set}() and {@link event_base_set}() functions. If the event already has a timeout set, it is replaced by the new one.</p> <p>If you call {@link event_add}() on an event that is already pending, it will leave it pending, and reschedule it with the provided timeout.</p> Valid event resource. </p> Optional timeout (in microseconds). </p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_base_free","fqn":"event_base_free","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":3692,"end":3707}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Destroy event base</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Destroys the specified event_base and frees all the resources associated. Note that it's not possible to destroy an event base with events attached to it.</p> /","params":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event base resource."}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_base_loop","fqn":"event_base_loop","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":5164,"end":5179}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Handle events</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Starts event loop for the specified event base.</p> <p>By default, the {@link event_base_loop}() function runs an event_base until there are no more events registered in it. To run the loop, it repeatedly checks whether any of the registered events has triggered (for example, if a read event's file descriptor is ready to read, or if a timeout event's timeout is ready to expire). Once this happens, it marks all triggered events as \"active\", and starts to run them. </p> <p>You can change the behavior of event_base_loop() by setting one or more flags in its flags argument. If EVLOOP_ONCE is set, then the loop will wait until some events become active, then run active events until there are no more to run, then return. If EVLOOP_NONBLOCK is set, then the loop will not wait for events to trigger: it will only check whether any events are ready to trigger immediately, and run their callbacks if so. </p> Returns 0 if it exited normally, -1 if it exited because of some unhandled error in the backend and 1 if no events were registered. </p> /","params":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event base resource."},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] Optional parameter, which can take any combination of EVLOOP_ONCE and EVLOOP_NONBLOCK."}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_base_loopbreak","fqn":"event_base_loopbreak","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":5763,"end":5783}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Tells the event_base to exit its loop immediately.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>It differs from {@link event_base_loopexit}() in that if the event_base is currently running callbacks for any active events, it will exit immediately after finishing the one it's currently processing. The behaviour is similar to break statement.</p> /","params":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event base resource."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_base_loopexit","fqn":"event_base_loopexit","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":6664,"end":6683}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Tells an event_base to stop looping after a given time has elapsed</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>If the event_base is currently running callbacks for any active events, it will continue running them, and not exit until they have all been run.</p> <p>If event loop isn't running {@link event_base_loopexit}() schedules the next instance of the event loop to stop right after the next round of callbacks are run (as if it had been invoked with EVLOOP_ONCE).</p> Valid event base resource. </p> Optional timeout parameter (in microseconds). If lower than 1, the event_base stops looping without a delay. </p> /","params":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_base_new","fqn":"event_base_new","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":3295,"end":3309}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Create and initialize new event base</p> <p>Returns new event base, which can be used later in {@link event_base_set}(), {@link event_base_loop}() and other functions.</p> /","params":[],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_base_priority_init","fqn":"event_base_priority_init","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":7697,"end":7721}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"npriorities","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Set the number of different event priority levels</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.2)</p> <p>By default all events are scheduled with the same priority (npriorities/2). Using {@link event_base_priority_init}() you can change the number of event priority levels and then set a desired priority for each event.</p> /","params":[{"name":"event_base","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event base resource."},{"name":"npriorities","declared_type":"int","description":"The number of event priority levels."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_base_set","fqn":"event_base_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":7076,"end":7090}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"base","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Associate event base with an event</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Associates the event_base with the event.</p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event resource."},{"name":"base","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event base resource."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_base_set","fqn":"event_buffer_base_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":14074,"end":14095}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"event_base","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Associate buffered event with an event base</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Assign the specified bevent to the event_base.</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"event_base","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event base resource."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_disable","fqn":"event_buffer_disable","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":17112,"end":17132}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"events","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Disable a buffered event</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Disables the specified buffered event.</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"events","declared_type":"int","description":"Any combination of EV_READ and EV_WRITE."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_enable","fqn":"event_buffer_enable","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":16696,"end":16715}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"events","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Enables the specified buffered event.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"events","declared_type":"int","description":"Any combination of EV_READ and EV_WRITE."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_fd_set","fqn":"event_buffer_fd_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":19768,"end":19787}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"fd","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Changes the file descriptor on which the buffered event operates.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"fd","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid PHP stream, must be castable to file descriptor."}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_free","fqn":"event_buffer_free","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":13646,"end":13663}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Destroys the specified buffered event and frees all the resources associated.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_new","fqn":"event_buffer_new","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":13308,"end":13324}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"readcb","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"writecb","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"errorcb","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"arg","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Create new buffered event</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Libevent provides an abstraction layer on top of the regular event API. Using buffered event you don't need to deal with the I/O manually, instead it provides input and output buffers that get filled and drained automatically.</p> <p>Every bufferevent has two data-related callbacks: a read callback and a write callback. By default, the read callback is called whenever any data is read from the underlying transport, and the write callback is called whenever enough data from the output buffer is emptied to the underlying transport. You can override the behavior of these functions by adjusting the read and write \"watermarks\" of the bufferevent (see {@link event_buffer_watermark_set}()).</p> <p>A bufferevent also has an \"error\" or \"event\" callback that gets invoked to tell the application about non-data-oriented events, like when a connection is closed or an error occurs.</p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid PHP stream resource. Must be castable to file descriptor."},{"name":"readcb","declared_type":"callable|null","description":"Callback to invoke where there is data to read, or NULL if no callback is desired."},{"name":"writecb","declared_type":"callable|null","description":"Callback to invoke where the descriptor is ready for writing, or NULL if no callback is desired."},{"name":"errorcb","declared_type":"callable","description":"Callback to invoke where there is an error on the descriptor, cannot be NULL."},{"name":"arg","declared_type":"mixed","description":"An argument that will be passed to each of the callbacks (optional)."}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_priority_set","fqn":"event_buffer_priority_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":15361,"end":15386}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"priority","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Assign a priority to a buffered event. Use it after initializing event, but before adding an event to the event_base.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>When multiple events trigger at the same time, Libevent does not define any order with respect to when their callbacks will be executed. You can define some events as more important than others by using priorities.</p> <p>When multiple events of multiple priorities become active, the low-priority events are not run. Instead, Libevent runs the high priority events, then checks for events again. Only when no high-priority events are active are the low-priority events run.</p> <p>When you do not set the priority for an event, the default is the number of queues in the event base, divided by 2.</p> Valid buffered event resource. </p> Priority level. Cannot be less than 0 and cannot exceed maximum priority level of the event base (see {@link event_base_priority_init}()). </p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"priority","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_read","fqn":"event_buffer_read","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":16319,"end":16336}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data_size","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Reads data from the input buffer of the buffered event.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"data_size","declared_type":"int","description":"Data size in bytes."}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_set_callback","fqn":"event_buffer_set_callback","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":20602,"end":20627}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"readcb","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"writecb","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"errorcb","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"arg","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Set or reset callbacks for a buffered event</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.4)</p> <p>Sets or changes existing callbacks for the buffered event.</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"readcb","declared_type":"callable|null","description":"Callback to invoke where there is data to read, or NULL if no callback is desired."},{"name":"writecb","declared_type":"callable|null","description":"Callback to invoke where the descriptor is ready for writing, or NULL if no callback is desired."},{"name":"errorcb","declared_type":"callable","description":"Callback to invoke where there is an error on the descriptor, cannot be NULL."},{"name":"arg","declared_type":"mixed","description":"An argument that will be passed to each of the callbacks (optional)."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_timeout_set","fqn":"event_buffer_timeout_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":17529,"end":17553}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"read_timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"write_timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Sets the read and write timeouts for the specified buffered event.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"read_timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"Read timeout (in seconds)."},{"name":"write_timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"Write timeout (in seconds)."}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_watermark_set","fqn":"event_buffer_watermark_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":19364,"end":19390}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"events","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"lowmark","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"highmark","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Set the watermarks for read and write events.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Every bufferevent has four watermarks:</p> <p><b>Read low-water mark</b><br/> Whenever a read occurs that leaves the bufferevent's input buffer at this level or higher, the bufferevent's read callback is invoked. Defaults to 0, so that every read results in the read callback being invoked.</p> <p><b>Read high-water mark</b><br/> If the bufferevent's input buffer ever gets to this level, the bufferevent stops reading until enough data is drained from the input buffer to take us below it again. Defaults to unlimited, so that we never stop reading because of the size of the input buffer.</p> <p><b>Write low-water mark</b><br/> Whenever a write occurs that takes us to this level or below, we invoke the write callback. Defaults to 0, so that a write callback is not invoked unless the output buffer is emptied.</p> <p><b>Write high-water mark</b><br/> Not used by a bufferevent directly, this watermark can have special meaning when a bufferevent is used as the underlying transport of another bufferevent.</p> <p>Libevent does not invoke read callback unless there is at least lowmark bytes in the input buffer; if the read buffer is beyond the highmark, reading is stopped. On output, the write callback is invoked whenever the buffered data falls below the lowmark.</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"events","declared_type":"int","description":"Any combination of EV_READ and EV_WRITE."},{"name":"lowmark","declared_type":"int","description":"Low watermark."},{"name":"highmark","declared_type":"int","description":"High watermark."}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_buffer_write","fqn":"event_buffer_write","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":15972,"end":15990}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data_size","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Writes data to the specified buffered event.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>The data is appended to the output buffer and written to the descriptor when it becomes available for writing.</p> /","params":[{"name":"bevent","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid buffered event resource."},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"The data to be written."},{"name":"data_size","declared_type":"int","description":"Optional size parameter. {@link event_buffer_write}() writes all the data by default"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_del","fqn":"event_del","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":11566,"end":11575}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Remove an event from the set of monitored events.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>Calling {@link event_del}() on an initialized event makes it non-pending and non-active. If the event was not pending or active, there is no effect.</p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event resource."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_free","fqn":"event_free","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":8191,"end":8201}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Free event resource.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event resource."}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_new","fqn":"event_new","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":7983,"end":7992}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Creates and returns a new event resource.</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> /","params":[],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_set","fqn":"event_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":11078,"end":11087}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"fd","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource|int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"events","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"callback","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"arg","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Prepares the event to be used in {@link event_add}().</p> <p>(PECL libevent >= 0.0.1)</p> <p>The event is prepared to call the function specified by the callback on the events specified in parameter events, which is a set of the following flags: EV_TIMEOUT, EV_SIGNAL, EV_READ, EV_WRITE and EV_PERSIST.</p> <p>EV_SIGNAL support was added in version 0.0.4</p> <p>After initializing the event, use {@link event_base_set}() to associate the event with its event base.</p> <p>In case of matching event, these three arguments are passed to the callback function: <table> <tr> <td><b>$fd</b></td> <td>Signal number or resource indicating the stream.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>$events</b></td> <td>A flag indicating the event. Consists of the following flags: EV_TIMEOUT, EV_SIGNAL, EV_READ, EV_WRITE and EV_PERSIST.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>$arg</b></td> <td>Optional parameter, previously passed to {@link event_set}() as arg.</td> </tr> </table> </p> Valid event resource. </p> Valid PHP stream resource. The stream must be castable to file descriptor, so you most likely won't be able to use any of filtered streams. </p> A set of flags indicating the desired event, can be EV_READ and/or EV_WRITE. The additional flag EV_PERSIST makes the event to persist until {@link event_del}() is called, otherwise the callback is invoked only once. </p> Callback function to be called when the matching event occurs. </p> Optional callback parameter. </p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"fd","declared_type":"resource|int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"events","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","description":"<p>"},{"name":"arg","declared_type":"mixed","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_timer_add","fqn":"event_timer_add","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":22545,"end":22560}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Alias of {@link event_add}().</p> Valid event resource. </p> Optional timeout (in microseconds). </p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_timer_del","fqn":"event_timer_del","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":22758,"end":22773}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Alias of {@link event_del}().</p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"Valid event resource."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_timer_new","fqn":"event_timer_new","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":20833,"end":20848}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Alias of {@link event_new}().</p> /","params":[],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_timer_pending","fqn":"event_timer_pending","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":22228,"end":22247}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Checks if a specific event is pending or scheduled.</p> Valid event resource. </p> Optional timeout (in microseconds). </p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"event_timer_set","fqn":"event_timer_set","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"libevent","location":{"file":"libevent/libevent.php","range":{"start":21872,"end":21887}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"event","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"callback","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"arg","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Prepares the timer event to be used in {@link event_add}().</p> <p>The event is prepared to call the function specified by the callback on the timeout event (EV_TIMEOUT).</p> <p>After initializing the event, use {@link event_base_set}() to associate the event with its event base.</p> <p>In case of matching event, these three arguments are passed to the callback function: <table> <tr> <td><b>$fd</b></td> <td>null</td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>$events</b></td> <td>A flag indicating the event. EV_TIMEOUT.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>$arg</b></td> <td>Optional parameter, previously passed to {@link event_timer_set}() as arg.</td> </tr> </table> </p> Valid event resource. </p> Callback function to be called when the matching event occurs. </p> Optional callback parameter. </p> /","params":[{"name":"event","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","description":"<p>"},{"name":"arg","declared_type":"mixed","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"excimer_set_timeout","fqn":"excimer_set_timeout","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"excimer","location":{"file":"excimer/globals.php","range":{"start":715,"end":734}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"callback","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"interval","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"float","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"ExcimerTimer|null"},"documentation":{"description":"Abbreviated interface for starting a wall-clock timer. Equivalent to: $timer = new ExcimerTimer; $timer->setCallback($callback); $timer->setInterval($interval); $timer->start(); return $timer; Note that you must keep a copy of the return value. If it goes out of scope, the object will be destroyed and the timer will stop. If the callback is not callable, a warning is raised and null is returned. /","params":[{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","description":null},{"name":"interval","declared_type":"float","description":null}],"return_type":"ExcimerTimer|null","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"exec","fqn":"exec","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_2.php","range":{"start":26606,"end":26610}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"command","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"output","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"result_code","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Execute an external program The command that will be executed. </p> If the output argument is present, then the specified array will be filled with every line of output from the command. Trailing whitespace, such as \\n, is not included in this array. Note that if the array already contains some elements, exec will append to the end of the array. If you do not want the function to append elements, call unset on the array before passing it to exec. </p> If the result_code argument is present along with the output argument, then the return status of the executed command will be written to this variable. </p> command and have all the data from the command passed directly back without any interference, use the passthru function. </p> <p> To get the output of the executed command, be sure to set and use the output parameter. ValueError if command is empty or contains null bytes. /","params":[{"name":"command","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"exif_imagetype","fqn":"exif_imagetype","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"exif","location":{"file":"exif/exif.php","range":{"start":4973,"end":4987}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Determine the type of an image returned otherwise the return value is <b>FALSE</b>. The return value is the same value that <b>getimagesize</b> returns in index 2 but <b>exif_imagetype</b> is much faster. </p> <p> <b>exif_imagetype</b> will emit an <b>E_NOTICE</b> and return <b>FALSE</b> if it is unable to read enough bytes from the file to determine the image type. /","params":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"The image being checked."}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"exif_read_data","fqn":"exif_read_data","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"exif","location":{"file":"exif/exif.php","range":{"start":2581,"end":2595}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"file","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"required_sections","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"as_arrays","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"read_thumbnail","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Reads the EXIF headers from JPEG or TIFF The location of the image file. This cannot be an URL. Since 7.2.0 this can either be a path to the file (stream wrappers are also supported as usual) or a stream resource. </p> Is a comma separated list of sections that need to be present in file to produce a result array. If none of the requested sections could be found the return value is <b>FALSE</b>. <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>FILE</td> <td>FileName, FileSize, FileDateTime, SectionsFound</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>COMPUTED</td> <td> html, Width, Height, IsColor, and more if available. Height and Width are computed the same way <b>getimagesize</b> does so their values must not be part of any header returned. Also, html is a height/width text string to be used inside normal HTML. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ANY_TAG</td> <td>Any information that has a Tag e.g. IFD0, EXIF, ...</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IFD0</td> <td> All tagged data of IFD0. In normal imagefiles this contains image size and so forth. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>THUMBNAIL</td> <td> A file is supposed to contain a thumbnail if it has a second IFD. All tagged information about the embedded thumbnail is stored in this section. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>COMMENT</td> <td>Comment headers of JPEG images.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>EXIF</td> <td> The EXIF section is a sub section of IFD0. It contains more detailed information about an image. Most of these entries are digital camera related. </td> </tr> </p> Specifies whether or not each section becomes an array. The <i>sections</i> COMPUTED, THUMBNAIL, and COMMENT always become arrays as they may contain values whose names conflict with other sections. </p> When set to <b>TRUE</b> the thumbnail itself is read. Otherwise, only the tagged data is read. </p> the header names and the array values are the values associated with those headers. If no data can be returned, <b>exif_read_data</b> will return <b>FALSE</b>. /","params":[{"name":"file","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"required_sections","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"as_arrays","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"read_thumbnail","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"exif_tagname","fqn":"exif_tagname","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"exif","location":{"file":"exif/exif.php","range":{"start":3421,"end":3433}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"index","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the header name for an index The Tag ID for which a Tag Name will be looked up. </p> not a defined EXIF tag id. /","params":[{"name":"index","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"exif_thumbnail","fqn":"exif_thumbnail","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"exif","location":{"file":"exif/exif.php","range":{"start":4256,"end":4270}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"file","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string|resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"width","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":fals