urns false. /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"The file pointer must be valid, and must point to a file successfully opened by fopen() or fsockopen() (and not yet closed by fclose())."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"fflush","fqn":"fflush","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_5.php","range":{"start":25530,"end":25536}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Flushes the output to a file /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"The file pointer must be valid, and must point to a file successfully opened by fopen() or fsockopen() (and not yet closed by fclose())."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"fgetc","fqn":"fgetc","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_5.php","range":{"start":13750,"end":13755}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets character from file pointer to by handle. Returns false on EOF. /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"The file pointer must be valid, and must point to a file successfully opened by fopen() or fsockopen() (and not yet closed by fclose())."}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"fgetcsv","fqn":"fgetcsv","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":22674,"end":22681}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"enclosure","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"escape","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array|false|null"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets line from file pointer and parse for CSV fields A valid file pointer to a file successfully opened by fopen, popen, or fsockopen. </p> Must be greater than the longest line (in characters) to be found in the CSV file (allowing for trailing line-end characters). It became optional in PHP 5. Omitting this parameter (or setting it to 0 in PHP 5.0.4 and later) the maximum line length is not limited, which is slightly slower. </p> Set the field delimiter (one character only). </p> Set the field enclosure character (one character only). </p> Set the escape character (one character only). Defaults as a backslash. </p> <p> A blank line in a CSV file will be returned as an array comprising a single null field, and will not be treated as an error. </p> <p> fgetcsv returns null if an invalid handle is supplied or false on other errors, including end of file. </p> ValueError if escape is not one byte long or the empty string. /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"enclosure","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"escape","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array|false|null","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"fgets","fqn":"fgets","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_5.php","range":{"start":14751,"end":14756}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets line from file pointer Reading ends when length - 1 bytes have been read, on a newline (which is included in the return value), or on EOF (whichever comes first). If no length is specified, it will keep reading from the stream until it reaches the end of the line. </p> <p> Until PHP 4.3.0, omitting it would assume 1024 as the line length. If the majority of the lines in the file are all larger than 8KB, it is more resource efficient for your script to specify the maximum line length. </p> the file pointed to by handle. </p> <p> If an error occurs, returns false. /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"The file pointer must be valid, and must point to a file successfully opened by fopen() or fsockopen() (and not yet closed by fclose())."},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"fgetss","fqn":"fgetss","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_5.php","range":{"start":15570,"end":15576}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"handle","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"null|int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"allowable_tags","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"false|string","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets line from file pointer and strip HTML tags Length of the data to be retrieved. </p> You can use the optional third parameter to specify tags which should not be stripped. </p> the file pointed to by handle, with all HTML and PHP code stripped. </p> <p> If an error occurs, returns false. /","params":[{"name":"handle","declared_type":"resource","description":"The file pointer must be valid, and must point to a file successfully opened by fopen() or fsockopen() (and not yet closed by fclose())."},{"name":"length","declared_type":"null|int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"allowable_tags","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"file","fqn":"file","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_5.php","range":{"start":31780,"end":31784}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Reads entire file into an array Path to the file. </p> The optional parameter flags can be one, or more, of the following constants: <ul> <li><tt>FILE_USE_INCLUDE_PATH</tt> - Search for the file in the include_path.</li> <li><tt>FILE_IGNORE_NEW_LINES</tt> - Omit newline at the end of each array element</li> <li><tt>FILE_SKIP_EMPTY_LINES</tt> - Skip empty lines</li> </ul> </p> A context resource created with the stream_context_create function. </p> line in the file, with the newline still attached. Upon failure, file returns false. <p> Each line in the resulting array will include the line ending, unless FILE_IGNORE_NEW_LINES is used, so you still need to use rtrim if you do not want the line ending present. </p> such as FILE_APPEND. Emits an E_WARNING level error if the file does not exist. /","params":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"context","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"file_exists","fqn":"file_exists","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_7.php","range":{"start":19242,"end":19253}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Checks whether a file or directory exists Path to the file or directory. </p> <p> On windows, use //computername/share/filename or \\\\computername\\share\\filename to check files on network shares. </p> filename exists; false otherwise. </p> <p> This function will return false for symlinks pointing to non-existing files. </p> <p> This function returns false for files inaccessible due to safe mode restrictions. However these files still can be included if they are located in safe_mode_include_dir. </p> <p> The check is done using the real UID/GID instead of the effective one. /","params":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"file_get_contents","fqn":"file_get_contents","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_5.php","range":{"start":32733,"end":32750}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"use_include_path","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"offset","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Reads entire file into a string Name of the file to read. </p> Note: As of PHP 5 the FILE_USE_INCLUDE_PATH constant can be used to trigger include path search. </p> A valid context resource created with stream_context_create. If you don't need to use a custom context, you can skip this parameter by null. </p> The offset where the reading starts. </p> Maximum length of data read. The default is to read until end of file is reached. </p> /","params":[{"name