ders","fqn":"get_headers","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":36954,"end":36965}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"url","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"associative","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetches all the headers sent by the server in response to an HTTP request The target URL. </p> If the optional format parameter is set to true, get_headers parses the response and sets the array's keys. </p> failure. /","params":[{"name":"url","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"associative","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"context","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_html_translation_table","fqn":"get_html_translation_table","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":24103,"end":24129}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"table","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the translation table used by <function>htmlspecialchars</function> and <function>htmlentities</function> There are two new constants (HTML_ENTITIES, HTML_SPECIALCHARS) that allow you to specify the table you want. </p> Like the htmlspecialchars and htmlentities functions you can optionally specify the quote_style you are working with. See the description of these modes in htmlspecialchars. </p> Encoding to use. If omitted, the default value for this argument is ISO-8859-1 in versions of PHP prior to 5.4.0, and UTF-8 from PHP 5.4.0 onwards. </p> <p> The following character sets are supported: </p><table class=\"doctable table\"> <caption><strong>Supported charsets</strong></caption> <thead> <tr> <th>Charset</th> <th>Aliases</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody class=\"tbody\"> <tr> <td>ISO-8859-1</td> <td>ISO8859-1</td> <td> Western European, Latin-1. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>ISO-8859-5</td> <td>ISO8859-5</td> <td> Little used cyrillic charset (Latin/Cyrillic). </td> </tr> <tr> <td>ISO-8859-15</td> <td>ISO8859-15</td> <td> Western European, Latin-9. Adds the Euro sign, French and Finnish letters missing in Latin-1 (ISO-8859-1). </td> </tr> <tr> <td>UTF-8</td> <td class=\"empty\">&nbsp;</td> <td> ASCII compatible multi-byte 8-bit Unicode. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>cp866</td> <td>ibm866, 866</td> <td> DOS-specific Cyrillic charset. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>cp1251</td> <td>Windows-1251, win-1251, 1251</td> <td> Windows-specific Cyrillic charset. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>cp1252</td> <td>Windows-1252, 1252</td> <td> Windows specific charset for Western European. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>KOI8-R</td> <td>koi8-ru, koi8r</td> <td> Russian. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>BIG5</td> <td>950</td> <td> Traditional Chinese, mainly used in Taiwan. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>GB2312</td> <td>936</td> <td> Simplified Chinese, national standard character set. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>BIG5-HKSCS</td> <td class=\"empty\">&nbsp;</td> <td> Big5 with Hong Kong extensions, Traditional Chinese. </td> </tr> <tr> <td>Shift_JIS</td> <td>SJIS, SJIS-win, cp932, 932</td> <td> Japanese </td> </tr> <tr> <td>EUC-JP</td> <td>EUCJP, eucJP-win</td> <td> Japanese </td> </tr> <tr> <td>MacRoman</td> <td class=\"empty\">&nbsp;</td> <td> Charset that was used by Mac OS. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><em>''</em></td> <td class=\"empty\">&nbsp;</td> <td> An empty string activates detection from script encoding (Zend multibyte), {@link https://php.net/manual/en/ini.core.php#ini.default-charset default_charset} and current locale {@link https://php.net/manual/en/function.nl-langinfo.php nl_langinfo()} and {@link https://php.net/manual/en/function.setlocale.php setlocale()}), in this order. Not recommended. </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <blockquote><p><strong>Note</strong>: Any other character sets are not recognized. The default encoding will be used instead and a warning will be emitted. </p></blockquote> /","params":[{"name":"table","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_include_path","fqn":"get_include_path","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":18674,"end":18690}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets the current include_path configuration option /","params":[],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_included_files","fqn":"get_included_files","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":16007,"end":16025}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"string[]"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns an array with the names of included or required files <p> The script originally called is considered an \"included file,\" so it will be listed together with the files referenced by <b>include</b> and family. </p> <p> Files that are included or required multiple times only show up once in the returned array. </p> /","params":[],"return_type":"string[]","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_loaded_extensions","fqn":"get_loaded_extensions","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":28028,"end":28049}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"zend_extensions","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"string[]"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns an array with the names of all modules compiled and loaded Only return Zend extensions, if not then regular extensions, like mysqli are listed. Defaults to false (return regular extensions). </p> /","params":[{"name":"zend_extensions","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string[]","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_magic_quotes_gpc","fqn":"get_magic_quotes_gpc","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_3.php","range":{"start":27915,"end":27935}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets the current configuration setting of magic quotes gpc /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_magic_quotes_runtime","fqn":"get_magic_quotes_runtime","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_3.php","range":{"start":28200,"end":28224}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets the current active configuration setting of magic_quotes_runtime /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_mangled_object_vars","fqn":"get_mangled_object_vars","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_9.php","range":{"start":45488,"end":45511}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"object","declared_type":"object","phpdoc_type":"object","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"It returns the same result as (array) $object, with the exception that it ignores overloaded array casts, such as used by ArrayObject. /","params":[{"name":"object","declared_type":"object","description":null}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_meta_tags","fqn":"get_meta_tags","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":25975,"end":25988}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"use_include_path","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Extracts all meta tag content attributes from a file and returns an array The path to the HTML file, as a string. This can be a local file or an URL. </p> <p> What get_meta_tags parses </p> <pre> <meta name=\"author\" content=\"name\"> <meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"php documentation\"> <meta name=\"DESCRIPTION\" content=\"a php manual\"> <meta name=\"geo.position\" content=\"49.33;-86.59\"> </head> <!-- parsing stops here --> </pre> <p> (pay attention to line endings - PHP uses a native function to parse the input, so a Mac file won't work on Unix). </p> Setting use_include_path to true will result in PHP trying to open the file along the standard include path as per the include_path directive. This is used for local files, not URLs. </p> <p> The value of the name property becomes the key, the value of the content property becomes the value of the returned array, so you can easily use standard array functions to traverse it or access single values. Special characters in the value of the name property are substituted with '_', the rest is converted to lower case. If two meta tags have the same name, only the last one is returned. </p> /","params":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"use_include_path","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_object_vars","fqn":"get_object_vars","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":18554,"end":18569}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"object","declared_type":"object","phpdoc_type":"object","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets the properties of the given object An object instance. </p> for the specified <i>object</i> in scope. If a property have not been assigned a value, it will be returned with a null value. /","params":[{"name":"object","declared_type":"object","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_parent_class","fqn":"get_parent_class","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":11868,"end":11884}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"object_or_class","declared_type":"object|string","phpdoc_type":"object|string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Retrieves the parent class name for object or class The tested object or class name </p> <i>object</i> is an instance or the name. </p> <p> If the object does not have a parent false will be returned. </p> <p> If called without parameter outside object, this function returns false.</p> /","params":[{"name":"object_or_class","declared_type":"object|string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_required_files","fqn":"get_required_files","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":16195,"end":16213}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"string[]"},"documentation":{"description":"Alias of <b>get_included_files</b> /","params":[],"return_type":"string[]","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_resource_id","fqn":"get_resource_id","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_9.php","range":{"start":46347,"end":46362}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"resource","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"A more obvious and type-safe form of \"(int) $resource\" /","params":[{"name":"resource","declared_type":"resource","description":null}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_resource_type","fqn":"get_resource_type","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":27566,"end":27583}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"resource","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the resource type The evaluated resource handle. </p> will return a string representing its type. If the type is not identified by this function, the return value will be the string Unknown. /","params":[{"name":"resource","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_resources","fqn":"get_resources","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Core","location":{"file":"Core/Core.php","range":{"start":35987,"end":36000}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"type","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"resource[]"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns active resources If defined, this will cause get_resources() to only return resources of the given type. A list of resource types is available. If the string Unknown is provided as the type, then only resources that are of an unknown type will be returned. If omitted, all resources will be returned. </p> /","params":[{"name":"type","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional]<p>"}],"return_type":"resource[]","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getallheaders","fqn":"getallheaders","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":30642,"end":30655}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"false|array","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetches all HTTP headers from the current request. This function is an alias for apache_request_headers(). Please read the apache_request_headers() documentation for more information on how this function works. /","params":[],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getcwd","fqn":"getcwd","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_7.php","range":{"start":11450,"end":11456}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets the current working directory the current working directory on success, or false on failure. <br> <br> On some Unix variants, getcwd will return false if any one of the parent directories does not have the readable or search mode set, even if the current directory does. See chmod for more information on modes and permissions. </p> /","params":[],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getdate","fqn":"getdate","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"date","location":{"file":"date/date.php","range":{"start":27102,"end":27109}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Get date/time information the timestamp. Elements from the returned associative array are as follows: </p> <p> <table> Key elements of the returned associative array <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Key</td> <td>Description</td> <td>Example returned values</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"seconds\"</td> <td>Numeric representation of seconds</td> <td>0 to 59</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"minutes\"</td> <td>Numeric representation of minutes</td> <td>0 to 59</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"hours\"</td> <td>Numeric representation of hours</td> <td>0 to 23</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"mday\"</td> <td>Numeric representation of the day of the month</td> <td>1 to 31</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"wday\"</td> <td>Numeric representation of the day of the week</td> <td>0 (for Sunday) through 6 (for Saturday)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"mon\"</td> <td>Numeric representation of a month</td> <td>1 through 12</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"year\"</td> <td>A full numeric representation of a year, 4 digits</td> <td>Examples: 1999 or 2003</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"yday\"</td> <td>Numeric representation of the day of the year</td> <td>0 through 365</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"weekday\"</td> <td>A full textual representation of the day of the week</td> <td>Sunday through Saturday</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>\"month\"</td> <td>A full textual representation of a month, such as January or March</td> <td>January through December</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>0</td> <td> Seconds since the Unix Epoch, similar to the values returned by time and used by date. </td> <td> System Dependent, typically -2147483648 through 2147483647. </td> </tr> </table> /","params":[{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getdir","fqn":"getdir","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_7.php","range":{"start":12890,"end":12896}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"directory","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"Directory|false","phpdoc_return_type":"Directory|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Alias of dir() /","params":[{"name":"directory","declared_type":"string","description":null},{"name":"context","declared_type":"resource","description":null}],"return_type":"Directory|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getenv","fqn":"getenv","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_3.php","range":{"start":19991,"end":19997}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"varname","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"name","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"local_only","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets the value of an environment variable The variable name. </p> Set to true to only return local environment variables (set by the operating system or putenv). </p> varname or an associative array with all environment variables if no variable name is provided, or false on an error. /","params":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"local_only","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"gethostbyaddr","fqn":"gethostbyaddr","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":35642,"end":35655}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"ip","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the Internet host name corresponding to a given IP address The host IP address. </p> on failure. /","params":[{"name":"ip","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"gethostbyname","fqn":"gethostbyname","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":35995,"end":36008}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the IPv4 address corresponding to a given Internet host name The host name. </p> hostname on failure. /","params":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"gethostbynamel","fqn":"gethostbynamel","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":36360,"end":36374}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get a list of IPv4 addresses corresponding to a given Internet host name The host name. </p> hostname could not be resolved. /","params":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"gethostname","fqn":"gethostname","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":36612,"end":36623}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets the host name returned. /","params":[],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getimagesize","fqn":"getimagesize","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":30137,"end":30149}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"image_info","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the size of an image This parameter specifies the file you wish to retrieve information about. It can reference a local file or (configuration permitting) a remote file using one of the supported streams. </p> This optional parameter allows you to extract some extended information from the image file. Currently, this will return the different JPG APP markers as an associative array. Some programs use these APP markers to embed text information in images. A very common one is to embed IPTC information in the APP13 marker. You can use the iptcparse function to parse the binary APP13 marker into something readable. </p> <p> Index 0 and 1 contains respectively the width and the height of the image. </p> <p> Some formats may contain no image or may contain multiple images. In these cases, getimagesize might not be able to properly determine the image size. getimagesize will return zero for width and height in these cases. </p> <p> Index 2 is one of the IMAGETYPE_XXX constants indicating the type of the image. </p> <p> Index 3 is a text string with the correct height=\"yyy\" width=\"xxx\" string that can be used directly in an IMG tag. </p> <p> mime is the correspondant MIME type of the image. This information can be used to deliver images with correct the HTTP Content-type header: getimagesize and MIME types </p> <p> channels will be 3 for RGB pictures and 4 for CMYK pictures. </p> <p> bits is the number of bits for each color. </p> <p> For some image types, the presence of channels and bits values can be a bit confusing. As an example, GIF always uses 3 channels per pixel, but the number of bits per pixel cannot be calculated for an animated GIF with a global color table. </p> <p> On failure, false is returned. </p> error of level E_WARNING. On read error, getimagesize will generate an error of level E_NOTICE. As of PHP 8.0.0, a ValueError is thrown if filename is empty. /","params":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"thr