es a gzip compressed string The data to decode, encoded by <b>gzencode</b>. </p> The maximum length of data to decode. </p> /","params":[{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"max_length","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"gzdeflate","fqn":"gzdeflate","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"zlib","location":{"file":"zlib/zlib.php","range":{"start":10107,"end":10116}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Deflate a string The data to deflate. </p> The level of compression. Can be given as 0 for no compression up to 9 for maximum compression. If not given, the default compression level will be the default compression level of the zlib library. </p> One of <b>ZLIB_ENCODING_*</b> constants. </p> /","params":[{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"gzencode","fqn":"gzencode","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"zlib","location":{"file":"zlib/zlib.php","range":{"start":11859,"end":11867}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Create a gzip compressed string The data to encode. </p> The level of compression. Can be given as 0 for no compression up to 9 for maximum compression. If not given, the default compression level will be the default compression level of the zlib library. </p> The encoding mode. Can be <b>FORCE_GZIP</b> (the default) or <b>FORCE_DEFLATE</b>. </p> <p> Prior to PHP 5.4.0, using <b>FORCE_DEFLATE</b> results in a standard zlib deflated string (inclusive zlib headers) after a gzip file header but without the trailing crc32 checksum. </p> <p> In PHP 5.4.0 and later, <b>FORCE_DEFLATE</b> generates RFC 1950 compliant output, consisting of a zlib header, the deflated data, and an Adler checksum. </p> /","params":[{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"gzeof","fqn":"gzeof","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"zlib","location":{"file":"zlib/zlib.php","range":{"start":1869,"end":1874}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Test for EOF on a gz-file pointer The gz-file pointer. It must be valid, and must point to a file successfully opened by <b>gzopen<