eprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"html_entity_decode","fqn":"html_entity_decode","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":19251,"end":19269}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Convert HTML entities  to their corresponding characters The input string. </p> The optional second flags parameter lets you define what will be done with 'single' and \"double\" quotes and which document type to use. The default is ENT_QUOTES | ENT_SUBSTITUTE | ENT_HTML401 (it was ENT_COMPAT | ENT_HTML401 prior to PHP 8.1): <table> Available flags constants <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Constant Name</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_COMPAT</td> <td>Will convert double-quotes and leave single-quotes alone.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_QUOTES</td> <td>Will convert both double and single quotes.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_NOQUOTES</td> <td>Will leave both double and single quotes unconverted.</td> </tr> </table> </p> The ISO-8859-1 character set is used as default for the optional third charset. This defines the character set used in conversion. </p> /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"htmlentities","fqn":"htmlentities","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":17872,"end":17884}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"double_encode","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Convert all applicable characters to HTML entities The input string. </p> Like htmlspecialchars, the optional second flags parameter lets you define what will be done with 'single' and \"double\" quotes, invalid code unit sequences and the used document type. The default is ENT_QUOTES | ENT_SUBSTITUTE | ENT_HTML401 (it was ENT_COMPAT | ENT_HTML401 prior to PHP 8.1): <table> Available flags constants <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Constant Name</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_COMPAT</td> <td>Will convert double-quotes and leave single-quotes alone.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_QUOTES</td> <td>Will convert both double and single quotes.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_NOQUOTES</td> <td>Will leave both double and single quotes unconverted.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_SUBSTITUTE</td> <td>Replace invalid code unit sequences with a Unicode Replacement Character U+FFFD (UTF-8) or &amp;#FFFD; (otherwise) instead of returning an empty string.</td> </tr> </table> </p> Like htmlspecialchars, it takes an optional third argument charset which defines character set used in conversion. Presently, the ISO-8859-1 character set is used as the default. </p> When double_encode is turned off PHP will not encode existing html entities. The default is to convert everything. </p> /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"double_encode","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"htmlspecialchars","fqn":"htmlspecialchars","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":16000,"end":16016}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"double_encode","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Convert special characters to HTML entities The {@link https://php.net/manual/en/language.types.string.php string} being converted. </p> A bitmask of one or more of the following flags, which specify how to handle quotes, invalid code unit sequences and the used document type. The default is <em><b>ENT_QUOTES | ENT_SUBSTITUTE | ENT_HTML401</b></em> (it was <em><b>ENT_COMPAT | ENT_HTML401</b></em> prior to PHP 8.1). </p><table> <caption><b>Available <em>flags</em> constants</b></caption> <thead> <tr> <th>Constant Name</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><b>ENT_COMPAT</b></td> <td>Will convert double-quotes and leave single-quotes alone.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_QUOTES</b></td> <td>Will convert both double and single quotes.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_NOQUOTES</b></td> <td>Will leave both double and single quotes unconverted.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_IGNORE</b></td> <td> Silently discard invalid code unit sequences instead of returning an empty string. Using this flag is discouraged as it {@link https://unicode.org/reports/tr36/#Deletion_of_Noncharacters »&nbsp;may have security implications}. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_SUBSTITUTE</b></td> <td> Replace invalid code unit sequences with a Unicode Replacement Character U+FFFD (UTF-8) or &amp;#FFFD; (otherwise) instead of returning an empty string. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_DISALLOWED</b></td> <td> Replace invalid code points for the given document type with a Unicode Replacement Character U+FFFD (UTF-8) or &amp;#FFFD; (otherwise) instead of leaving them as is. This may be useful, for instance, to ensure the well-formedness of XML documents with embedded external content. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_HTML401</b></td> <td> Handle code as HTML 4.01. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_XML1</b></td> <td> Handle code as XML 1. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_XHTML</b></td> <td> Handle code as XHTML. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><b>ENT_HTML5</b></td> <td> Handle code as HTML 5. </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> Defines encoding used in conversion. If omitted, the default value for this argument is ISO-8859-1 in versions of PHP prior to 5.4.0, and UTF-8 from PHP 5.4.0 onwards. </p> <p> For the purposes of this function, the encodings <em>ISO-8859-1</em>, <em>ISO-8859-15</em>, <em>UTF-8</em>, <em>cp866</em>, <em>cp1251</em>, <em>cp1252</em>, and <em>KOI8-R</em> are effectively equivalent, provided the <em><b>string</b></em> itself is valid for the encoding, as the characters affected by  <b>htmlspecialchars()</b> occupy the same positions in all of these encodings. </p> When <em><b>double_encode</b></em> is turned off PHP will not encode existing html entities, the default is to convert everything. </p> /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"double_encode","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"htmlspecialchars_decode","fqn":"htmlspecialchars_decode","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":20377,"end":20400}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Convert special HTML entities back to characters The string to decode </p> A bitmask of one or more of the following flags, which specify how to handle quotes and which document type to use. The default is ENT_QUOTES | ENT_SUBSTITUTE | ENT_HTML401 (it was ENT_COMPAT | ENT_HTML401 prior to PHP 8.1): <table> flags constants <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Constant Name</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_COMPAT</td> <td>Will convert double-quotes and leave single-quotes alone</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_QUOTES</td> <td>Will convert both double and single quotes</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>ENT_NOQUOTES</td> <td>Will leave both double and single quotes unconverted</td> </tr> </table> </p> /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_t