se,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"to_encoding","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Convert string to requested character encoding The input charset. </p> The output charset. </p> <p> If you append the string //TRANSLIT to <i>out_charset</i> transliteration is activated. This means that when a character can't be represented in the target charset, it can be approximated through one or several similarly looking characters. If you append the string //IGNORE, characters that cannot be represented in the target charset are silently discarded. Otherwise, <i>str</i> is cut from the first illegal character and an <b>E_NOTICE</b> is generated. </p> The string to be converted. </p> /","params":[{"name":"from_encoding","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"to_encoding","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_get_encoding","fqn":"iconv_get_encoding","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":2125,"end":2143}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"type","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|string[]|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Retrieve internal configuration variables of iconv extension The value of the optional <i>type</i> can be: all input_encoding output_encoding internal_encoding </p> successful or <b>FALSE</b> on failure. <p> If <i>type</i> is omitted or set to \"all\", <b>iconv_get_encoding</b> returns an array that stores all these variables. </p> /","params":[{"name":"type","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|string[]|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_mime_decode","fqn":"iconv_mime_decode","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":11155,"end":11172}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Decodes a MIME header field The encoded header, as a string. </p> <i>mode</i> determines the behaviour in the event <b>iconv_mime_decode</b> encounters a malformed MIME header field. You can specify any combination of the following bitmasks. <table> Bitmasks acceptable to <b>iconv_mime_decode</b> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Value</td> <td>Constant</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>1</td> <td>ICONV_MIME_DECODE_STRICT</td> <td> If set, the given header is decoded in full conformance with the standards defined in RFC2047. This option is disabled by default because there are a lot of broken mail user agents that don't follow the specification and don't produce correct MIME headers. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>2</td> <td>ICONV_MIME_DECODE_CONTINUE_ON_ERROR</td> <td> If set, <b>iconv_mime_decode_headers</b> attempts to ignore any grammatical errors and continue to process a given header. </td> </tr> </table> </p> The optional <i>charset</i> parameter specifies the character set to represent the result by. If omitted, iconv.internal_encoding will be used. </p> or <b>FALSE</b> if an error occurs during the decoding. /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_mime_decode_headers","fqn":"iconv_mime_decode_headers","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":13230,"end":13255}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"headers","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Decodes multiple MIME header fields at once The encoded headers, as a string. </p> <i>mode</i> determines the behaviour in the event <b>iconv_mime_decode_headers</b> encounters a malformed MIME header field. You can specify any combination of the following bitmasks. <br> Bitmasks acceptable to <b>iconv_mime_decode_headers</b></p> <table> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Value</td> <td>Constant</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>1</td> <td>ICONV_MIME_DECODE_STRICT</td> <td> If set, the given header is decoded in full conformance with the standards defined in RFC2047. This option is disabled by default because there are a lot of broken mail user agents that don't follow the specification and don't produce correct MIME headers. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>2</td> <td>ICONV_MIME_DECODE_CONTINUE_ON_ERROR</td> <td> If set, <b>iconv_mime_decode_headers</b> attempts to ignore any grammatical errors and continue to process a given header. </td> </tr> </table> The optional <i>charset</i> parameter specifies the character set to represent the result by. If omitted, iconv.internal_encoding will be used. </p> MIME header fields specified by <i>encoded_headers</i> on success, or <b>FALSE</b> if an error occurs during the decoding. <p> Each key of the return value represents an individual field name and the corresponding element represents a field value. If more than one field of the same name are present, <b>iconv_mime_decode_headers</b> automatically incorporates them into a numerically indexed array in the order of occurrence. </p> /","params":[{"name":"headers","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_mime_encode","fqn":"iconv_mime_encode","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":9537,"end":9554}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"field_name","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field_value","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"options","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Composes a MIME header field The field name. </p> The field value. </p> You can control the behaviour of <b>iconv_mime_encode</b> by specifying an associative array that contains configuration items to the optional third parameter <i>preferences</i>. The items supported by <b>iconv_mime_encode</b> are listed below. Note that item names are treated case-sensitive. <table> Configuration items supported by <b>iconv_mime_encode</b> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Item</td> <td>Type</td> <td>Description</td> <td>Default value</td> <td>Example</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>scheme</td> <td>string</td> <td> Specifies the method to encode a field value by. The value of this item may be either \"B\" or \"Q\", where \"B\" stands for base64 encoding scheme and \"Q\" stands for quoted-printable encoding scheme. </td> <td>B</td> <td>B</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>input-charset</td> <td>string</td> <td> Specifies the character set in which the first parameter <i>field_name</i> and the second parameter <i>field_value</i> are presented. If not given, <b>iconv_mime_encode</b> assumes those parameters are presented to it in the iconv.internal_encoding ini setting. </td> <td> iconv.internal_encoding </td> <td>ISO-8859-1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>output-charset</td> <td>string</td> <td> Specifies the character set to use to compose the MIME header. </td> <td> iconv.internal_encoding </td> <td>UTF-8</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>line-length</td> <td>integer</td> <td> Specifies the maximum length of the header lines. The resulting header is \"folded\" to a set of multiple lines in case the resulting header field would be longer than the value of this parameter, according to RFC2822 - Internet Message Format. If not given, the length will be limited to 76 characters. </td> <td>76</td> <td>996</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>line-break-chars</td> <td>string</td> <td> Specifies the sequence of characters to append to each line as an end-of-line sign when \"folding\" is performed on a long header field. If not given, this defaults to \"\\r\\n\" (CR LF). Note that this parameter is always treated as an ASCII string regardless of the value of input-charset. </td> <td>\\r\\n</td> <td>\\n</td> </tr> </table> </p> or <b>FALSE</b> if an error occurs during the encoding. /","params":[{"name":"field_name","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field_value","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"options","declared_type":"array","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_set_encoding","fqn":"iconv_set_encoding","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":2605,"end":2623}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"type","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Set current setting for character encoding conversion The value of <i>type</i> can be any one of these: input_encoding output_encoding internal_encoding </p> The character set. </p> /","params":[{"name":"type","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_strlen","fqn":"iconv_strlen","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":3089,"end":3101}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the character count of string The string. </p> If <i>charset</i> parameter is omitted, <i>str</i> is assumed to be encoded in iconv.internal_encoding. </p> /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_strpos","fqn":"iconv_strpos","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":5922,"end":5934}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"haystack","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"needle","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"offset","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int<0,max>|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Finds position of first occurrence of a needle within a haystack The entire string. </p> The searched substring. </p> The optional <i>offset</i> parameter specifies the position from which the search should be performed. </p> If <i>charset</i> parameter is omitted, <i>string</i> are assumed to be encoded in iconv.internal_encoding. </p> <i>needle</i> in <i>haystack</i>. <p> If <i>needle</i> is not found, <b>iconv_strpos</b> will return <b>FALSE</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"haystack","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"needle","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"offset","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int<0,max>|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_strrpos","fqn":"iconv_strrpos","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":6663,"end":6676}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"haystack","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"needle","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Finds the last occurrence of a needle within a haystack The entire string. </p> The searched substring. </p> If <i>charset</i> parameter is omitted, <i>string</i> are assumed to be encoded in iconv.internal_encoding. </p> <i>needle</i> in <i>haystack</i>. <p> If <i>needle</i> is not found, <b>iconv_strrpos</b> will return <b>FALSE</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"haystack","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"needle","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"iconv_substr","fqn":"iconv_substr","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"iconv","location":{"file":"iconv/iconv.php","range":{"start":5010,"end":5022}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"offset","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Cut out part of a string The original string. </p> If <i>offset</i> is non-negative, <b>iconv_substr</b> cuts the portion out of <i>str</i> beginning at <i>offset</i>'th character, counting from zero. </p> <p> If <i>offset</i> is negative, <b>iconv_substr</b> cuts out the portion beginning at the position, <i>offset</i> characters away from the end of <i>str</i>. </p> If <i>length</i> is given and is positive, the return value will contain at most <i>length</i> characters of the portion that begins at <i>offset</i> (depending on the length of <i>string</i>). </p> <p> If negative <i>length</i> is passed, <b>iconv_substr</b> cuts the portion out of <i>str</i> from the <i>offset</i>'th character up to the character that is <i>length</i> characters away from the end of the string. In case <i>offset</i> is also negative, the start position is calculated beforehand according to the rule explained above. </p> If <i>charset</i> parameter is omitted, <i>string</i> are assumed to be encoded in iconv.internal_encoding. </p> <p> Note that <i>offset</i> and <i>length</i> parameters are always deemed to represent offsets that are calculated on the basis of the character set determined by <i>charset</i>, whilst the counterpart <b>substr</b> always takes these for byte offsets. </p> <i>offset</i> and <i>length</i> parameters. <p> If <i>str</i> is shorter than <i>offset</i> characters long, <b>FALSE</b> will be returned. </p> /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"offset","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"idate","fqn":"idate","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"date","location":{"file":"date/date.php","range":{"start":10561,"end":10566}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"format","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Format a local time/date as integer <table> The following characters are recognized in the format parameter string <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>format character</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>B</td> <td>Swatch Beat/Internet Time</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>d</td> <td>Day of the month</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>h</td> <td>Hour (12 hour format)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>H</td> <td>Hour (24 hour format)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>i</td> <td>Minutes</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>I (uppercase i)</td> <td>returns 1 if DST is activated, 0 otherwise</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>L (uppercase l)</td> <td>returns 1 for leap year, 0 otherwise</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>m</td> <td>Month number</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>s</td> <td>Seconds</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>t</td> <td>Days in current month</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>U</td> <td>Seconds since the Unix Epoch - January 1 1970 00:00:00 UTC - this is the same as time</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>w</td> <td>Day of the week (0 on Sunday)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>W</td> <td>ISO-8601 week number of year, weeks starting on Monday</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>y</td> <td>Year (1 or 2 digits - check note below)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Y</td> <td>Year (4 digits)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>z</td> <td>Day of the year</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Z</td> <td>Timezone offset in seconds</td> </tr> </table> </p> that defaults to the current local time if a timestamp is not given. <p> As idate always returns an integer and as they can't start with a \"0\", idate may return fewer digits than you would expect. See the example below. </p> /","params":[{"name":"format","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional] Default value: time(). The optional timestamp parameter is an integer Unix timestamp"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"idn_to_ascii","fqn":"idn_to_ascii","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"intl","location":{"file":"intl/intl.php","range":{"start":222056,"end":222068}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"variant","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"idna_info","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= 5.3.0, PHP 7, PECL intl &gt;= 1.0.2, PHP 7, PECL idn &gt;= 0.1)<br/> Convert domain name to IDNA ASCII form. Domain to convert. In PHP 5 must be UTF-8 encoded. If e.g. an ISO-8859-1 (aka Western Europe latin1) encoded string is passed it will be converted into an ACE encoded \"xn--\" string. It will not be the one you expected though! </p> Conversion options - combination of IDNA_* constants (except IDNA_ERROR_* constants). </p> Either INTL_IDNA_VARIANT_2003 for IDNA 2003 or INTL_IDNA_VARIANT_UTS46 for UTS #46. </p> This parameter can be used only if INTL_IDNA_VARIANT_UTS46 was used for variant. In that case, it will be filled with an array with the keys 'result', the possibly illegal result of the transformation, 'isTransitionalDifferent', a boolean indicating whether the usage of the transitional mechanisms of UTS #46 either has or would have changed the result and 'errors', which is an int representing a bitset of the error constants IDNA_ERROR_*. </p> /","params":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"variant","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"idn_to_utf8","fqn":"idn_to_utf8","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"intl","location":{"file":"intl/intl.php","range":{"start":223618,"end":223629}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"variant","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"idna_info","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= 5.3.0, PHP 7, PECL intl &gt;= 1.0.2, PHP 7, PECL idn &gt;= 0.1)<br/> Convert domain name from IDNA ASCII to Unicode. Domain to convert in IDNA ASCII-compatible format. The ASCII encoded domain name. Looks like \"xn--...\" if the it originally contained non-ASCII characters. </p> Conversion options - combination of IDNA_* constants (except IDNA_ERROR_* constants). </p> Either INTL_IDNA_VARIANT_2003 for IDNA 2003 or INTL_IDNA_VARIANT_UTS46 for UTS #46. </p> This parameter can be used only if INTL_IDNA_VARIANT_UTS46 was used for variant. In that case, it will be filled with an array with the keys 'result', the possibly illegal result of the transformation, 'isTransitionalDifferent', a boolean indicating whether the usage of the transitional mechanisms of UTS #46 either has or would have changed the result and 'errors', which is an int representing a bitset of the error constants IDNA_ERROR_*. </p> RFC 3490 4.2 states though \"ToUnicode never fails. If any step fails, then the original input sequence is returned immediately in that step.\" /","params":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"variant","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"igbinary_serialize","fqn":"igbinary_serialize","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"igbinary","location":{"file":"igbinary/igbinary.php","range":{"start":1311,"end":1329}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"value","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string|null"},"documentation":{"description":"Generates a storable representation of a value. This is useful for storing or passing PHP values around without losing their type and structure. To make the serialized string into a PHP value again, use {@link igbinary_unserialize}. igbinary_serialize() handles all types, except the resource-type. You can even serialize() arrays that contain references to itself. Circular references inside the array/object you are serialize()ing will also be stored. If object implements {@link https://secure.php.net/~helly/php/ext/spl/interfaceSerializable.html Serializable} -interface, PHP will call the member function serialize to get serialized representation of object. When serializing objects, PHP will attempt to call the member function __sleep prior to serialization. This is to allow the object to do any last minute clean-up, etc. prior to being serialized. Likewise, when the object is restored using unserialize() the __wakeup member function is called. /","params":[{"name":"value","declared_type":"mixed","description":"The value to be serialized."}],"return_type":"string|null","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"igbinary_unserialize","fqn":"igbinary_unserialize","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"igbinary","location":{"file":"igbinary/igbinary.php","range":{"start":2178,"end":2198}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"str","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"mixed|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Creates a PHP value from a stored representation. igbinary_unserialize() takes a single serialized variable and converts it back into a PHP value. If the variable being unserialized is an object, after successfully reconstructing the object PHP will automatically attempt to call the __wakeup() member function (if it exists). In case the passed string is not unserializeable, NULL is returned and E_WARNING is issued. /","params":[{"name":"str","declared_type":"string","description":"The serialized string."}],"return_type":"mixed|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"ignore_user_abort","fqn":"ignore_user_abort","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_4.php","range":{"start":31628,"end":31645}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"enable","declared_type":"?bool","phpdoc_type":"bool|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Set whether a client disconnect should abort script execution If set, this function will set the ignore_user_abort ini setting to the given value. If not, this function will only return the previous setting without changing it. </p> /","params":[{"name":"enable","declared_type":"bool|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"image2wbmp","fqn":"image2wbmp","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"gd","location":{"file":"gd/gd.php","range":{"start":68329,"end":68339}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"image","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource|GdImage","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"filename","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"threshold","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Output image to browser or file Path to the saved file. If not given, the raw image stream will be outputted directly. </p> Threshold value, between 0 and 255 (inclusive). </p> /","params":[{"name":"image","declared_type":"resource|GdImage","description":null},{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"threshold","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"image_type_to_extension","fqn":"image_type_to_extension","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":32701,"end":32724}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"image_type","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"include_dot","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get file extension for image type One of the IMAGETYPE_XXX constant. </p> Removed since 8.0. Whether to prepend a dot to the extension or not. Default to true. </p> /","params":[{"name":"image_type","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"include_dot","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"image_type_to_mime_type","fqn":"image_type_to_mime_type","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_0.php","range":{"start":32183,"end":32206}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"image_type","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Get Mime-Type for image-type returned by getimagesize, exif_read_data, exif_thumbnail, exif_imagetype One of the IMAGETYPE_XXX constants. </p> <table> Returned values Constants <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>imagetype</td> <td>Returned value</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_GIF</td> <td>image/gif</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_JPEG</td> <td>image/jpeg</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_PNG</td> <td>image/png</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_SWF</td> <td>application/x-shockwave-flash</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_PSD</td> <td>image/psd</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_BMP</td> <td>image/bmp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_TIFF_II (intel byte order)</td> <td>image/tiff</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td> IMAGETYPE_TIFF_MM (motorola byte order) </td> <td>image/tiff</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_JPC</td> <td>application/octet-stream</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_JP2</td> <td>image/jp2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_JPX</td> <td>application/octet-stream</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_JB2</td> <td>application/octet-stream</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_SWC</td> <td>application/x-shockwave-flash</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_IFF</td> <td>image/iff</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_WBMP</td> <td>image/vnd.wap.wbmp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_XBM</td> <td>image/xbm</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>IMAGETYPE_ICO</td> <td>image/vnd.microsoft.icon</td> </tr> </table> /","params":[{"name":"image_type","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"imageaffine","fqn":"imageaffine","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"gd","location":{"file":"gd/gd.php","range":{"start":96912,"end":96923}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"image","declared_type":"GdImage","phpdoc_type":"resourc