tion.date-default-timezone-set.php date_default_timezone_set()} and as returned by {@link https://php.net/manual/en/function.date-default-timezone-get.php date_default_timezone_get()}. </p> </li> <li> <p> An {@link https://php.net/manual/en/class.intltimezone.php IntlTimeZone}, which will be used directly. </p> </li> <li> <p> A {@link https://php.net/manual/en/class.datetimezone.php DateTimeZone}. Its identifier will be extracted and an ICU timezone object will be created; the timezone will be backed by ICU's database, not PHP's. </p> </li> <li> <p> A {@link https://php.net/manual/en/language.types.string.php string}, which should be a valid ICU timezone identifier. See  <b>IntlTimeZone::createTimeZoneIDEnumeration()</b>. Raw offsets such as <em>\"GMT+08:30\"</em> are also accepted. </p> </li> </ul> </p> A locale to use or <b>NULL</b> to use {@link https://php.net/manual/en/intl.configuration.php#ini.intl.default-locale the default locale}. </p> The created {@link https://php.net/manual/en/class.intlcalendar.php IntlCalendar} instance or <b>NULL</b> on failure. /","params":[{"name":"timezone","declared_type":"IntlTimeZone|DateTimeZone|string|null","description":"[optional] <p> <p>"},{"name":"locale","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"IntlCalendar|null","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"intlcal_equals","fqn":"intlcal_equals","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"intl","location":{"file":"intl/intl.php","range":{"start":257317,"end":257331}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"calendar","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","phpdoc_type":"IntlCalendar","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"other","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","phpdoc_type":"IntlCalendar","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;=5.5.0 PECL intl &gt;= 3.0.0a1)<br/> Compare time of two IntlCalendar objects for equality The calendar object, on the procedural style interface. </p> Returns <b>TRUE</b> if the current time of both this and the passed in {@link https://php.net/manual/en/class.intlcalendar.php IntlCalendar} object are the same, or <b>FALSE</b> otherwise. The value <b>FALSE</b> can also be returned on failure. This can only happen if bad arguments are passed in. In any case, the two cases can be distinguished by calling  {@link https://php.net/manual/en/function.intl-get-error-code.php intl_get_error_code()}. </p> /","params":[{"name":"calendar","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","description":"<p>"},{"name":"other","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","description":null}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"intlcal_field_difference","fqn":"intlcal_field_difference","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"intl","location":{"file":"intl/intl.php","range":{"start":238408,"end":238432}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"calendar","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","phpdoc_type":"IntlCalendar","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"float","phpdoc_type":"float","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;=5.5.0 PECL intl &gt;= 3.0.0a1)<br/> Calculate difference between given time and this object's time The calendar object, on the procedural style interface. </p> The time against which to compare the quantity represented by the <em>field</em>. For the result to be positive, the time given for this parameter must be ahead of the time of the object the method is being i