Zone}, which will be used directly. </p> </li> <li> <p> A {@link https://php.net/manual/en/class.datetimezone.php DateTimeZone}. Its identifier will be extracted and an ICU timezone object will be created; the timezone will be backed by ICU's database, not PHP's. </p> </li> <li> <p> A {@link https://php.net/manual/en/language.types.string.php string}, which should be a valid ICU timezone identifier. See  <b>IntlTimeZone::createTimeZoneIDEnumeration()</b>. Raw offsets such as <em>\"GMT+08:30\"</em> are also accepted. </p> </li> </ul> /","params":[{"name":"calendar","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timezone","declared_type":"IntlTimeZone|DateTimeZone|string|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"intlcal_to_date_time","fqn":"intlcal_to_date_time","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"intl","location":{"file":"intl/intl.php","range":{"start":261123,"end":261143}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"calendar","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","phpdoc_type":"IntlCalendar","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"DateTime|false","phpdoc_return_type":"DateTime|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;=5.5.0 PECL intl &gt;= 3.0.0a2)<br/> Convert an IntlCalendar into a DateTime object The calendar object, on the procedural style interface. </p> A {@link https://php.net/manual/en/class.datetime.php DateTime} object with the same timezone as this object (though using PHP's database instead of ICU's) and the same time, except for the smaller precision (second precision instead of millisecond). Returns <b>FALSE</b> on failure. /","params":[{"name":"calendar","declared_type":"IntlCalendar","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"DateTime|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":fals