 </p> <p> Note that you probably want to specify the mode as an octal number, which means it should have a leading zero. The mode is also modified by the current umask, which you can change using umask(). </p> Allows the creation of nested directories specified in the pathname. Default to false. </p> /","params":[{"name":"directory","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"permissions","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"recursive","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"context","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mktime","fqn":"mktime","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"date","location":{"file":"date/date.php","range":{"start":13366,"end":13372}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"hour","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"hour","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"minute","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"second","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"month","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"day","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"year","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"is_dst","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get Unix timestamp for a date The number of the hour. </p> The number of the minute. </p> The number of seconds past the minute. </p> The number of the month. </p> The number of the day. </p> The number of the year, may be a two or four digit value, with values between 0-69 mapping to 2000-2069 and 70-100 to 1970-2000. On systems where time_t is a 32bit signed integer, as most common today, the valid range for year is somewhere between 1901 and 2038. However, before PHP 5.1.0 this range was limited from 1970 to 2038 on some systems (e.g. Windows). </p> This parameter can be set to 1 if the time is during daylight savings time (DST), 0 if it is not, or -1 (the default) if it is unknown whether the time is within daylight savings time or not. If it's unknown, PHP tries to figure it out itself. This can cause unexpected (but not incorrect) results. Some times are invalid if DST is enabled on the system PHP is running on or is_dst is set to 1. If DST is enabled in e.g. 2:00, all times between 2:00 and 3:00 are invalid and mktime returns an undefined (usually negative) value. Some systems (e.g. Solaris 8) enable DST at midnight so time 0:30 of the day when DST is enabled is evaluated as 23:30 of the previous day. </p> <p> As of PHP 5.1.0, this parameter became deprecated. As a result, the new timezone handling features should be used instead. </p> <p> This parameter has been removed in PHP 7.0.0. </p> given. If the arguments are invalid, the function returns false (before PHP 5.1 it returned -1). /","params":[{"name":"hour","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"minute","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"second","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"month","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"day","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"year","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"is_dst","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","v