 e.g. hostname:port (Linux), or hostname,port (Windows). </p> The username. </p> The password. </p> If a second call is made to mssql_connect with the same arguments, no new link will be established, but instead, the link identifier of the already opened link will be returned. This parameter modifies this behavior and makes mssql_connect always open a new link, even if mssql_connect was called before with the same parameters. </p> /","params":[{"name":"servername","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"username","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"password","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"new_link","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mssql_data_seek","fqn":"mssql_data_seek","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mssql","location":{"file":"mssql/mssql.php","range":{"start":11735,"end":11750}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row_number","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 4, PHP 5, PECL odbtp &gt;= 1.1.1)<br/> Moves internal row pointer The result resource that is being evaluated. </p> The desired row number of the new result pointer. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"row_number","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mssql_execute","fqn":"mssql_execute","kind":"Function","origin":"Php