":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 4, PHP 5, PECL odbtp &gt;= 1.1.1)<br/> Send MS SQL query An SQL query. </p> A MS SQL link identifier, returned by mssql_connect or mssql_pconnect. </p> <p> If the link identifier isn't specified, the last opened link is assumed. If no link is open, the function tries to establish a link as if mssql_connect was called, and use it. </p> The number of records to batch in the buffer. </p> returned, or false on error. /","params":[{"name":"query","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"batch_size","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mssql_result","fqn":"mssql_result","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mssql","location":{"file":"mssql/mssql.php","range":{"start":13100,"end":13112}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 4, PHP 5, PECL odbtp &gt;= 1.1.1)<br/> Get result data The result resource that is being evaluated. This result comes from a call to mssql_query. </p> The row number. </p> Can be the field's offset, the field's name or the field's table dot field's name (tablename.fieldname). If the column name has been aliased ('select foo as bar from...'), it uses the alias instead of the column name. </p> <p> Specifying a numeric offset for the field argument is much quicker than specifying a fieldname or tablename.fieldname argument. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"row","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field","declared_type":"mixed","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mssql_rows_affected","fqn":"mssql_rows_affected","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mssql","location":{"file":"mssql/mssql.php","range":{"start":5281,"end":5300}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 4 &gt;= 4.0.4, PHP 5, PECL odbtp &gt;= 1.1.1)<br/> Returns the number of records affected by the query A MS SQL link identifier, returned by mssql_connect or mssql_pconnect. </p> /","params":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mssql_select_db","fqn":"mssql_select_db","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mssql","location":{"file":"mssql/mssql.php","range":{"start":3571,"end":3586}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"database_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 4, PHP 5, PECL odbtp &gt;= 1.1.1)<br/> Select MS SQL database The database name. </p> <p> To escape the name of a database that contains spaces, hyphens (\"-\"), or any other exceptional characters, the database name must be enclosed in brackets, as is shown in the example, below. This technique must also be applied when selecting a database name that is also a reserved word (such as primary). </p> A MS SQL link identifier, returned by mssql_connect or mssql_pconnect. </p> <p> If no link identifier is specified, the last opened link is assumed. If no link is open, the function will try to establish a link as if mssql_connect was called, and use it. </p> /","params":[{"name":"database_name","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mt_getrandmax","fqn":"mt_getrandmax","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"random","location":{"file":"random/random.php","range":{"start":2960,"end":2973}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Show largest possible random value /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mt_rand","fqn":"mt_rand","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"random","location":{"file":"random/random.php","range":{"start":2710,"end":2717}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"min","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"max","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Generate a random value via the Mersenne Twister Random Number Generator Optional lowest value to be returned (default: 0) </p> Optional highest value to be returned (default: mt_getrandmax()) </p> and max (or mt_getrandmax, inclusive) /","params":[{"name":"min","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"max","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mt_srand","fqn":"mt_srand","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"random","location":{"file":"random/random.php","range":{"start":918,"end":926}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"seed","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"Seeds the Mersenne Twister Random Number Generator An optional seed value </p> Use one of the following constants to specify the implementation of the algorithm to use. </p> /","params":[{"name":"seed","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql","fqn":"mysql","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":27486,"end":27491}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"database_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"query","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[{"name":"database_name","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"query","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_affected_rows","fqn":"mysql_affected_rows","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":11961,"end":11980}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Get number of affected rows in previous MySQL operation failed. </p> <p> If the last query was a DELETE query with no WHERE clause, all of the records will have been deleted from the table but this function will return zero with MySQL versions prior to 4.1.2. </p> <p> When using UPDATE, MySQL will not update columns where the new value is the same as the old value. This creates the possibility that <b>mysql_affected_rows</b> may not actually equal the number of rows matched, only the number of rows that were literally affected by the query. </p> <p> The REPLACE statement first deletes the record with the same primary key and then inserts the new record. This function returns the number of deleted records plus the number of inserted records. /","params":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_client_encoding","fqn":"mysql_client_encoding","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":24634,"end":24655}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the name of the character set /","params":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_close","fqn":"mysql_close","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":3937,"end":3948}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Close MySQL connection /","params":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_connect","fqn":"mysql_connect","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":2156,"end":2169}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"server","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"username","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"password","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"new_link","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"client_flags","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Open a connection to a MySQL Server The MySQL server. It can also include a port number. e.g. \"hostname:port\" or a path to a local socket e.g. \":/path/to/socket\" for the localhost. </p> <p> If the PHP directive mysql.default_host is undefined (default), then the default value is 'localhost:3306'. In \"ini.sql.safe-mode\", this parameter is ignored and value 'localhost:3306' is always used. </p> The username. Default value is defined by mysql.default_user. In \"ini.sql.safe-mode\", this parameter is ignored and the name of the user that owns the server process is used. </p> The password. Default value is defined by mysql.default_password. In \"ini.sql.safe-mode\", this parameter is ignored and empty password is used. </p> If a second call is made to <b>mysql_connect</b> with the same arguments, no new link will be established, but instead, the link identifier of the already opened link will be returned. The <i>new_link</i> parameter modifies this behavior and makes <b>mysql_connect</b> always open a new link, even if <b>mysql_connect</b> was called before with the same parameters. In \"ini.sql.safe-mode\", this parameter is ignored. </p> The <i>client_flags</i> parameter can be a combination of the following constants: 128 (enable LOAD DATA LOCAL handling), <b>MYSQL_CLIENT_SSL</b>, <b>MYSQL_CLIENT_COMPRESS</b>, <b>MYSQL_CLIENT_IGNORE_SPACE</b> or <b>MYSQL_CLIENT_INTERACTIVE</b>. Read the section about for further information. In \"ini.sql.safe-mode\", this parameter is ignored. </p> /","params":[{"name":"server","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"username","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"password","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"new_link","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"client_flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_data_seek","fqn":"mysql_data_seek","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":18169,"end":18184}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row_number","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Move internal result pointer The desired row number of the new result pointer. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":null},{"name":"row_number","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_db_name","fqn":"mysql_db_name","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":30811,"end":30824}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Retrieves database name from the call to {@see mysql_list_dbs} The result pointer from a call to <b>mysql_list_dbs</b>. </p> The index into the result set. </p> The field name. </p> is returned, use <b>mysql_error</b> to determine the nature of the error. /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"row","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field","declared_type":"mixed","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_db_query","fqn":"mysql_db_query","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":7929,"end":7943}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"database","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"query","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Selects a database and executes a query on it The name of the database that will be selected. </p> The MySQL query. </p> <p> Data inside the query should be properly escaped. </p> or false on error. The function also returns true/false for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE queries to indicate success/failure. /","params":[{"name":"database","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"query","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"resource|bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_dbname","fqn":"mysql_dbname","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":31029,"end":31041}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"row","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"field","declared_type":null,"description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_errno","fqn":"mysql_errno","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":10856,"end":10867}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the numerical value of the error message from previous MySQL operation 0 (zero) if no error occurred. /","params":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_error","fqn":"mysql_error","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":10466,"end":10477}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the text of the error message from previous MySQL operation '' (empty string) if no error occurred. /","params":[{"name":"link_identifier","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_escape_string","fqn":"mysql_escape_string","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":22992,"end":23011}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"unescaped_string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Escapes a string for use in a mysql_query The string that is to be escaped. </p> /","params":[{"name":"unescaped_string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_fetch_array","fqn":"mysql_fetch_array","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":15894,"end":15911}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"result_type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetch a result row as an associative array, a numeric array, or both The type of array that is to be fetched. It's a constant and can take the following values: <b>MYSQL_ASSOC</b>, <b>MYSQL_NUM</b>, and <b>MYSQL_BOTH</b>. </p> if there are no more rows. The type of returned array depends on how <i>result_type</i> is defined. By using <b>MYSQL_BOTH</b> (default), you'll get an array with both associative and number indices. Using <b>MYSQL_ASSOC</b>, you only get associative indices (as <b>mysql_fetch_assoc</b> works), using <b>MYSQL_NUM</b>, you only get number indices (as <b>mysql_fetch_row</b> works). </p> <p> If two or more columns of the result have the same field names, the last column will take precedence. To access the other column(s) of the same name, you must use the numeric index of the column or make an alias for the column. For aliased columns, you cannot access the contents with the original column name. /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":null},{"name":"result_type","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_fetch_assoc","fqn":"mysql_fetch_assoc","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":16648,"end":16665}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetch a result row as an associative array false if there are no more rows. </p> <p> If two or more columns of the result have the same field names, the last column will take precedence. To access the other column(s) of the same name, you either need to access the result with numeric indices by using <b>mysql_fetch_row</b> or add alias names. See the example at the <b>mysql_fetch_array</b> description about aliases. /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":null}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_fetch_field","fqn":"mysql_fetch_field","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":19632,"end":19649}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"object"},"documentation":{"description":"Get column information from a result and return as an object The numerical field offset. If the field offset is not specified, the next field that was not yet retrieved by this function is retrieved. The <i>field_offset</i> starts at 0. </p> of the object are: </p> <p> name - column name table - name of the table the column belongs to def - default value of the column max_length - maximum length of the column not_null - 1 if the column cannot be null primary_key - 1 if the column is a primary key unique_key - 1 if the column is a unique key multiple_key - 1 if the column is a non-unique key numeric - 1 if the column is numeric blob - 1 if the column is a BLOB type - the type of the column unsigned - 1 if the column is unsigned zerofill - 1 if the column is zero-filled /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":null},{"name":"field_offset","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"object","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"mysql_fetch_lengths","fqn":"mysql_fetch_lengths","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysql","location":{"file":"mysql/mysql.php","range":{"start":18487,"end":18506}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the length of each output in a result /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resour