h of data to be copied. </p> /","params":[{"name":"lob_to","declared_type":"OCI_Lob","description":"<p>"},{"name":"lob_from","declared_type":"OCI_Lob","description":"<p>"},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"oci_lob_is_equal","fqn":"oci_lob_is_equal","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"oci8","location":{"file":"oci8/oci8.php","range":{"start":51679,"end":51695}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"lob1","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"OCI_Lob","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"lob2","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"OCI_Lob","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL OCI8 &gt;= 1.1.0)<br/> Compares two LOB/FILE locators for equality A LOB identifier. </p> A LOB identifier. </p> /","params":[{"name":"lob1","declared_type":"OCI_Lob","description":"<p>"},{"name":"lob2","declared_type":"OCI_Lob","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"oci_new_collection","fqn":"oci_new_collection","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"oci8","location":{"file":"oci8/oci8.php","range":{"start":58397,"end":58415}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"tdo","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"schema","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"OCI_Collection|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL OCI8 &gt;= 1.1.0)<br/> Allocates new collection object An Oracle connection identifier, returned by {@see oci_connect} or {@see oci_pconnect}. </p> Should be a valid named type (uppercase). </p> Should point to the scheme, where the named type was created. The name of the current user is the default value. </p> error. /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"tdo","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"schema","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"OCI_Collection|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"oci_new_connect","fqn":"oci_new_connect","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"oci8","location":{"file":"oci8/oci8.php","range":{"start":46070,"end":46085}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"username","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"password","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"connection_string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"character_set","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"session_mode","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL OCI8 &gt;= 1.1.0)<br/> Connect to the Oracle server using a unique connection The Oracle user name. </p> The password for <i>username</i>. </p> the Oracle instance to connect to. It can be an Easy Connect string, or a Connect Name from the tnsnames.ora file, or the name of a local Oracle instance. </p> <p> If not specified, PHP uses environment variables such as <b>TWO_TASK</b> (on Linux) or <b>LOCAL</b> (on Windows) and <b>ORACLE_SID</b> to determine the Oracle instance to connect to. </p> <p> To use the Easy Connect naming method, PHP must be linked with Oracle 10g or greater Client libraries. The Easy Connect string for Oracle 10g is of the form: [//]host_name[:port][/service_name]. From Oracle 11g, the syntax is: [//]host_name[:port][/service_name][:server_type][/instance_name]. Service names can be found by running the Oracle utility lsnrctl status on the database server machine. </p> <p> The tnsnames.ora file can be in the Oracle Net search path, which includes $ORACLE_HOME/network/admin and /etc. Alternatively set TNS_ADMIN so that $TNS_ADMIN/tnsnames.ora is read. Make sure the web daemon has read access to the file. </p> the character set used by the Oracle Client libraries. The character set does not need to match the character set used by the database. If it doesn't match, Oracle will do its best to convert data to and from the database character set. Depending on the character sets this may not give usable results. Conversion also adds some time overhead. </p> <p> If not specified, the Oracle Client libraries determine a character set from the <b>NLS_LANG</b> environment variable. </p> <p> Passing this parameter can reduce the time taken to connect. </p> parameter is available since version PHP 5 (PECL OCI8 1.1) and accepts the following values: <b>OCI_DEFAULT</b>, <b>OCI_SYSOPER</b> and <b>OCI_SYSDBA</b>. If either <b>OCI_SYSOPER</b> or <b>OCI_SYSDBA</b> were specified, this function will try to establish privileged connection using external credentials. Privileged connections are disabled by default. To enable them you need to set oci8.privileged_connect to On. </p> <p> PHP 5.3 (PECL OCI8 1.3.4) introduced the <b>OCI_CRED_EXT</b> mode value. This tells Oracle to use External or OS authentication, which must be configured in the database. The <b>OCI_CRED_EXT</b> flag can only be used with username of &#x00022;/&#x00022; and a empty password. oci8.privileged_connect may be On or Off. </p> <p> <b>OCI_CRED_EXT</b> may be combined with the <b>OCI_SYSOPER</b> or <b>OCI_SYSDBA</b> modes. </p> <p> <b>OCI_CRED_EXT</b> is not supported on Windows for security reasons. </p> /","params":[{"name":"username","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"password","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"connection_string","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>Contains"},{"name":"character_set","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>Determines"},{"name":"session_mode","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>This"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"oci_new_cursor","fqn":"oci_new_cursor","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"oci8","location":{"file":"oci8/oci8.php","range":{"start":36200,"end":36214}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL OCI8 &gt;= 1.1.0)<br/> Allocates and returns a new cursor (statement handle) An Oracle connection identifier, returned by {@see oci_connect} or {@see oci_pconnect}. </p> /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"oci_new_descriptor","fqn":"oci_new_descriptor","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"oci8","location":{"file":"oci8/oci8.php","range":{"start":53967,"end":53985}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional"