ction","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Zend OPcache","location":{"file":"Zend OPcache/OPcache.php","range":{"start":4235,"end":4273}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"Tells whether a script is cached in OPCache file cache This function checks if a PHP script has been cached in OPCache. This can be used to more easily detect the \"warming\" of the cache for a particular script. This function only checks file cache, not in-memory cache. In order to check in-memory cache, use opcache_is_script_cached. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"opcache_jit_blacklist","fqn":"opcache_jit_blacklist","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Zend OPcache","location":{"file":"Zend OPcache/OPcache.php","range":{"start":3714,"end":3735}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"closure","declared_type":"Closure","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"Blacklists a function from being JIT compiled This function blacklists a particular function from being JIT compiled when Tracing JIT is in use. The function is specified using a Closure. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"opcache_reset","fqn":"opcache_reset","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Zend OPcache","location":{"file":"Zend OPcache/OPcache.php","range":{"start":1543,"end":1556}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= 5.5.0, PECL ZendOpcache &gt;= 7.0.0 )<br/> Resets the contents of the opcode cache /","params":[],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"opendir","fqn":"opendir","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_7.php","range":{"start":10001,"end":10008}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"directory","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Open directory handle The directory path that is to be opened </p> For a description of the context parameter, refer to the streams section of the manual. </p> false on failure. </p> <p> If path is not a valid directory or the directory can not be opened due to permission restrictions or filesystem errors, opendir returns false and generates a PHP error of level E_WARNING. You can suppress the error output of opendir by prepending '@' to the front of the function name. /","params":[{"name":"directory","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"context","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"openlog","fqn":"openlog","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_7.php","range":{"start":36489,"end":36496}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"prefix","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"facility","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Open connection to system logger The string ident is added to each message. </p> The option argument is used to indicate what logging options will be used when generating a log message. <table> openlog Options <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Constant</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_CONS</td> <td> if there is an error while sending data to the system logger, write directly to the system console </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_NDELAY</td> <td> open the connection to the logger immediately </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_ODELAY</td> <td> (default) delay opening the connection until the first message is logged </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_PERROR</td> <td>print log message also to standard error</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_PID</td> <td>include PID with each message</td> </tr> </table> You can use one or more of this options. When using multiple options you need to OR them, i.e. to open the connection immediately, write to the console and include the PID in each message, you will use: LOG_CONS | LOG_NDELAY | LOG_PID </p> The facility argument is used to specify what type of program is logging the message. This allows you to specify (in your machine's syslog configuration) how messages coming from different facilities will be handled. <table> openlog Facilities <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Constant</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_AUTH</td> <td> security/authorization messages (use LOG_AUTHPRIV instead in systems where that constant is defined) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_AUTHPRIV</td> <td>security/authorization messages (private)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_CRON</td> <td>clock daemon (cron and at)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_DAEMON</td> <td>other system daemons</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_KERN</td> <td>kernel messages</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_LOCAL0 ... LOG_LOCAL7</td> <td>reserved for local use, these are not available in Windows</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_LPR</td> <td>line printer subsystem</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_MAIL</td> <td>mail subsystem</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_NEWS</td> <td>USENET news subsystem</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_SYSLOG</td> <td>messages generated internally by syslogd</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_USER</td> <td>generic user-level messages</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>LOG_UUCP</td> <td>UUCP subsystem</td> </tr> </table> </p> <p> LOG_USER is the only valid log type under Windows operating systems </p> /","params":[{"name":"prefix","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"facility","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"openssl_cipher_iv_length","fqn":"openssl_cipher_iv_length","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"openssl","location":{"file":"openssl/openssl.php","range":{"start":32122,"end":32146}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"cipher_algo","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= PHP 5.3.3)<br/> Gets the cipher iv length The method. </p> /","params":[{"name":"cipher_algo","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"openssl_cipher_key_length","fqn":"openssl_cipher_key_length","kind":"Fu