:true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"connection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"statement_name","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"statement_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"params","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Sends a request to execute a prepared statement with given parameters, and waits for the result. PostgreSQL database connection resource. When <i>connection</i> is not present, the default connection is used. The default connection is the last connection made by <b>pg_connect</b> or <b>pg_pconnect</b>. </p> The name of the prepared statement to execute. if \"\" is specified, then the unnamed statement is executed. The name must have been previously prepared using <b>pg_prepare</b>, <b>pg_send_prepare</b> or a PREPARE SQL command. </p> An array of parameter values to substitute for the $1, $2, etc. placeholders in the original prepared query string. The number of elements in the array must match the number of placeholders. </p> <p> Elements are converted to strings by calling this function. </p> /","params":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"statement_name","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"params","declared_type":"array","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"pg_exit_pipeline_mode","fqn":"pg_exit_pipeline_mode","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"pgsql","location":{"file":"pgsql/pgsql.php","range":{"start":83923,"end":83944}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"connection","declared_type":"PgSql\\Connection","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"pg_fetch_all","fqn":"pg_fetch_all","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"pgsql","location":{"file":"pgsql/pgsql.php","range":{"start":31822,"end":31834}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetches all rows from a result as an array PostgreSQL query result resource, returned by <b>pg_query</b>, <b>pg_query_params</b> or <b>pg_execute</b> (among others). </p> An optional parameter that controls how the returned array is indexed. <i>result_type</i> is a constant and can take the following values: <b>PGSQL_ASSOC</b>, <b>PGSQL_NUM</b> and <b>PGSQL_BOTH</b>. Using <b>PGSQL_NUM</b>, <b>pg_fetch_array</b> will return an array with numerical indices, using <b>PGSQL_ASSOC</b> it will return only associative indices while <b>PGSQL_BOTH</b>, the default, will return both numerical and associative indices. </p> of field values indexed by field name. </p> <p> <b>FALSE</b> is returned if there are no rows in the result, or on any other error. /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"pg_fetch_all_columns","fqn":"pg_fetch_all_columns","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"pgsql","location":{"file":"pgsql/pgsql.php","range":{"start":32635,"end":32655}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"field","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetches all rows in a particular result column as an array PostgreSQL query result resource, returned by <b>pg_query</b>, <b>pg_query_params</b> or <b>pg_execute</b> (among others). </p> Column number, zero-based, to be retrieved from the result resource. Defaults to the first column if not specified. </p> <p> <b>FALSE</b> is returned if <i>column</i> is larger than the number of columns in the result, or on any other error. </p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"field","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"pg_fetch_array","fqn":"pg_fetch_array","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"pgsql","location":{"file":"pgsql/pgsql.php","range":{"start":29268,"end":29282}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetch a row as an array PostgreSQL query result resource, returned by <b>pg_query</b>, <b>pg_query_params</b> or <b>pg_execute</b> (among others). </p> Row number in result to fetch. Rows are numbered from 0 upwards. If omitted or <b>NULL</b>, the next row is fetched. </p> An optional parameter that controls how the returned array is indexed. <i>result_type</i> is a constant and can take the following values: <b>PGSQL_ASSOC</b>, <b>PGSQL_NUM</b> and <b>PGSQL_BOTH</b>. Using <b>PGSQL_NUM</b>, <b>pg_fetch_array</b> will return an array with numerical indices, using <b>PGSQL_ASSOC</b> it will return only associative indices while <b>PGSQL_BOTH</b>, the default, will return both numerical and associative indices. </p> associatively (indexed by field name), or both. Each value in the array is represented as a string. Database NULL values are returned as <b>NULL</b>. </p> <p> <b>FALSE</b> is returned if <i>row</i> exceeds the number of rows in the set, there are no more rows, or on any other error. /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"row","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"pg_fetch_assoc","fqn":"pg_fetch_assoc","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"pgsql","location":{"file":"pgsql/pgsql.php","range":{"start":27791,"end":27805}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"row","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetch a row as an associative array PostgreSQL query result resource, returned by <b>pg_query</b>