ion":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":17821,"end":17833}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"community","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"retries","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Return all objects including their respective object ID within the specified one In case of an error, an E_WARNING message is shown. /","params":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>The hostname of the SNMP agent (server).</p>"},{"name":"community","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>The read community.</p>"},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>The SNMP object id which precedes the wanted one.</p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>The number of microseconds until the first timeout.</p>"},{"name":"retries","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>The number of times to retry if timeouts occur.</p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"snmpset","fqn":"snmpset","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":21949,"end":21956}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"community","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"value","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"retries","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Set the value of an SNMP object The hostname of the SNMP agent (server). </p> The write community. </p> The SNMP object id. </p> </p> types <tr valign=\"top\"><td>=</td><td>The type is taken from the MIB</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>i</td><td>INTEGER</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>u</td><td>INTEGER</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>s</td><td>STRING</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>x</td><td>HEX STRING</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>d</td><td>DECIMAL STRING</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>n</td><td>NULLOBJ</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>o</td><td>OBJID</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>t</td><td>TIMETICKS</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>a</td><td>IPADDRESS</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>b</td><td>BITS</td></tr> </table> If <b>OPAQUE_SPECIAL_TYPES</b> was defined while compiling the SNMP library, the following are also valid: </p> types <tr valign=\"top\"><td>U</td><td>unsigned int64</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>I</td><td>signed int64</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>F</td><td>float</td></tr> <tr valign=\"top\"><td>D</td><td>double</td></tr> </table> Most of these will use the obvious corresponding ASN.1 type. &#x00027;s&#x00027;, &#x00027;x&#x00027;, &#x00027;d&#x00027; and &#x00027;b&#x00027; are all different ways of specifying an OCTET STRING value, and the &#x00027;u&#x00027; unsigned type is also used for handling Gauge32 values. </p> If the MIB-Files are loaded by into the MIB Tree with \"snmp_read_mib\" or by specifying it in the libsnmp config, &#x00027;=&#x00027; may be used as the <i>type</i> parameter for all object ids as the type can then be automatically read from the MIB. </p> Note that there are two ways to set a variable of the type BITS like e.g. \"SYNTAX BITS {telnet(0), ftp(1), http(2), icmp(3), snmp(4), ssh(5), https(6)}\": </p> Using type \"b\" and a list of bit numbers. This method is not recommended since GET query for the same OID would return e.g. 0xF8. Using type \"x\" and a hex number but without(!) the usual \"0x\" prefix. See examples section for more details. </p> The new value. </p> The number of microseconds until the first timeout. </p> The number of times to retry if timeouts occur. </p> <p> If the SNMP host rejects the data type, an E_WARNING message like \"Warning: Error in packet. Reason: (badValue) The value given has the wrong type or length.\" is shown. If an unknown or invalid OID is specified the warning probably reads \"Could not add variable\". </p> /","params":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"community","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"string","description":"The MIB defines the type of each object id. It has to be specified as a single character from the below list."},{"name":"value","declared_type":"mixed","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"retries","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"snmpwalk","fqn":"snmpwalk","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":17004,"end":17012}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"community","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"retries","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Fetch all the SNMP objects from an agent The SNMP agent (server). </p> The read community. </p> If <b>NULL</b>, <i>object_id</i> is taken as the root of the SNMP objects tree and all objects under that tree are returned as an array. </p> <p> If <i>object_id</i> is specified, all the SNMP objects below that <i>object_id</i> are returned. </p> The number of microseconds until the first timeout. </p> <i>object_id</i> as root or <b>FALSE</b> on error. /","params":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"community","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"retries","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>The number of times to retry if timeouts occur.</p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"snmpwalkoid","fqn":"snmpwalkoid","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":18828,"end":18839}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"community","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"retries","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Query for a tree of information about a network entity The SNMP agent. </p> The read community. </p> If <b>NULL</b>, <i>object_id</i> is taken as the root of the SNMP objects tree and all objects under that tree are returned as an array. </p> <p> If <i>object_id</i> is specified, all the SNMP objects below that <i>object_id</i> are returned. </p> The number of microseconds until the first timeout. </p> The number of times to retry if timeouts occur. </p> object value starting from the <i>object_id</i> as root or <b>FALSE</b> on error. /","params":[{"name":"hostname","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"community","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"object_id","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"retries","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_accept","fqn":"socket_accept","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":12251,"end":12264}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"Socket|false","phpdoc_return_type":"resource|Socket|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Accepts a connection on a socket A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b>. </p> error code can be retrieved by calling <b>socket_last_error</b>. This error code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|Socket|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_addrinfo_bind","fqn":"socket_addrinfo_bind","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":1994,"end":2014}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"AddressInfo","phpdoc_type":"resource|AddressInfo","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"Socket|false","phpdoc_return_type":"resource|Socket|null|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 7 &gt;= 7.2.0)<br/> Create a Socket resource, and bind it to the provided AddrInfo resource.<br/> The return value of this function may be used with {@see socket_listen()}. Resource created from {@see socket_addrinfo_lookup()} </p> /","params":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"resource|AddressInfo","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|Socket|null|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_addrinfo_connect","fqn":"socket_addrinfo_connect","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":1445,"end":1468}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"AddressInfo","phpdoc_type":"resource|AddressInfo","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"Socket|false","phpdoc_return_type":"resource|Socket|null|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Create a Socket resource, and connect it to the provided AddrInfo resource.<br/> The return value of this function may be used with the rest of the socket functions. Resource created from {@see socket_addrinfo_lookup()} </p> /","params":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"resource|AddressInfo","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|Socket|null|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_addrinfo_explain","fqn":"socket_addrinfo_explain","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":2706,"end":2729}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"AddressInfo","phpdoc_type":"resource|AddressInfo","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 7 &gt;= 7.2.0)<br/> Get information about addrinfo Resource created from {@see socket_addrinfo_lookup()} </p> /","params":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"resource|AddressInfo","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_addrinfo_lookup","fqn":"socket_addrinfo_lookup","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":807,"end":829}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"host","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"service","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"hints","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"error_code","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"AddressInfo[]|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 7 &gt;= 7.2.0)<br/> Get array with contents of getaddrinfo about the given hostname. Hostname to search. </p> The service to connect to. If service is a name, it is translated to the corresponding port number. </p> Hints provide criteria for selecting addresses returned. You may specify the hints as defined by getadrinfo. </p> /","params":[{"name":"host","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"service","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"hints","declared_type":"array","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"AddressInfo[]|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_atmark","fqn":"socket_atmark","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":44919,"end":44932}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"Determines whether socket is at out-of-band mark /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_bind","fqn":"socket_bind","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":22214,"end":22225}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"port","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Binds a name to a socket A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b>. </p> If the socket is of the <b>AF_INET</b> family, the <i>address</i> is an IP in dotted-quad notation (e.g. 127.0.0.1). </p> <p> If the socket is of the <b>AF_UNIX</b> family, the <i>address</i> is the path of a Unix-domain socket (e.g. /tmp/my.sock). </p> The <i>port</i> parameter is only used when binding an <b>AF_INET</b> socket, and designates the port on which to listen for connections. </p> <p> The error code can be retrieved with <b>socket_last_error</b>. This code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"port","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_clear_error","fqn":"socket_clear_error","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":42787,"end":42805}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"?Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"Clears the error on the socket or the last error code A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_close","fqn":"socket_close","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":14647,"end":14659}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"Closes a socket resource A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_cmsg_space","fqn":"socket_cmsg_space","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":43386,"end":43403}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"num","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"?int","phpdoc_return_type":"int|null"},"documentation":{"description":"Calculate message buffer size /","params":[{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","description":null},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":null},{"name":"num","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"int|null","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_connect","fqn":"socket_connect","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":20804,"end":20818}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"port","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Initiates a connection on a socket The <i>address</i> parameter is either an IPv4 address in dotted-quad notation (e.g. 127.0.0.1) if <i>socket</i> is <b>AF_INET</b>, a valid IPv6 address (e.g. ::1) if IPv6 support is enabled and <i>socket</i> is <b>AF_INET6</b> or the pathname of a Unix domain socket, if the socket family is <b>AF_UNIX</b>. </p> The <i>port</i> parameter is only used and is mandatory when connecting to an <b>AF_INET</b> or an <b>AF_INET6</b> socket, and designates the port on the remote host to which a connection should be made. </p> <b>socket_last_error</b>. This code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. </p> <p> If the socket is non-blocking then this function returns <b>FALSE</b> with an error Operation now in progress. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":null},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"port","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_create","fqn":"socket_create","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":9330,"end":9343}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"Socket|false","phpdoc_return_type":"resource|Socket|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Create a socket (endpoint for communication) The <i>domain</i> parameter specifies the protocol family to be used by the socket. </p> <table> Available address/protocol families <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Domain</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>AF_INET</b></td> <td> IPv4 Internet based protocols. TCP and UDP are common protocols of this protocol family. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>AF_INET6</b></td> <td> IPv6 Internet based protocols. TCP and UDP are common protocols of this protocol family. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>AF_UNIX</b></td> <td> Local communication protocol family. High efficiency and low overhead make it a great form of IPC (Interprocess Communication). </td> </tr> </table> The <i>type</i> parameter selects the type of communication to be used by the socket. </p> <table> Available socket types <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Type</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SOCK_STREAM</b></td> <td> Provides sequenced, reliable, full-duplex, connection-based byte streams. An out-of-band data transmission mechanism may be supported. The TCP protocol is based on this socket type. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SOCK_DGRAM</b></td> <td> Supports datagrams (connectionless, unreliable messages of a fixed maximum length). The UDP protocol is based on this socket type. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SOCK_SEQPACKET</b></td> <td> Provides a sequenced, reliable, two-way connection-based data transmission path for datagrams of fixed maximum length; a consumer is required to read an entire packet with each read call. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SOCK_RAW</b></td> <td> Provides raw network protocol access. This special type of socket can be used to manually construct any type of protocol. A common use for this socket type is to perform ICMP requests (like ping). </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SOCK_RDM</b></td> <td> Provides a reliable datagram layer that does not guarantee ordering. This is most likely not implemented on your operating system. </td> </tr> </table> The <i>protocol</i> parameter sets the specific protocol within the specified <i>domain</i> to be used when communicating on the returned socket. The proper value can be retrieved by name by using <b>getprotobyname</b>. If the desired protocol is TCP, or UDP the corresponding constants <b>SOL_TCP</b>, and <b>SOL_UDP</b> can also be used. </p> <table> Common protocols <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Name</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>icmp</td> <td> The Internet Control Message Protocol is used primarily by gateways and hosts to report errors in datagram communication. The \"ping\" command (present in most modern operating systems) is an example application of ICMP. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>udp</td> <td> The User Datagram Protocol is a connectionless, unreliable, protocol with fixed record lengths. Due to these aspects, UDP requires a minimum amount of protocol overhead. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>tcp</td> <td> The Transmission Control Protocol is a reliable, connection based, stream oriented, full duplex protocol. TCP guarantees that all data packets will be received in the order in which they were sent. If any packet is somehow lost during communication, TCP will automatically retransmit the packet until the destination host acknowledges that packet. For reliability and performance reasons, the TCP implementation itself decides the appropriate octet boundaries of the underlying datagram communication layer. Therefore, TCP applications must allow for the possibility of partial record transmission. </td> </tr> </table> or <b>FALSE</b> on error. The actual error code can be retrieved by calling <b>socket_last_error</b>. This error code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. /","params":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|Socket|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_create_listen","fqn":"socket_create_listen","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":10437,"end":10457}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"port","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"backlog","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"Socket|false","phpdoc_return_type":"resource|Socket|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Opens a socket on port to accept connections The port on which to listen on all interfaces. </p> The <i>backlog</i> parameter defines the maximum length the queue of pending connections may grow to. <b>SOMAXCONN</b> may be passed as <i>backlog</i> parameter, see <b>socket_listen</b> for more information. </p> on success or <b>FALSE</b> on error. The error code can be retrieved with <b>socket_last_error</b>. This code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. /","params":[{"name":"port","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"backlog","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|Socket|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_create_pair","fqn":"socket_create_pair","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":11672,"end":11690}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"pair","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Creates a pair of indistinguishable sockets and stores them in an array The <i>domain</i> parameter specifies the protocol family to be used by the socket. See <b>socket_create</b> for the full list. </p> The <i>type</i> parameter selects the type of communication to be used by the socket. See <b>socket_create</b> for the full list. </p> The <i>protocol</i> parameter sets the specific protocol within the specified <i>domain</i> to be used when communicating on the returned socket. The proper value can be retrieved by name by using <b>getprotobyname</b>. If the desired protocol is TCP, or UDP the corresponding constants <b>SOL_TCP</b>, and <b>SOL_UDP</b> can also be used. </p> <p> See <b>socket_create</b> for the full list of supported protocols. </p> Reference to an array in which the two socket resources will be inserted. </p> /","params":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_export_stream","fqn":"socket_export_stream","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":9614,"end":9634}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|Socket|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Export a socket into a stream that encapsulates a socket /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":null}],"return_type":"resource|Socket|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_get_option","fqn":"socket_get_option","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":40246,"end":40263}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Gets socket options for the socket A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> The <i>level</i> parameter specifies the protocol level at which the option resides. For example, to retrieve options at the socket level, a <i>level</i> parameter of <b>SOL_SOCKET</b> would be used. Other levels, such as <b>TCP</b>, can be used by specifying the protocol number of that level. Protocol numbers can be found by using the <b>getprotobyname</b> function. </p> Available Socket Options <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Option</td> <td>Description</td> <td>Type</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_DEBUG</b></td> <td> Reports whether debugging information is being recorded. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_BROADCAST</b></td> <td> Reports whether transmission of broadcast messages is supported. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_REUSEADDR</b></td> <td> Reports whether local addresses can be reused. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_KEEPALIVE</b></td> <td> Reports whether connections are kept active with periodic transmission of messages. If the connected socket fails to respond to these messages, the connection is broken and processes writing to that socket are notified with a SIGPIPE signal. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_LINGER</b></td> <td> <p> Reports whether the <i>socket</i> lingers on <b>socket_close</b> if data is present. By default, when the socket is closed, it attempts to send all unsent data. In the case of a connection-oriented socket, <b>socket_close</b> will wait for its peer to acknowledge the data. </p> <p> If l_onoff is non-zero and l_linger is zero, all the unsent data will be discarded and RST (reset) is sent to the peer in the case of a connection-oriented socket. </p> <p> On the other hand, if l_onoff is non-zero and l_linger is non-zero, <b>socket_close</b> will block until all the data is sent or the time specified in l_linger elapses. If the socket is non-blocking, <b>socket_close</b> will fail and return an error. </p> </td> <td> array. The array will contain two keys: l_onoff and l_linger. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_OOBINLINE</b></td> <td> Reports whether the <i>socket</i> leaves out-of-band data inline. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_SNDBUF</b></td> <td> Reports the size of the send buffer. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_RCVBUF</b></td> <td> Reports the size of the receive buffer. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_ERROR</b></td> <td> Reports information about error status and clears it. </td> <td> int (cannot be set by <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_TYPE</b></td> <td> Reports the <i>socket</i> type (e.g. <b>SOCK_STREAM</b>). </td> <td> int (cannot be set by <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_DONTROUTE</b></td> <td> Reports whether outgoing messages bypass the standard routing facilities. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_RCVLOWAT</b></td> <td> Reports the minimum number of bytes to process for <i>socket</i> input operations. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_RCVTIMEO</b></td> <td> Reports the timeout value for input operations. </td> <td> array. The array will contain two keys: sec which is the seconds part on the timeout value and usec which is the microsecond part of the timeout value. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_SNDTIMEO</b></td> <td> Reports the timeout value specifying the amount of time that an output function blocks because flow control prevents data from being sent. </td> <td> array. The array will contain two keys: sec which is the seconds part on the timeout value and usec which is the microsecond part of the timeout value. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>SO_SNDLOWAT</b></td> <td> Reports the minimum number of bytes to process for <i>socket</i> output operations. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>TCP_NODELAY</b></td> <td> Reports whether the Nagle TCP algorithm is disabled. </td> <td> int </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MCAST_JOIN_GROUP</b></td> <td> Joins a multicast group. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> array with keys \"group\", specifying a string with an IPv4 or IPv6 multicast address and \"interface\", specifying either an interface number (type int) or a string with the interface name, like \"eth0\". 0 can be specified to indicate the interface should be selected using routing rules. (can only be used in <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MCAST_LEAVE_GROUP</b></td> <td> Leaves a multicast group. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> array. See <b>MCAST_JOIN_GROUP</b> for more information. (can only be used in <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MCAST_BLOCK_SOURCE</b></td> <td> Blocks packets arriving from a specific source to a specific multicast group, which must have been previously joined. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> array with the same keys as <b>MCAST_JOIN_GROUP</b>, plus one extra key, source, which maps to a string specifying an IPv4 or IPv6 address of the source to be blocked. (can only be used in <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MCAST_UNBLOCK_SOURCE</b></td> <td> Unblocks (start receiving again) packets arriving from a specific source address to a specific multicast group, which must have been previously joined. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> array with the same format as <b>MCAST_BLOCK_SOURCE</b>. (can only be used in <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MCAST_JOIN_SOURCE_GROUP</b></td> <td> Receive packets destined to a specific multicast group whose source address matches a specific value. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> array with the same format as <b>MCAST_BLOCK_SOURCE</b>. (can only be used in <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MCAST_LEAVE_SOURCE_GROUP</b></td> <td> Stop receiving packets destined to a specific multicast group whose soure address matches a specific value. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> array with the same format as <b>MCAST_BLOCK_SOURCE</b>. (can only be used in <b>socket_set_option</b>) </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>IP_MULTICAST_IF</b></td> <td> The outgoing interface for IPv4 multicast packets. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> Either int specifying the interface number or a string with an interface name, like eth0. The value 0 can be used to indicate the routing table is to used in the interface selection. The function <b>socket_get_option</b> returns an interface index. Note that, unlike the C API, this option does NOT take an IP address. This eliminates the interface difference between <b>IP_MULTICAST_IF</b> and <b>IPV6_MULTICAST_IF</b>. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>IPV6_MULTICAST_IF</b></td> <td> The outgoing interface for IPv6 multicast packets. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> The same as <b>IP_MULTICAST_IF</b>. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>IP_MULTICAST_LOOP</b></td> <td> The multicast loopback policy for IPv4 packets, which determines whether multicast packets sent by this socket also reach receivers in the same host that have joined the same multicast group on the outgoing interface used by this socket. This is the case by default. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> int (either 0 or 1). For <b>socket_set_option</b> any value will be accepted and will be converted to a boolean following the usual PHP rules. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>IPV6_MULTICAST_LOOP</b></td> <td> Analogous to <b>IP_MULTICAST_LOOP</b>, but for IPv6. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> int. See <b>IP_MULTICAST_LOOP</b>. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>IP_MULTICAST_TTL</b></td> <td> The time-to-live of outgoing IPv4 multicast packets. This should be a value between 0 (don't leave the interface) and 255. The default value is 1 (only the local network is reached). (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> int between 0 and 255. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>IPV6_MULTICAST_HOPS</b></td> <td> Analogous to <b>IP_MULTICAST_TTL</b>, but for IPv6 packets. The value -1 is also accepted, meaning the route default should be used. (added in PHP 5.4) </td> <td> int between -1 and 255. </td> </tr> </table> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","description":"<table>"}],"return_type":"array|int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_get_status","fqn":"socket_get_status","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":40481,"end":40498}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array","phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Alias: {@see stream_get_meta_data} Retrieves header/meta data from streams/file pointers The stream can be any stream created by fopen, fsockopen and pfsockopen. </p> <p> timed_out (bool) - true if the stream timed out while waiting for data on the last call to fread or fgets. </p> <p> blocked (bool) - true if the stream is in blocking IO mode. See stream_set_blocking. </p> <p> eof (bool) - true if the stream has reached end-of-file. Note that for socket streams this member can be true even when unread_bytes is non-zero. To determine if there is more data to be read, use feof instead of reading this item. </p> <p> unread_bytes (int) - the number of bytes currently contained in the PHP's own internal buffer. </p> You shouldn't use this value in a script. <p> stream_type (string) - a label describing the underlying implementation of the stream. </p> <p> wrapper_type (string) - a label describing the protocol wrapper implementation layered over the stream. See for more information about wrappers. </p> <p> wrapper_data (mixed) - wrapper specific data attached to this stream. See for more information about wrappers and their wrapper data. </p> <p> filters (array) - and array containing the names of any filters that have been stacked onto this stream. Documentation on filters can be found in the Filters appendix. </p> <p> mode (string) - the type of access required for this stream (see Table 1 of the fopen() reference) </p> <p> seekable (bool) - whether the current stream can be seeked. </p> <p> uri (string) - the URI/filename associated with this stream. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_getopt","fqn":"socket_getopt","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":43633,"end":43646}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|int|false","phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"Alias of {@see socket_get_option} /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","description":null},{"name":"level","declared_type":"int","description":null},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","description":null}],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_getpeername","fqn":"socket_getpeername","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":19596,"end":19614}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"port","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Queries the remote side of the given socket which may either result in host/port or in a Unix filesystem path, dependent on its type A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> If the given socket is of type <b>AF_INET</b> or <b>AF_INET6</b>, <b>socket_getpeername</b> will return the peers (remote) IP address in appropriate notation (e.g. 127.0.0.1 or fe80::1) in the <i>address</i> parameter and, if the optional <i>port</i> parameter is present, also the associated port. </p> <p> If the given socket is of type <b>AF_UNIX</b>, <b>socket_getpeername</b> will return the Unix filesystem path (e.g. /var/run/daemon.sock) in the <i>address</i> parameter. </p> If given, this will hold the port associated to <i>address</i>. </p> <b>FALSE</b> if the socket type is not any of <b>AF_INET</b>, <b>AF_INET6</b>, or <b>AF_UNIX</b>, in which case the last socket error code is not updated. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_getsockname","fqn":"socket_getsockname","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":18226,"end":18244}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"port","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Queries the local side of the given socket which may either result in host/port or in a Unix filesystem path, dependent on its type A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> If the given socket is of type <b>AF_INET</b> or <b>AF_INET6</b>, <b>socket_getsockname</b> will return the local IP address in appropriate notation (e.g. 127.0.0.1 or fe80::1) in the <i>address</i> parameter and, if the optional <i>port</i> parameter is present, also the associated port. </p> <p> If the given socket is of type <b>AF_UNIX</b>, <b>socket_getsockname</b> will return the Unix filesystem path (e.g. /var/run/daemon.sock) in the <i>address</i> parameter. </p> If provided, this will hold the associated port. </p> <b>FALSE</b> if the socket type is not any of <b>AF_INET</b>, <b>AF_INET6</b>, or <b>AF_UNIX</b>, in which case the last socket error code is not updated. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_import_stream","fqn":"socket_import_stream","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":43117,"end":43137}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"Socket|false","phpdoc_return_type":"resource|Socket|false|null"},"documentation":{"description":"Import a stream The stream resource to import. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"resource|Socket|false|null","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_last_error","fqn":"socket_last_error","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":42433,"end":42450}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"?Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the last error on the socket A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_listen","fqn":"socket_listen","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":14310,"end":14323}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"backlog","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Listens for a connection on a socket A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b>. </p> A maximum of <i>backlog</i> incoming connections will be queued for processing. If a connection request arrives with the queue full the client may receive an error with an indication of ECONNREFUSED, or, if the underlying protocol supports retransmission, the request may be ignored so that retries may succeed. </p> <p> The maximum number passed to the <i>backlog</i> parameter highly depends on the underlying platform. On Linux, it is silently truncated to <b>SOMAXCONN</b>. On win32, if passed <b>SOMAXCONN</b>, the underlying service provider responsible for the socket will set the backlog to a maximum reasonable value. There is no standard provision to find out the actual backlog value on this platform. </p> <b>socket_last_error</b>. This code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"backlog","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_read","fqn":"socket_read","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":16870,"end":16881}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Reads a maximum of length bytes from a socket A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> The maximum number of bytes read is specified by the <i>length</i> parameter. Otherwise you can use <b>&#92;r</b>, <b>&#92;n</b>, or <b>&#92;0</b> to end reading (depending on the <i>type</i> parameter, see below). </p> Optional <i>type</i> parameter is a named constant: <b>PHP_BINARY_READ</b> (Default) - use the system recv() function. Safe for reading binary data. or <b>FALSE</b> on error (including if the remote host has closed the connection). The error code can be retrieved with <b>socket_last_error</b>. This code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual representation of the error. </p> <p> <b>socket_read</b> returns a zero length string (\"\") when there is no more data to read.</p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_recv","fqn":"socket_recv","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":24130,"end":24141}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Receives data from a connected socket The <i>socket</i> must be a socket resource previously created by socket_create(). </p> The data received will be fetched to the variable specified with <i>buf</i>. If an error occurs, if the connection is reset, or if no data is available, <i>buf</i> will be set to <b>NULL</b>. </p> Up to <i>len</i> bytes will be fetched from remote host. </p> The value of <i>flags</i> can be any combination of the following flags, joined with the binary OR (|) operator. </p> <table> Possible values for <i>flags</i> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Flag</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_OOB</b></td> <td> Process out-of-band data. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_PEEK</b></td> <td> Receive data from the beginning of the receive queue without removing it from the queue. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_WAITALL</b></td> <td> Block until at least <i>len</i> are received. However, if a signal is caught or the remote host disconnects, the function may return less data. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_DONTWAIT</b></td> <td> With this flag set, the function returns even if it would normally have blocked. </td> </tr> </table> or <b>FALSE</b> if there was an error. The actual error code can be retrieved by calling <b>socket_last_error</b>. This error code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_recvfrom","fqn":"socket_recvfrom","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":28426,"end":28441}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"port","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Receives data from a socket whether or not it is connection-oriented The <i>socket</i> must be a socket resource previously created by socket_create(). </p> The data received will be fetched to the variable specified with <i>buf</i>. </p> Up to <i>len</i> bytes will be fetched from remote host. </p> The value of <i>flags</i> can be any combination of the following flags, joined with the binary OR (|) operator. </p> <table> Possible values for <i>flags</i> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Flag</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_OOB</b></td> <td> Process out-of-band data. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_PEEK</b></td> <td> Receive data from the beginning of the receive queue without removing it from the queue. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_WAITALL</b></td> <td> Block until at least <i>len</i> are received. However, if a signal is caught or the remote host disconnects, the function may return less data. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_DONTWAIT</b></td> <td> With this flag set, the function returns even if it would normally have blocked. </td> </tr> </table> If the socket is of the type <b>AF_UNIX</b> type, <i>name</i> is the path to the file. Else, for unconnected sockets, <i>name</i> is the IP address of, the remote host, or <b>NULL</b> if the socket is connection-oriented. </p> This argument only applies to <b>AF_INET</b> and <b>AF_INET6</b> sockets, and specifies the remote port from which the data is received. If the socket is connection-oriented, <i>port</i> will be <b>NULL</b>. </p> or <b>FALSE</b> if there was an error. The actual error code can be retrieved by calling <b>socket_last_error</b>. This error code may be passed to <b>socket_strerror</b> to get a textual explanation of the error. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_recvmsg","fqn":"socket_recvmsg","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":28746,"end":28760}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"message","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Read a message /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":null}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_select","fqn":"socket_select","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":4745,"end":4758}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"read","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"write","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"except","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"microseconds","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Runs the select() system call on the given arrays of sockets with a specified timeout The sockets listed in the <i>read</i> array will be watched to see if characters become available for reading (more precisely, to see if a read will not block - in particular, a socket resource is also ready on end-of-file, in which case a <b>socket_read</b> will return a zero length string). </p> The sockets listed in the <i>write</i> array will be watched to see if a write will not block. </p> The sockets listed in the <i>except</i> array will be watched for exceptions. </p> The <i>tv_sec</i> and <i>tv_usec</i> together form the timeout parameter. The timeout is an upper bound on the amount of time elapsed before <b>socket_select</b> return. <i>tv_sec</i> may be zero , causing <b>socket_select</b> to return immediately. This is useful for polling. If <i>tv_sec</i> is <b>NULL</b> (no timeout), <b>socket_select</b> can block indefinitely. </p> socket resources contained in the modified arrays, which may be zero if the timeout expires before anything interesting happens. On error <b>FALSE</b> is returned. The error code can be retrieved with <b>socket_last_error</b>. </p> <p> Be sure to use the === operator when checking for an error. Since the <b>socket_select</b> may return 0 the comparison with == would evaluate to <b>TRUE</b>: Understanding <b>socket_select</b>'s result <code> $e = NULL; if (false === socket_select($r, $w, $e, 0)) { echo \"socket_select() failed, reason: \" . socket_strerror(socket_last_error()) . \"\\n\"; } </code> /","params":[{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"microseconds","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_send","fqn":"socket_send","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":25588,"end":25599}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Sends data to a connected socket A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> A buffer containing the data that will be sent to the remote host. </p> The number of bytes that will be sent to the remote host from <i>buf</i>. </p> The value of <i>flags</i> can be any combination of the following flags, joined with the binary OR (|) operator. <table> Possible values for <i>flags</i> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_OOB</b></td> <td> Send OOB (out-of-band) data. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_EOR</b></td> <td> Indicate a record mark. The sent data completes the record. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_EOF</b></td> <td> Close the sender side of the socket and include an appropriate notification of this at the end of the sent data. The sent data completes the transaction. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_DONTROUTE</b></td> <td> Bypass routing, use direct interface. </td> </tr> </table> </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_sendmsg","fqn":"socket_sendmsg","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":25910,"end":25924}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"message","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;=5.5.0)<br/> Send a message /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":null},{"name":"message","declared_type":"array","description":null},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":null}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_sendto","fqn":"socket_sendto","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":30526,"end":30539}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"port","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Sends a message to a socket, whether it is connected or not A valid socket resource created using <b>socket_create</b>. </p> The sent data will be taken from buffer <i>buf</i>. </p> <i>len</i> bytes from <i>buf</i> will be sent. </p> The value of <i>flags</i> can be any combination of the following flags, joined with the binary OR (|) operator. <table> Possible values for <i>flags</i> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_OOB</b></td> <td> Send OOB (out-of-band) data. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_EOR</b></td> <td> Indicate a record mark. The sent data completes the record. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_EOF</b></td> <td> Close the sender side of the socket and include an appropriate notification of this at the end of the sent data. The sent data completes the transaction. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>MSG_DONTROUTE</b></td> <td> Bypass routing, use direct interface. </td> </tr> </table> </p> IP address of the remote host. </p> <i>port</i> is the remote port number at which the data will be sent. </p> remote host, or <b>FALSE</b> if an error occurred. /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"port","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_set_block","fqn":"socket_set_block","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":13007,"end":13023}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Sets blocking mode on a socket resource A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_set_blocking","fqn":"socket_set_blocking","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":30283,"end":30302}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"enable","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Alias: {@see stream_set_blocking} The stream. </p> If mode is FALSE, the given stream will be switched to non-blocking mode, and if TRUE, it will be switched to blocking mode. This affects calls like fgets and fread that read from the stream. In non-blocking mode an fgets call will always return right away while in blocking mode it will wait for data to become available on the stream. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"enable","declared_type":"bool","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_set_nonblock","fqn":"socket_set_nonblock","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":12634,"end":12653}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Sets nonblocking mode for file descriptor fd A valid socket resource created with <b>socket_create</b> or <b>socket_accept</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource|Socket","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"socket_set_option","fqn":"socket_set_option","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"sockets","location":{"file":"sockets/sockets.php","range":{"start":41256,"end":41273}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"Socket","phpdoc_type":"resource|Socket","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"level","d