on Case sensitive regular expression. </p> <p> If you want to split on any of the characters which are considered special by regular expressions, you'll need to escape them first. If you think <b>split</b> (or any other regex function, for that matter) is doing something weird, please read the file regex.7, included in the regex/ subdirectory of the PHP distribution. It's in manpage format, so you'll want to do something along the lines of man /usr/local/src/regex/regex.7 in order to read it. </p> The input string. </p> If <i>limit</i> is set, the returned array will contain a maximum of <i>limit</i> elements with the last element containing the whole rest of <i>string</i>. </p> <i>string</i> formed by splitting it on boundaries formed by the case-sensitive regular expression <i>pattern</i>. </p> <p> If there are n occurrences of <i>pattern</i>, the returned array will contain n+1 items. For example, if there is no occurrence of <i>pattern</i>, an array with only one element will be returned. Of course, this is also true if <i>string</i> is empty. If an error occurs, <b>split</b> returns <b>FALSE</b>. /","params":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"limit","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"spliti","fqn":"spliti","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"regex","location":{"file":"regex/ereg.php","range":{"start":7677,"end":7683}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"limit","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Split string into array by regular expression case insensitive Case insensitive regular expression. </p> <p> If you want to split on any of the characters which are considered special by regular expressions, you'll need to escape them first. If you think <b>spliti</b> (or any other regex function, for that matter) is doing something weird, please read the file regex.7, included in the regex/ subdirectory of the PHP distribution. It's in manpage format, so you'll want to do something along the lines of man /usr/local/src/regex/regex.7 in order to read it. </p> The input string. </p> If <i>limit</i> is set, the returned array will contain a maximum of <i>limit</i> elements with the last element containing the whole rest of <i>string</i>. </p> <i>string</i> formed by splitting it on boundaries formed by the case insensitive regular expression <i>pattern</i>. </p> <p> If there are n occurrences of <i>pattern</i>, the returned array will contain n+1 items. For example, if there is no occurrence of <i>pattern</i>, an array with only one element will be returned. Of course, this is also true if <i>string</i> is empty. If an error occurs, <b>spliti</b> returns <b>FALSE</b>. /","params":[{"name":"pattern","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"limit","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sprintf","fqn":"sprintf","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_2.php","range":{"start":11777,"end":11784}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"format","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"values","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"values","declared_type":"mixed","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":true,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Return a formatted string The format string is composed of zero or more directives: ordinary characters (excluding %) that are copied directly to the result, and conversion specifications, each of which results in fetching its own parameter. This applies to both sprintf and printf. </p> <p> Each conversion specification consists of a percent sign (%), followed by one or more of these elements, in order: An optional sign specifier that forces a sign (- or +) to be used on a number. By default, only the - sign is used on a number if it's negative. This specifier forces positive numbers to have the + sign attached as well, and was added in PHP 4.3.0.</p> </p> format. Prior to PHP 8.0.0, a E_WARNING was emitted instead. As of PHP 8.0.0, a ValueError is thrown if [width] is less than zero or bigger than PHP_INT_MAX. Prior to PHP 8.0.0, a E_WARNING was emitted instead. As of PHP 8.0.0, a ValueError is thrown if [precision] is less than zero or bigger than PHP_INT_MAX. Prior to PHP 8.0.0, a E_WARNING was emitted instead. are given than required. Prior to PHP 8.0.0, false was returned and a E_WARNING emitted instead. /","params":[{"name":"format","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError","\\ArgumentCountError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sql_regcase","fqn":"sql_regcase","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"regex","location":{"file":"regex/ereg.php","range":{"start":8271,"end":8282}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Make regular expression for case insensitive match The input string. </p> <i>string</i>, ignoring case. This expression is <i>string</i> with each alphabetic character converted to a bracket expression; this bracket expression contains that character's uppercase and lowercase form. Other characters remain unchanged. /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqlite_array_query","fqn":"sqlite_array_query","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"SQLite","location":{"file":"SQLite/SQLite.php","range":{"start":32599,"end":32617}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"dbhandle","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"query","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"result_type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"decode_binary","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL sqlite &gt;= 1.0.0)<br/> Execute a query against a given database and returns an array The query to be executed. </p> <p> Data inside the query should be properly escaped. </p> The SQLite Database resource; returned from {@see sqlite_open()} when used procedurally.  This parameter is not required when using the object-oriented method. </p> parameter accepts a constant and determines how the returned array will be indexed. Using <b>SQLITE_ASSOC</b> will return only associative indices (named fields) while <b>SQLITE_NUM</b> will return only numerical indices (ordinal field numbers). <b>SQLITE_BOTH</b> will return both associative and numerical indices. <b>SQLITE_BOTH</b> is the default for this function.</p> parameter is set to <b>TRUE</b> (the default), PHP will decode the binary encoding it applied to the data if it was encoded using the {@link sqlite_escape_string()}.  You should normally leave this value at its default, unless you are interoperating with databases created by other sqlite capable applications.</p> <p>The column names returned by <b>SQLITE_ASSOC</b> and <b>SQLITE_BOTH</b> will be case-folded according to the value of the {@link php.net/en/sqlite.configuration.php#ini.sqlite.assoc-case sqlite.assoc_case} configuration option.</p> /","params":[{"name":"query","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"dbhandle","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"result_type","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>The optional <i>result_type</i>"},{"name":"decode_binary","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>When the <i>decode_binary</i>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqlite_busy_timeout","fqn":"sqlite_busy_timeout","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"SQLite","location":{"file":"SQLite/SQLite.php","range":{"start":46529,"end":46548}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"dbhandle","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"milliseconds","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL sqlite &gt;= 1.0.0)<br/> Set busy timeout duration, or disable busy handlers {@see sqlite_open()} when used procedurally. This parameter is not required when using the object-oriented method.</p> The number of milliseconds. When set to 0, busy handlers will be disabled and SQLite will return immediately with a <b>SQLITE_BUSY</b> status code if another process/thread has the database locked for an update. </p> <p> PHP sets the default busy timeout to be 60 seconds when the database is opened. </p> <p> There are one thousand (1000) milliseconds in one second. </p> /","params":[{"name":"dbhandle","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>The SQLite Database resource; returned from"},{"name":"milliseconds","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqlite_changes","fqn":"sqlite_changes","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"SQLite","location":{"file":"SQLite/SQLite.php","range":{"start":39643,"end":39657}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"db","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL sqlite &gt;= 1.0.0)<br/> Returns the number of rows that were changed by the most recent SQL statement /","params":[{"name":"db","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqlite_close","fqn":"sqlite_close","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"SQLite","location":{"file":"SQLite/SQLite.php","range":{"start":27637,"end":27649}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"dbhandle","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL sqlite &gt;= 1.0.0)<br/> Closes an open SQLite database The SQLite Database resource; returned from sqlite_open when used procedurally. </p> /","params":[{"name":"dbhandle","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqlite_column","fqn":"sqlite_column","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"SQLite","location":{"file":"SQLite/SQLite.php","range":{"start":38820,"end":38833}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"result","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"index_or_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"decode_binary","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"mixed"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5, PECL sqlite &gt;= 1.0.0)<br/> Fetches a column from the current row of a result set The column index or name to fetch. </p> parameter is set to <b>TRUE</b> (the default), PHP will decode the binary encoding it applied to the data if it was encoded using the {@see sqlite_escape_string()}.  You should normally leave this value at its default, unless you are interoperating with databases created by other sqlite capable applications.</p> /","params":[{"name":"result","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>The SQLite result resource. This parameter is not required when using the object-oriented method.</p>"},{"name":"index_or_name","declared_type":"mixed","description":"<p>"},{"name":"decode_binary","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>When the <b>decode_binary</b>"}],"return_type":"mixed","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqlite_create_aggregate","fqn":"sqlite_create_aggregate","kind":"Func