ll,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_resolve_include_path","fqn":"stream_resolve_include_path","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":34899,"end":34926}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Resolve filename against the include path according to the same rules as fopen()/include(). /","params":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"The filename to resolve."}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_select","fqn":"stream_select","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":3260,"end":3273}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"read","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"write","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"except","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"microseconds","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Runs the equivalent of the select() system call on the given arrays of streams with a timeout specified by tv_sec and tv_usec The streams listed in the read array will be watched to see if characters become available for reading (more precisely, to see if a read will not block - in particular, a stream resource is also ready on end-of-file, in which case an fread will return a zero length string). </p> The streams listed in the write array will be watched to see if a write will not block. </p> The streams listed in the except array will be watched for high priority exceptional (\"out-of-band\") data arriving. </p> <p> When stream_select returns, the arrays read, write and except are modified to indicate which stream resource(s) actually changed status. </p> You do not need to pass every array to stream_select. You can leave it out and use an empty array or null instead. Also do not forget that those arrays are passed by reference and will be modified after stream_select returns. The tv_sec and tv_usec together form the timeout parameter, tv_sec specifies the number of seconds while tv_usec the number of microseconds. The timeout is an upper bound on the amount of time that stream_select will wait before it returns. If tv_sec and tv_usec are both set to 0, stream_select will not wait for data - instead it will return immediately, indicating the current status of the streams. </p> <p> If tv_sec is null stream_select can block indefinitely, returning only when an event on one of the watched streams occurs (or if a signal interrupts the system call). </p> <p> Using a timeout value of 0 allows you to instantaneously poll the status of the streams, however, it is NOT a good idea to use a 0 timeout value in a loop as it will cause your script to consume too much CPU time. </p> <p> It is much better to specify a timeout value of a few seconds, although if you need to be checking and running other code concurrently, using a timeout value of at least 200000 microseconds will help reduce the CPU usage of your script. </p> <p> Remember that the timeout value is the maximum time that will elapse; stream_select will return as soon as the requested streams are ready for use. </p> See tv_sec description. </p> stream resources contained in the modified arrays, which may be zero if the timeout expires before anything interesting happens. On error false is returned and a warning raised (this can happen if the system call is interrupted by an incoming signal). /","params":[{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"int|null","description":"<p>"},{"name":"microseconds","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_set_blocking","fqn":"stream_set_blocking","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":29602,"end":29621}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"enable","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Set blocking/non-blocking mode on a stream The stream. </p> If mode is FALSE, the given stream will be switched to non-blocking mode, and if TRUE, it will be switched to blocking mode. This affects calls like fgets and fread that read from the stream. In non-blocking mode an fgets call will always return right away while in blocking mode it will wait for data to become available on the stream. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"enable","declared_type":"bool","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_set_chunk_size","fqn":"stream_set_chunk_size","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_8.php","range":{"start":4309,"end":4330}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"size","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Set the stream chunk size. Will return <b>FALSE</b> if chunk_size is less than 1 or greater than <b>PHP_INT_MAX</b>. /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"The target stream."},{"name":"size","declared_type":"int","description":"The desired new chunk size."}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_set_read_buffer","fqn":"stream_set_read_buffer","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":27210,"end":27232}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"size","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Sets read file buffering on the given stream The file pointer. </p> The number of bytes to buffer. If buffer is 0 then write operations are unbuffered. This ensures that all writes with fwrite are completed before other processes are allowed to write to that output stream. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"size","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_set_timeout","fqn":"stream_set_timeout","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":37560,"end":37578}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"microseconds","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"microseconds","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Set timeout period on a stream The target stream. </p> The seconds part of the timeout to be set. </p> The microseconds part of the timeout to be set. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"microseconds","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_set_write_buffer","fqn":"stream_set_write_buffer","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":26607,"end":26630}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"size","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Sets write file buffering on the given stream The file pointer. </p> The number of bytes to buffer. If buffer is 0 then write operations are unbuffered. This ensures that all writes with fwrite are completed before other processes are allowed to write to that output stream. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"size","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_accept","fqn":"stream_socket_accept","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":14789,"end":14809}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"peer_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Accept a connection on a socket created by {@see stream_socket_server} Override the default socket accept timeout. Time should be given in seconds. </p> Will be set to the name (address) of the client which connected, if included and available from the selected transport. </p> <p> Can also be determined later using stream_socket_get_name. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource","description":null},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"float|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_client","fqn":"stream_socket_client","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":11992,"end":12012}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"error_code","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"error_message","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"?float","phpdoc_type":"float|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Open Internet or Unix domain socket connection Address to the socket to connect to. </p> Will be set to the system level error number if connection fails. </p> Will be set to the system level error message if the connection fails. </p> Number of seconds until the connect() system call should timeout. This parameter only applies when not making asynchronous connection attempts. <p> To set a timeout for reading/writing data over the socket, use the stream_set_timeout, as the timeout only applies while making connecting the socket. </p> </p> Bitmask field which may be set to any combination of connection flags. Currently the select of connection flags is limited to STREAM_CLIENT_CONNECT (default), STREAM_CLIENT_ASYNC_CONNECT and STREAM_CLIENT_PERSISTENT. </p> A valid context resource created with stream_context_create. </p> be used together with the other file functions (such as fgets, fgetss, fwrite, fclose, and feof), false on failure. /","params":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"timeout","declared_type":"float|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"context","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_enable_crypto","fqn":"stream_socket_enable_crypto","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":18079,"end":18106}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"enable","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"crypto_method","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"session_stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool|int"},"documentation":{"description":"Turns encryption on/off on an already connected socket The stream resource. </p> Enable/disable cryptography on the stream. </p> Setup encryption on the stream. Valid methods are:<br> STREAM_CRYPTO_METHOD_SSLv2_CLIENT</p> Seed the stream with settings from session_stream. </p> 0 if there isn't enough data and you should try again (only for non-blocking sockets). /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"enable","declared_type":"bool","description":"<p>"},{"name":"crypto_method","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"session_stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool|int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_get_crypto_status","fqn":"stream_socket_get_crypto_status","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/streams.php","range":{"start":3541,"end":3572}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the current crypto status of a stream /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":null}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_get_name","fqn":"stream_socket_get_name","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":15299,"end":15321}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"remote","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Retrieve the name of the local or remote sockets The socket to get the name of. </p> If set to true the remote socket name will be returned, if set to false the local socket name will be returned. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"remote","declared_type":"bool","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_pair","fqn":"stream_socket_pair","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":19522,"end":19540}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Creates a pair of connected, indistinguishable socket streams The protocol family to be used: STREAM_PF_INET, STREAM_PF_INET6 or STREAM_PF_UNIX </p> The type of communication to be used: STREAM_SOCK_DGRAM, STREAM_SOCK_RAW, STREAM_SOCK_RDM, STREAM_SOCK_SEQPACKET or STREAM_SOCK_STREAM </p> The protocol to be used: STREAM_IPPROTO_ICMP, STREAM_IPPROTO_IP, STREAM_IPPROTO_RAW, STREAM_IPPROTO_TCP or STREAM_IPPROTO_UDP </p> false on failure. /","params":[{"name":"domain","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"type","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_recvfrom","fqn":"stream_socket_recvfrom","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":16332,"end":16354}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Receives data from a socket, connected or not The remote socket. </p> The number of bytes to receive from the socket. </p> The value of flags can be any combination of the following: <table> Possible values for flags <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>STREAM_OOB</td> <td> Process OOB (out-of-band) data. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>STREAM_PEEK</td> <td> Retrieve data from the socket, but do not consume the buffer. Subsequent calls to fread or stream_socket_recvfrom will see the same data. </td> </tr> </table> </p> If address is provided it will be populated with the address of the remote socket. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"length","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_sendto","fqn":"stream_socket_sendto","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":17259,"end":17279}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int|false","phpdoc_return_type":"int|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Sends a message to a socket, whether it is connected or not The socket to send data to. </p> The data to be sent. </p> The value of flags can be any combination of the following: <table> possible values for flags <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>STREAM_OOB</td> <td> Process OOB (out-of-band) data. </td> </tr> </table> </p> The address specified when the socket stream was created will be used unless an alternate address is specified in address. </p> <p> If specified, it must be in dotted quad (or [ipv6]) format. </p> /","params":[{"name":"socket","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"int|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_server","fqn":"stream_socket_server","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":13952,"end":13972}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"error_code","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"error_message","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"context","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Create an Internet or Unix domain server socket The type of socket created is determined by the transport specified using standard URL formatting: transport://target. </p> <p> For Internet Domain sockets (AF_INET) such as TCP and UDP, the target portion of the remote_socket parameter should consist of a hostname or IP address followed by a colon and a port number. For Unix domain sockets, the target portion should point to the socket file on the filesystem. </p> <p> Depending on the environment, Unix domain sockets may not be available. A list of available transports can be retrieved using stream_get_transports. See for a list of built-in transports. </p> If the optional errno and errstr arguments are present they will be set to indicate the actual system level error that occurred in the system-level socket(), bind(), and listen() calls. If the value returned in errno is 0 and the function returned false, it is an indication that the error occurred before the bind() call. This is most likely due to a problem initializing the socket. Note that the errno and errstr arguments will always be passed by reference. </p> See errno description. </p> A bitmask field which may be set to any combination of socket creation flags. </p> <p> For UDP sockets, you must use STREAM_SERVER_BIND as the flags parameter. </p> </p> /","params":[{"name":"address","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"context","declared_type":"resource","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_socket_shutdown","fqn":"stream_socket_shutdown","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":18735,"end":18757}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Shutdown a full-duplex connection An open stream (opened with stream_socket_client, for example) </p> One of the following constants: STREAM_SHUT_RD (disable further receptions), STREAM_SHUT_WR (disable further transmissions) or STREAM_SHUT_RDWR (disable further receptions and transmissions). </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_supports_lock","fqn":"stream_supports_lock","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":21102,"end":21122}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Tells whether the stream supports locking. The stream to check. </p> /","params":[{"name":"stream","declared_type":"resource","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_wrapper_register","fqn":"stream_wrapper_register","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":33739,"end":33762}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"class","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Register a URL wrapper implemented as a PHP class The wrapper name to be registered. </p> The classname which implements the protocol. </p> Should be set to STREAM_IS_URL if protocol is a URL protocol. Default is 0, local stream. </p> <p> stream_wrapper_register will return false if the protocol already has a handler. </p> /","params":[{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"class","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_wrapper_restore","fqn":"stream_wrapper_restore","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":35463,"end":35485}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Restores a previously unregistered built-in wrapper </p> /","params":[{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stream_wrapper_unregister","fqn":"stream_wrapper_unregister","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_6.php","range":{"start":35174,"end":35199}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Unregister a URL wrapper </p> /","params":[{"name":"protocol","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"strftime","fqn":"strftime","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"date","location":{"file":"date/date.php","range":{"start":22903,"end":22911}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"format","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"?int","phpdoc_type":"int|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Format a local time/date according to locale settings The following characters are recognized in the format parameter string <table> <tr valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\" bgcolor=\"silver\"> <th>format</th> <th>Description</th> <th>Example returned values</th> <th> Day</th> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%a</td> <td>An abbreviated textual representation of the day</td> <td>Sun through Sat</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%A</td> <td>A full textual representation of the day</td> <td>Sunday through Saturday</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%d</td> <td>Two-digit day of the month (with leading zeros)</td> <td>01 to 31</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%e</td> <td>Day of the month, with a space preceding single digits</td> <td> 1 to 31</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%j</td> <td>Day of the year, 3 digits with leading zeros</td> <td>001 to 366</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%u</td> <td>ISO-8601 numeric representation of the day of the week</td> <td>1 (for Monday) though 7 (for Sunday)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%w</td> <td>Numeric representation of the day of the week</td> <td>0 (for Sunday) through 6 (for Saturday)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <th colspan=\"3\" bgcolor=\"silver\">Week</th> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%U</td> <td>Week number of the given year, starting with the first Sunday as the first week</td> <td>13 (for the 13th full week of the year)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%V</td> <td>ISO-8601:1988 week number of the given year, starting with the first week of the year with at least 4 weekdays, with Monday being the start of the week</td> <td>01 through 53 (where 53 accounts for an overlapping week)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%W</td> <td>A numeric representation of the week of the year, starting with the first Monday as the first week</td> <td>46 (for the 46th week of the year beginning with a Monday)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <th colspan=\"3\" bgcolor=\"silver\">Month</th> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%b</td> <td>Abbreviated month name, based on the locale</td> <td>Jan through Dec</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%B</td> <td>Full month name, based on the locale</td> <td>January through December</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%h</td> <td>Abbreviated month name, based on the locale (an alias of %b)</td> <td>Jan through Dec</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%m</td> <td>Two digit representation of the month</td> <td>01 (for January) through 12 (for December)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <th colspan=\"3\" bgcolor=\"silver\">Year</th> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%C</td> <td>Two digit representation of the century (year divided by 100, truncated to an integer)</td> <td>19 for the 20th Century</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%g</td> <td>Two digit representation of the year going by ISO-8601:1988 standards (see %V)</td> <td>Example: 09 for the week of January 6, 2009</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%G</td> <td>The full four-digit version of %g</td> <td>Example: 2008 for the week of January 3, 2009</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%y</td> <td>Two digit representation of the year</td> <td>Example: 09 for 2009, 79 for 1979</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%Y</td> <td>Four digit representation for the year</td> <td>Example: 2038</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <th colspan=\"3\" bgcolor=\"silver\">Time</th> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%H</td> <td>Two digit representation of the hour in 24-hour format</td> <td>00 through 23</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%I</td> <td>Two digit representation of the hour in 12-hour format</td> <td>01 through 12</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%l (lower-case 'L')</td> <td>Hour in 12-hour format, with a space preceding single digits</td> <td> 1 through 12</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%M</td> <td>Two digit representation of the minute</td> <td>00 through 59</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%p</td> <td>UPPER-CASE 'AM' or 'PM' based on the given time</td> <td>Example: AM for 00:31, PM for 22:23</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%P</td> <td>lower-case 'am' or 'pm' based on the given time</td> <td>Example: am for 00:31, pm for 22:23</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%r</td> <td>Same as \"%I:%M:%S %p\"</td> <td>Example: 09:34:17 PM for 21:34:17</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%R</td> <td>Same as \"%H:%M\"</td> <td>Example: 00:35 for 12:35 AM, 16:44 for 4:44 PM</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%S</td> <td>Two digit representation of the second</td> <td>00 through 59</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%T</td> <td>Same as \"%H:%M:%S\"</td> <td>Example: 21:34:17 for 09:34:17 PM</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%X</td> <td>Preferred time representation based on locale, without the date</td> <td>Example: 03:59:16 or 15:59:16</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%z</td> <td>Either the time zone offset from UTC or the abbreviation (depends on operating system)</td> <td>Example: -0500 or EST for Eastern Time</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%Z</td> <td>The time zone offset/abbreviation option NOT given by %z (depends on operating system)</td> <td>Example: -0500 or EST for Eastern Time</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <th colspan=\"3\" bgcolor=\"silver\">Time and Date Stamps</th> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%c</td> <td>Preferred date and time stamp based on local</td> <td>Example: Tue Feb 5 00:45:10 2009 for February 4, 2009 at 12:45:10 AM</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%D</td> <td>Same as \"%m/%d/%y\"</td> <td>Example: 02/05/09 for February 5, 2009</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%F</td> <td>Same as \"%Y-%m-%d\" (commonly used in database datestamps)</td> <td>Example: 2009-02-05 for February 5, 2009</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%s</td> <td>Unix Epoch Time timestamp (same as the time function)</td> <td>Example: 305815200 for September 10, 1979 08:40:00 AM</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%x</td> <td>Preferred date representation based on locale, without the time</td> <td>Example: 02/05/09 for February 5, 2009</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <th colspan=\"3\" bgcolor=\"silver\">Miscellaneous</th> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%n</td> <td>A newline character (\"\\n\")</td> <td>---</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%t</td> <td>A Tab character (\"\\t\")</td> <td>---</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>%%</td> <td>A literal percentage character (\"%\")</td> <td>---</td> </tr> </table> <p> Maximum length of this parameter is 1023 characters. </p> Contrary to ISO-9899:1999, Sun Solaris starts with Sunday as 1. As a result, %u may not function as described in this manual. Unix timestamp that defaults to the current local time if a timestamp is not given.. using the given timestamp or the current local time if no timestamp is given. Month and weekday names and other language-dependent strings respect the current locale set with setlocale. /","params":[{"name":"format","declared_type":"string","description":null},{"name":"timestamp","declared_type":"int|null","description":"[optional] defaults to the value of time()"}],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"strip_tags","fqn":"strip_tags","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_1.php","range":{"start":32315,"end":32325}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"allowed_tags","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string[]|string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Strip HTML and PHP tags from a string The input string. </p> You can use the optional second parameter to specify tags which should not be stripped. </p> <p> HTML comments and PHP tags are also stripped. This is hardcoded and can not be changed with allowable_tags. </p> /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"allowed_tags","declared_type":"string[]|string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"stripcslashes","fqn":"stripcslashes","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"standard","location":{"file":"standard/standard_1.php","range":{"start":9584,"end":9597}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Un-quote string quoted with <function>addcslashe