se},{"name":"svn_repos_recover","fqn":"svn_repos_recover","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"svn","location":{"file":"svn/svn.php","range":{"start":22569,"end":22586}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"path","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PECL svn &gt;= 0.1.0)<br/> Run recovery procedures on the repository located at path. Its description </p> /","params":[{"name":"path","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"svn_resolved","fqn":"svn_resolved","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"svn","location":{"file":"svn/svn.php","range":{"start":11632,"end":11644}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":null,"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"svn_revert","fqn":"svn_revert","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"svn","location":{"file":"svn/svn.php","range":{"start":11581,"end":11591}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"path","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"recursive","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PECL svn &gt;= 0.3.0)<br/> Revert changes to the working copy The path to the working repository. </p> Optionally make recursive changes. </p> /","params":[{"name":"path","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"recursive","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"svn_status","fqn":"svn_status","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"svn","location":{"file":"svn/svn.php","range":{"start":17214,"end":17224}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"path","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"(PECL svn &gt;= 0.1.0)<br/> Returns the status of working copy files and directories Local path to file or directory to retrieve status of. </p> Relative paths will be resolved as if the current working directory was the one that contains the PHP binary. To use the calling script&#x00027;s working directory, use <b>realpath</b> or dirname(__FILE__). Any combination of <b>SVN_NON_RECURSIVE</b>, <b>SVN_ALL</b> (regardless of modification status), <b>SVN_SHOW_UPDATES</b> (entries will be added for items that are out-of-date), <b>SVN_NO_IGNORE</b> (disregard svn:ignore properties when scanning for new files) and <b>SVN_IGNORE_EXTERNALS</b>. </p> the status of items in the repository: </p> <pre> Array ( [0] => Array ( // information on item ) [1] => ... ) </pre> <p> The information on the item is an associative array that can contain the following keys: </p> path String path to file/directory of this entry on local filesystem. text_status Status of item's text. Refer to status constants for possible values. repos_text_status Status of item's text in repository. Only accurate if <i>update</i> was set to <b>TRUE</b>. Refer to status constants for possible values. prop_status Status of item's properties. Refer to status constants for possible values. repos_prop_status Status of item's property in repository. Only accurate if <i>update</i> was set to <b>TRUE</b>. Refer to status constants for possible values. locked Whether or not the item is locked. (Only set if <b>TRUE</b>.) copied Whether or not the item was copied (scheduled for addition with history). (Only set if <b>TRUE</b>.) switched Whether or not the item was switched using the switch command. (Only set if <b>TRUE</b>) <p> These keys are only set if the item is versioned: </p> name Base name of item in repository. url URL of item in repository. repos Base URL of repository. revision Integer revision of item in working copy. kind Type of item, i.e. file or directory. Refer to type constants for possible values. schedule Scheduled action for item, i.e. addition or deletion. Constants for these magic numbers are not available, they can be emulated by using: <code> if (!defined('svn_wc_schedule_normal')) { define('svn_wc_schedule_normal', 0); // nothing special define('svn_wc_schedule_add', 1); // item will be added define('svn_wc_schedule_delete', 2); // item will be deleted define('svn_wc_schedule_replace', 3); // item will be added and deleted } </code> deleted Whether or not the item was deleted, but parent revision lags behind. (Only set if <b>TRUE</b>.) absent Whether or not the item is absent, that is, Subversion knows that there should be something there but there isn't. (Only set if <b>TRUE</b>.) incomplete Whether or not the entries file for a directory is incomplete. (Only set if <b>TRUE</b>.) cmt_date Integer Unix timestamp of last commit date. (Unaffected by <i>update</i>.) cmt_rev Integer revision of last commit. (Unaffected by <i>update</i>.) cmt_author String author of last commit. (Unaffected by <i>update /","params":[{"name":"path","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"svn_switch","fqn":"svn_switch","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":