e <i>is_final</i> parameter is set and <b>TRUE</b> when the last data is parsed. </p> If set and <b>TRUE</b>, <i>data</i> is the last piece of data sent in this parse. </p> <p> For unsuccessful parses, error information can be retrieved with <b>xml_get_error_code</b>, <b>xml_error_string</b>, <b>xml_get_current_line_number</b>, <b>xml_get_current_column_number</b> and <b>xml_get_current_byte_index</b>. </p> <p> Entity errors are reported at the end of the data thus only if <i>is_final</i> is set and <b>TRUE</b>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":"XMLParser|resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"is_final","declared_type":"bool","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"xml_parse_into_struct","fqn":"xml_parse_into_struct","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"xml","location":{"file":"xml/xml.php","range":{"start":15358,"end":15379}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"XMLParser|resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"values","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true},{"name":"index","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":true}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Parse XML data into an array structure A reference to the XML parser. </p> A string containing the XML data. </p> An array containing the values of the XML data </p> An array containing pointers to the location of the appropriate values in the $values. </p> success. This is not the same as <b>FALSE</b> and <b>TRUE</b>, be careful with operators such as ===. /","params":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":"XMLParser|resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"data","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null},{"name":"","declared_type":null,"description":null}],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"xml_parser_create","fqn":"xml_parser_create","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"xml","location":{"file":"xml/xml.php","range":{"start":1125,"end":1142}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false|XMLParser"},"documentation":{"description":"Create an XML parser The optional <i>encoding</i> specifies the character encoding for the input/output in PHP 4. Starting from PHP 5, the input encoding is automatically detected, so that the <i>encoding</i> parameter specifies only the output encoding. In PHP 4, the default output encoding is the same as the input charset. If empty string is passed, the parser attempts to identify which encoding the document is encoded in by looking at the heading 3 or 4 bytes. In PHP 5.0.0 and 5.0.1, the default output charset is ISO-8859-1, while in PHP 5.0.2 and upper is UTF-8. The supported encodings are ISO-8859-1, UTF-8 and US-ASCII. </p> /","params":[{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false|XMLParser","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"xml_parser_create_ns","fqn":"xml_parser_create_ns","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"xml","location":{"file":"xml/xml.php","range":{"start":2255,"end":2275}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false|XMLParser"},"documentation":{"description":"Create an XML parser with namespace support The optional <i>encoding</i> specifies the character encoding for the input/output in PHP 4. Starting from PHP 5, the input encoding is automatically detected, so that the <i>encoding</i> parameter specifies only the output encoding. In PHP 4, the default output encoding is the same as the input charset. In PHP 5.0.0 and 5.0.1, the default output charset is ISO-8859-1, while in PHP 5.0.2 and upper is UTF-8. The supported encodings are ISO-8859-1, UTF-8 and US-ASCII. </p> With a namespace aware parser tag parameters passed to the various handler functions will consist of namespace and tag name separated by the string specified in <i>separator</i>. </p> /","params":[{"name":"encoding","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"resource|false|XMLParser","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"xml_parser_free","fqn":"xml_parser_free","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"xml","location":{"file":"xml/xml.php","range":{"start":18722,"end":18737}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"XMLParser|resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Free an XML parser refer to a valid parser, or else it frees the parser and returns <b>TRUE</b>. /","params":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":"XMLParser|resource","description":"A reference to the XML parser to free."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"xml_parser_get_option","fqn":"xml_parser_get_option","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"xml","location":{"file":"xml/xml.php","range":{"start":21747,"end":21768}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"XMLParser|resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"string|int|bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Get options from an XML parser and <b>XML_OPTION_TARGET_ENCODING</b> are available. See <b>xml_parser_set_option</b> for their description. not refer to a valid parser or if <i>option</i> isn't valid (generates also a <b>E_WARNING</b>). Else the option's value is returned. 8.0.0, passing an invalid value to option generated a E_WARNING as well as making the function return false. /","params":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":"XMLParser|resource","description":"A reference to the XML parser to get an option from."},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","description":"Which option to fetch. <b>XML_OPTION_CASE_FOLDING</b>"}],"return_type":"string|int|bool","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"xml_parser_set_option","fqn":"xml_parser_set_option","kind":"Function","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"xml","location":{"file":"xml/xml.php","range":{"start":20684,"end":20705}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"XMLParser|resource","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"value","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"mixed","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Set options in an XML parser A reference to the XML parser to set an option in. </p> Which option to set. See below. </p> <p> The following options are available: <table> XML parser options <tr valign=\"top\"> <td>Option constant</td> <td>Data type</td> <td>Description</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>XML_OPTION_CASE_FOLDING</b></td> <td>integer</td> <td> Controls whether case-folding is enabled for this XML parser. Enabled by default. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>XML_OPTION_SKIP_TAGSTART</b></td> <td>integer</td> <td> Specify how many characters should be skipped in the beginning of a tag name. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>XML_OPTION_SKIP_WHITE</b></td> <td>integer</td> <td> Whether to skip values consisting of whitespace characters. </td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\"> <td><b>XML_OPTION_TARGET_ENCODING</b></td> <td>string</td> <td> Sets which target encoding to use in this XML parser.By default, it is set to the same as the source encoding used by <b>xml_parser_create</b>. Supported target encodings are ISO-8859-1, US-ASCII and UTF-8. </td> </tr> </table> </p> The option's new value. </p> refer to a valid parser, or if the option could not be set. Else the option is set and <b>TRUE</b> is returned. 8.0.0, passing an invalid value to option generated an E_WARNING and made the function return false. /","params":[{"name":"parser","declared_type":"XMLParser|resource","description":"<p>"},{"name":"option","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"value","declared_type":"mixed","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"xml_set_character_data_handler","fqn":"xml_set_charact