,"kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":11952,"end":11971}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns a bit mask of recommended backends for current platform. Returns the set of all backends compiled into this binary of libev and also recommended for this platform, meaning it will work for most file descriptor types. This set is often smaller than the one returned by Ev::supportedBackends(), as for example kqueue is broken on most BSD systems and will not be auto-detected unless it is requested explicitly. This is the set of backends that libev will probe with no backends specified explicitly. /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"resume","fqn":"Ev::resume","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":12736,"end":12742}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"Resume previously suspended default event loop. Ev::suspend() and Ev::resume() methods suspend and resume a loop correspondingly. All timer watchers will be delayed by the time spend between suspend and resume , and all periodic watchers will be rescheduled(that is, they will lose any events that would have occurred while suspended). After calling Ev::suspend() it is not allowed to call any function on the given loop other than Ev::resume(). Also it is not allowed to call Ev::resume() without a previous call to Ev::suspend(). Calling suspend / resume has the side effect of updating the event loop time (see Ev::nowUpdate()). /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"run","fqn":"Ev::run","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":13386,"end":13389}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"Begin checking for events and calling callbacks for the default loop. Begin checking for events and calling callbacks for the default loop . Returns when a callback calls Ev::stop() method, or the flags are nonzero(in which case the return value is true) or when there are no active watchers which reference the loop( EvWatcher::keepalive() is TRUE), in which case the return value will be FALSE. The return value can generally be interpreted as if TRUE, there is more work left to do. /","params":[{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"One of the Ev::FLAG_* flags"}],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"sleep","fqn":"Ev::sleep","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":13596,"end":13601}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"float","phpdoc_type":"float","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"Block the process for the given number of seconds. /","params":[{"name":"seconds","declared_type":"float","description":"Fractional number of seconds"}],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"stop","fqn":"Ev::stop","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":13770,"end":13774}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"h