ptional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"owned","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"persistent","declared_type":"bool","phpdoc_type":"bool","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"CData|null"},"documentation":{"description":"Method that creates an arbitrary C structure. Creates a native data structure of the given C type. Any type declared for the instance is allowed. Note: Calling {@see FFI::new()} statically is deprecated since PHP 8.3. or an instance of {@see FFI\\CType} which has already been created. data. Managed data lives together with the returned {@see FFI\\CData} object, and is released when the last reference to that object is released by regular PHP reference counting or GC. Unmanaged data should be released by calling {@see FFI::free()}, when no longer needed. permanently on the system heap (using `malloc()`), or on the PHP request heap (using `emalloc()`). object, or {@see null} on failure for PHP versions prior to 8.4. /","params":[{"name":"type","declared_type":"string|CType","description":"is a valid C declaration as {@see string},"},{"name":"owned","declared_type":"bool","description":"Whether to create owned (i.e. managed) or unmanaged"},{"name":"persistent","declared_type":"bool","description":"Whether to allocate the C data structure"}],"return_type":"CData|null","var_type":null,"throws":["ParserException"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"scope","fqn":"FFI::scope","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"FFI","location":{"file":"FFI/FFI.php","range":{"start":5649,"end":5654}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"FFI","phpdoc_return_type":"FFI"},"documentation":{"description":"FFI definition parsing and shared library loading may take significant time. It's not useful to do it on each HTTP request in the WEB environment. However, it's possible to preload FFI definitions and libraries at php startup, and instantiate FFI objects when necessary. Header files may be extended with `FFI_SCOPE` define (default preloading scope is \"C\"). This name is going to be used as {@see FFI::scope()} argument. It's possible to preload a few files into a single scope. ```c #define FFI_LIB \"libc.so.6\" #define FFI_SCOPE \"libc\" int printf(const char *format, ...); ``` These files are loaded through the same FFI::load() load function, executed from a file loaded by `opcache.preload` in the `php.ini` directive. ```c ffi.preload=/etc/php/ffi/printf.h ``` Finally, FFI::scope() instantiates an FFI object that implements all C definitions from the given scope. ```php $ffi = FFI::scope(\"libc\"); $ffi->printf(\"Hello world!\\n\"); ``` /","params":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","description":"The scope name defined by a special `FFI_SCOPE` define."}],"return_type":"FFI","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"sizeof","fqn":"FFI::sizeof","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"FFI","location":{"file":"FFI/FFI.php","range":{"start":12427,"end":12433}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"ptr","declared_type":"CData|CType","phpdoc_type":"CData|CType","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int<0, max>"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the size of a C data type of the given {@see FFI\\CData} or {@see FFI\\CType}. /","params":[{"name":"ptr","declared_type":"CData|CType","description":"The handle of the C data or type."}],"return_type":"int<0, max>","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"string"