 the actual key for the item, we hash on the server key when deciding which memcached server to talk to. This allows related items to be grouped together on a single server for efficiency with multi operations. </p> The key under which to store the value. </p> The value to store. </p> The expiration time, defaults to 0. See Expiration Times for more info. </p> The <b>Memcached::getResultCode</b> will return <b>Memcached::RES_NOTSTORED</b> if the key already exists. /","params":[{"name":"server_key","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"key","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"value","declared_type":"mixed","description":"<p>"},{"name":"expiration","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"addServer","fqn":"Memcached::addServer","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"memcached","location":{"file":"memcached/memcached.php","range":{"start":51621,"end":51630}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"host","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"port","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"weight","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PECL memcached &gt;= 0.1.0)<br/> Add a server to the server pool The hostname of the memcache server. If the hostname is invalid, data-related operations will set <b>Memcached::RES_HOST_LOOKUP_FAILURE</b> result code. </p> The port on which memcache is running. Usually, this is 11211. </p> The weight of the server relative to the total weight of all the servers in the pool. This controls the probability of the server being selected for operations. This is used only with consistent distribution option and usually corresponds to the amount of memory available to memcache on that server. </p> /","params":[{"name":"host","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"port","declared_type":"int","description":"<p>"},{"name":"weight","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"addServers","fqn":"Memcached::addServers","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"memcached","location":{"file":"memcached/memcached.php","range":{"start":51950,"end":51960}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"servers","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PECL memcached &gt;= 0.1.1)<br/> Add multiple servers to the server pool /","params":[{"name":"servers","declared_type":"array","description":null}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"append","fqn":"Memcached::append","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"memcached","location":{"file":"memcached/memcached.php","range":{"start":39306,"end":39312}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"key","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"value","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PECL memcached &gt;= 0.1.0)<br/> Append data to an existing item The key under which to store the value. </p> The string to append. </p> The <b>Memcached::getResultCode</b> will return <b>Memcached::RES_NOTSTORED</b> if the key doe