"MongoDB::createCollection","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mongo","location":{"file":"mongo/mongo.php","range":{"start":32031,"end":32047}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"options","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"MongoCollection"},"documentation":{"description":"Creates a collection <p> An array containing options for the collections. Each option is its own element in the options array, with the option name listed below being the key of the element. The supported options depend on the MongoDB server version. At the moment, the following options are supported: </p> <p> <b>capped</b> <p> If the collection should be a fixed size. </p> </p> <p> <b>size</b> <p> If the collection is fixed size, its size in bytes.</p></p> <p><b>max</b> <p>If the collection is fixed size, the maximum number of elements to store in the collection.</p></p> <i>autoIndexId</i> <p> If capped is <b>TRUE</b> you can specify <b>FALSE</b> to disable the automatic index created on the <em>_id</em> field. Before MongoDB 2.2, the default value for <em>autoIndexId</em> was <b>FALSE</b>. </p> </p> /","params":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","description":"The name of the collection."},{"name":"options","declared_type":"array","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"MongoCollection","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"createDBRef","fqn":"MongoDB::createDBRef","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mongo","location":{"file":"mongo/mongo.php","range":{"start":33641,"end":33652}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"collection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"b