mongo","location":{"file":"mongo/mongo.php","range":{"start":106310,"end":106321}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"collection","declared_type":"MongoCollection","phpdoc_type":"MongoCollection","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"write_options","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"<p>(PECL mongo &gt;= 1.5.0)</p> MongoUpdateBatch constructor. Its write concern will be copied and used as the default write concern if none is given as $write_options or during {@see MongoWriteBatch::execute()}.</p> </thead> <tbody class=\"tbody\"><tr><td>w (int|string)</td><td>{@link https://php.net/manual/en/mongo.writeconcerns.php Write concern} value</td></tr> <tr><td>wtimeout (int)</td><td>{@link https://php.net/manual/en/mongo.writeconcerns.php Maximum time to wait for replication}</td></tr> <tr><td>ordered</td><td>Determins if MongoDB must apply this batch in order (sequentally, one item at a time) or can rearrange it. Defaults to <strong><code>TRUE</code></strong></td></tr> <tr><td>j (bool)</td><td>Wait for journaling on the primary. This value is discouraged, use WriteConcern instead</td></tr> <tr><td>fsync (bool)</td><td>Wait for fsync on the primary. This value is discouraged, use WriteConcern instead</td></tr> </tbody></table> /","params":[{"name":"collection","declared_type":"MongoCollection","description":"<p>The MongoCollection to execute the batch on."},{"name":"write_options","declared_type":"array","description":"<p class=\"para\">An array of Write Options.</p><table class=\"doctable informaltable\"><thead><tr><th>key</th><th>value meaning</th></tr>"}],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"__construct","fqn":"MongoWriteBatch::__construct","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mongo","location":{"file":"mongo/mongo.php","range":{"start":102040,"end":102051}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"collection","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"MongoCollection","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"batch_type","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"write_options","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":null},"documentation":{"description":"<p>(PECL mongo &gt;= 1.5.0)</p> MongoWriteBatch constructor. Its {@link https://php.net/manual/en/mongo.writeconcerns.php write concern} will be copied and used as the default write concern if none is given as <code >$write_options</code> or during {@see MongoWriteBatch::execute()}. One of: </p><ul> <li class=\"member\"><em>0</em> - make an MongoWriteBatch::COMMAND_INSERT batch</li> <li class=\"member\"><em>1</em> - make an MongoWriteBatch::COMMAND_UPDATE batch</li> <li class=\"member\"><em>2</em> - make a  MongoWriteBatch::COMMAND_DELETE batch</li> </ul> <p> An array of Write Options.</p><table><thead><tr><th>key</th><th>value meaning</th></tr> </thead> <tbody><tr><td>w (int|string)</td><td>{@link https://php.net/manual/en/mongo.writeconcerns.php Write concern} value</td></tr> <tr><td>wtimeout (int)</td><td>{@link https://php.net/manual/en/mongo.writeconcerns.php Maximum time to wait for replication}</td></tr> <tr><td>ordered</td><td>Determins if MongoDB must apply this batch in order (sequentally, one item at a time) or can rearrange it. Defaults to <strong><code>TRUE</code></strong></td></tr> <tr><td>j (bool)</td><td>Wait for journaling on the primary. This value is discouraged, use WriteConcern instead</td></tr> <tr><td>fsync (bool)</td><td>Wait for fsync on the primary. This value is discouraged, use WriteConcern instead</td></tr> </tbody></table> /","params":[{"name":"collection","declared_type":"MongoCollection","description":"The {@see MongoCollection} to execute the batch on."},{"name":"batch_type","declared_type":"string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"write_options","declared_type":"array","description":"[optional]"}],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"add","fqn":"MongoWriteBatch::add","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mongo","location":{"file":"mongo/mongo.php","range":{"start":104140,"end":104143}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"item","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>(PECL mongo &gt;= 1.5.0)</p> Adds a write operation to a batch An array that describes a write operation. The structure of this value depends on the batch's operation type. </p><table> <thead> <tr> <th>Batch type</th> <th>Argument expectation</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong><code>MongoWriteBatch::COMMAND_INSERT</code></strong></td> <td> The document to add. </td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><code>MongoWriteBatch::COMMAND_UPDATE</code></strong></td> <td> <p>Raw update operation.</p> <p>Required keys are <em>\"q\"</em> and <em>\"u\"</em>, which correspond to the <code>$criteria</code> and <code>$new_object</code> parameters of {@see MongoCollection::update()}, respectively.</p> <p>Optional keys are <em>\"multi\"</em> and <em>\"upsert\"</em>, which correspond to the <em>\"multiple\"</em> and <em>\"upsert\"</em> options for {@see MongoCollection::update()}, respectively. If unspecified, both options default to <strong><code>FALSE</code></strong>.</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong><code>MongoWriteBatch::COMMAND_DELETE</code></strong></td> <td> <p class=\"para\">Raw delete operation.</p> <p>Required keys are: <em>\"q\"</em> and <em>\"limit\"</em>, which correspond to the <code>$criteria</code> parameter and <em>\"justOne\"</em> option of {@see MongoCollection::remove()}, respectively.</p> <p>The <em>\"limit\"</em> option is an integer; however, MongoDB only supports <em>0</em> (i.e. remove all matching ocuments) and <em>1</em> (i.e. remove at most one matching document) at this time.</p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> /","params":[{"name":"item","declared_type":"array","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"execute","fqn":"MongoWriteBatch::execute","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mongo","location":{"file":"mongo/mongo.php","range":{"start":104830,"end":104837}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"write_options","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>(PECL mongo &gt;= 1.5.0)</p> Executes a batch of write operations If the batch had to be split into multiple batches, the return value will aggregate the values from individual batches and return only the totals. If the batch was empty, an array containing only the 'ok' field is returned (as <b>TRUE</b>) although nothing will be shipped over the wire (NOOP). /","params":[{"name":"write_options","declared_type":"array","description":"See {@see MongoWriteBatch::__construct}"}],"return_type":"array","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getDocument","fqn":"MongoWriteConcernException::getDocument","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mongo","location":{"file":"mongo/mongo.php","range":{"start":107090,"end":107101}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"array"},"documentation":{"description":"Get