nfo","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysqli","location":{"file":"mysqli/mysqli.php","range":{"start":10927,"end":10942}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Dump debugging information into the log /","params":[],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"escape_string","fqn":"mysqli::escape_string","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysqli","location":{"file":"mysqli/mysqli.php","range":{"start":29404,"end":29417}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"string","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Escapes special characters in a string for use in an SQL statement, taking into account the current charset of the connection Characters encoded are NUL (ASCII 0), \\n, \\r, \\, ', \", and Control-Z. /","params":[{"name":"string","declared_type":"string","description":"The string to be escaped."}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"execute_query","fqn":"mysqli::execute_query","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysqli","location":{"file":"mysqli/mysqli.php","range":{"start":14269,"end":14282}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"query","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"params","declared_type":"?array","phpdoc_type":"array|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"mysqli_result|bool","phpdoc_return_type":"mysqli_result|bool"},"documentation":{"description":"<p>Prepares the SQL query, binds parameters, and executes it. The mysqli::execute_query() method is a shortcut for mysqli::prepare(), mysqli_stmt::bind_param(), mysqli_stmt::execute(), and mysqli_stmt::get_result().</p> <p>The statement template can contain zero or more question mark (?) parameter markers⁠—also called placeholders. The parameter values must be provided as an array using params parameter.</p> <p>A prepared statement is created under the hood but it's never exposed outside of the function. It's impossible to access properties of the statement as one would do with the mysqli_stmt object. Due to this limitation, the status information is copied to the mysqli object and is available using its methods, e.g. mysqli_affected_rows() or mysqli_error().</p> statement. The SQL statement may contain zero or more parameter markers represented by question mark (?) characters at the appropriate positions. <b>Note:</b> The markers are legal only in certain places in SQL statements. For example, they are permitted in the VALUES() list of an INSERT statement (to specify column values for a row), or in a comparison with a column in a WHERE clause to specify a comparison value. However, they are not permitted for identifiers (such as table or column names). there are bound parameters in the SQL statement being executed. Each value is treated as a string. which produce a result set, such as SELECT, SHOW, DESCRIBE or EXPLAIN, returns a mysqli_result object. For other successful queries, returns true. /","params":[{"name":"query","declared_type":"string","description":"The query, as a string. It must consist of a single SQL"},{"name":"params","declared_type":"array|null","description":"An optional list array with as many elements as"}],"return_type":"mysqli_result|bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"get_charset","fqn":"mysqli::get_charset","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"mysqli","location":{"file":"mysqli/mysqli.php","