phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= 5.1.0, PHP 7, PECL pdo &gt;= 0.1.0)<br/> Set an attribute /","params":[{"name":"attribute","declared_type":"int","description":null},{"name":"value","declared_type":"mixed","description":null}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":["PDOException"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqliteCreateAggregate","fqn":"PDO::sqliteCreateAggregate","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":60616,"end":60637}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"function_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"step_func","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"finalize_func","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"num_args","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= 5.1.0, PHP 7, PECL pdo_sqlite &gt;= 1.0.0)<br/> Registers an aggregating User Defined Function for use in SQL statements The name of the function used in SQL statements. </p> Callback function called for each row of the result set. Your PHP function should accumulate the result and store it in the aggregation context. </p> Callback function to aggregate the \"stepped\" data from each row. Once all the rows have been processed, this function will be called and it should then take the data from the aggregation context and return the result. This callback function should return a type understood by SQLite (i.e. scalar type). </p> Hint to the SQLite parser if the callback function accepts a predetermined number of arguments. </p> /","params":[{"name":"function_name","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"step_func","declared_type":"callable","description":"<p>"},{"name":"finalize_func","declared_type":"callable","description":"<p>"},{"name":"num_args","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqliteCreateCollation","fqn":"PDO::sqliteCreateCollation","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":61641,"end":61662}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"callback","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= 5.3.11, PHP 7)<br/> Registers a User Defined Function for use as a collating function in SQL statements Name of the SQL collating function to be created or redefined. </p> The name of a PHP function or user-defined function to apply as a callback, defining the behavior of the collation. It should accept two strings and return as strcmp() does, i.e. it should return -1, 1, or 0 if the first string sorts before, sorts after, or is equal to the second. </p> /","params":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"sqliteCreateFunction","fqn":"PDO::sqliteCreateFunction","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":62917,"end":62937}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"function_name","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"callback","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"num_args","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP 5 &gt;= 5.1.0, PHP 7, PECL pdo_sqlite &gt;= 1.0.0)<br/> Registers a User Defined Function for use in SQL statements The name of the function used in SQL statements. </p> Callback function to handle the defined SQL function. </p> The number of arguments that the SQL function takes. If this parameter is -1, then the SQL function may take any number of arguments. </p> A bitwise conjunction of flags. Currently, only <b>PDO::SQLITE_DETERMINISTIC</b> is supported, which specifies that the function always returns the same result given the same inputs within a single SQL statement. </p> /","params":[{"name":"function_name","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","description":"<p>"},{"name":"num_args","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"[optional] <p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getApiVersion","fqn":"Pdo\\Firebird::getApiVersion","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":116174,"end":116187}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the API version Returns the Firebird API version as defined by the C constant FB_API_VER in ibase.h. /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"getWarningCount","fqn":"Pdo\\Mysql::getWarningCount","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":104607,"end":104622}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Returns the number of warnings from the last executed query query. /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"copyFromArray","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::copyFromArray","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":106742,"end":106755}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"rows","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"array","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Copy data from a PHP array into a table Copies data from rows array to table tableName using separator as fields delimiter and fields list. separator. /","params":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","description":"String containing table name."},{"name":"rows","declared_type":"array","description":"An indexed array (or Traversable) of strings with fields separated by"},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","description":"Delimiter used to separate fields in an entry of the rows array."},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","description":"How to interpret SQL NULL values."},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"string|null","description":"List of fields to insert."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"copyFromFile","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::copyFromFile","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":107947,"end":107959}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Copy data from file into table Copies data from file specified by filename into table tableName using separator as fields delimiter and fields list through the connection's error handling (see PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE); with PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION a PDOException is thrown. /","params":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","description":"String containing table name."},{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"Filename containing the data to import."},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","description":"Delimiter used to separate fields in an entry of the rows array."},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","description":"How to interpret SQL NULL values."},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"string|null","description":"List of fields to insert."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":["\\PDOException"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"copyToArray","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::copyToArray","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":108825,"end":108836}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Copy data from database table into PHP array Copies data from tableName into array using separator as fields delimiter and fields list /","params":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","description":"String containing table name."},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","description":"Delimiter used to separate fields in an entry of the rows array."},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","description":"How to interpret SQL NULL values."},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"string|null","description":"List of fields to export."}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"copyToFile","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::copyToFile","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":110009,"end":110019}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Copy data from table into file Copies data from table into file specified by filename using separator as fields delimiter and fields list. the failure is reported through the connection's error handling (see PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE); with PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION a PDOException is thrown. /","params":[{"name":"tableName","declared_type":"string","description":"String containing table name."},{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"Filename to export data."},{"name":"separator","declared_type":"string","description":"Delimiter used to separate fields in an entry of the rows array."},{"name":"nullAs","declared_type":"string","description":"How to interpret SQL NULL values."},{"name":"fields","declared_type":"string|null","description":"List of fields to export."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":["\\PDOException"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"escapeIdentifier","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::escapeIdentifier","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":110940,"end":110956}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"input","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"string","phpdoc_return_type":"string"},"documentation":{"description":"Escapes a string for use as an SQL identifier Escapes a string for use as an SQL identifier, such as a table, column, or function name. This is useful when a user-supplied identifier might contain special characters that would otherwise not be interpreted as part of the identifier by the SQL parser, or when the identifier might contain upper case characters whose case should be preserved. /","params":[{"name":"input","declared_type":"string","description":"A string containing text to be escaped."}],"return_type":"string","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getNotify","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::getNotify","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":112357,"end":112366}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"fetchMode","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"timeoutMilliseconds","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"array|false","phpdoc_return_type":"array|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Get asynchronous notification Returns a result set representing a pending asynchronous notification. following constants: PDO::FETCH_DEFAULT PDO::FETCH_BOTH PDO::FETCH_ASSOC PDO::FETCH_NUM milliseconds. false. The row has a message field (the channel name) and a pid field (the process ID of the notifying backend). If the notification carries a non-empty payload, the row also has a payload field. With PDO::FETCH_NUM, these fields are at indexes 0, 1, and 2. PDO::FETCH_* constants. A ValueError is thrown if timeoutMilliseconds is less than 0. A E_WARNING is raised when timeoutMilliseconds is greater than the value that can be contained in a signed 32-bit integer, in which case it will be the maximum value of a signed 32-bit integer. /","params":[{"name":"fetchMode","declared_type":"int","description":"The format the result set should be returned as, one of the"},{"name":"timeoutMilliseconds","declared_type":"int","description":"The length of time to wait for a response, in"}],"return_type":"array|false","var_type":null,"throws":["\\ValueError"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"getPid","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::getPid","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":112892,"end":112898}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"int","phpdoc_return_type":"int"},"documentation":{"description":"Get the PID of the backend process handling this connection Returns the PID of the backend process handling this connection. Note that the PID belongs to a process executing on the database server host, not the local host. /","params":[],"return_type":"int","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"lobCreate","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::lobCreate","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":113381,"end":113390}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"string|false","phpdoc_return_type":"string|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Creates a new large object Pdo\\Pgsql::lobCreate creates a large object and returns the OID which refers to it. It can be opened to read or write data with Pdo\\Pgsql::lobOpen. false on failure. /","params":[],"return_type":"string|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"lobOpen","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::lobOpen","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":113645,"end":113652}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"oid","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mode","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":null,"optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":null,"phpdoc_return_type":"resource|false"},"documentation":{"description":"Opens an existing large object stream. Must be called inside a transaction. /","params":[],"return_type":"resource|false","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"lobUnlink","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::lobUnlink","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":114231,"end":114240}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"oid","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Deletes the large object Pdo\\Pgsql::lobCreate creates a large object and returns the OID which refers to it. It can be opened to read or write data with Pdo\\Pgsql::lobOpen. Deletes a large object from the database identified by OID. /","params":[{"name":"oid","declared_type":"string","description":"A large object identifier."}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"setNoticeCallback","fqn":"Pdo\\Pgsql::setNoticeCallback","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":115156,"end":115173}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"callback","declared_type":"?callable","phpdoc_type":"callable|null","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"Set a callback to handle notice and warning messages generated by the backend Set a callback to handle notice and warning messages generated by the backend. This includes messages emitted by PostgreSQL itself, as well as those raised by user-defined SQL functions using RAISE. Please note that the actual receipt of these messages depends on the backend setting client_min_messages. state. Otherwise, the handler is a callback with the following signature: voidhandler stringmessage message A message generated by the backend. /","params":[{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable|null","description":"If null is passed, the handler is reset to its default"}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"createAggregate","fqn":"Pdo\\Sqlite::createAggregate","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":98866,"end":98881}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"step","declared_type":"callable","phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"finalize","declared_type":"callable","phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"numArgs","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Registers an aggregating user-defined function for use in SQL statements This method is similar to Pdo\\Sqlite::createFunction except that it registers functions that can be used to calculate a result aggregated across all the rows of a query. callback should accumulate the result and store it in the aggregation context. This function need to be defined as: mixedstep mixedcontext intrownumber mixedvalue mixedvalues context null for the first row; on subsequent rows it will have the value that was previously returned from the step function; you should use this to maintain the aggregate state. rownumber The current row number. value The first argument passed to the aggregate. values Further arguments passed to the aggregate. The return value of this function will be used as the context argument in the next call of the step or finalize functions. row. Once all the rows have been processed, this function will be called, and it should then take the data from the aggregation context and return the result. This callback function should return a type understood by SQLite (i.e. scalar type). This function need to be defined as: mixedfini mixedcontext introwcount context Holds the return value from the very last call to the step function. rowcount Holds the number of rows over which the aggregate was performed. The return value of this function will be used as the return value for the aggregate. predetermined number of arguments. /","params":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","description":"The name of the function used in SQL statements."},{"name":"step","declared_type":"callable","description":"Callback function called for each row of the result set. The"},{"name":"finalize","declared_type":"callable","description":"Callback function to aggregate the \"stepped\" data from each"},{"name":"numArgs","declared_type":"int","description":"Hint to the SQLite parser if the callback function accepts a"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"createCollation","fqn":"Pdo\\Sqlite::createCollation","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":99990,"end":100005}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Registers a user-defined function for use as a collating function in SQL statements This method is similar to Pdo\\Sqlite::createFunction except that it registers functions that are used to collate strings. must accept two strings and return -1, 0, or 1 if the first string sorts before, sorts identically, or sorts after the second string respectively. An internal function that behaves like this is strcmp. This function need to be defined as: intcollation stringstring1 stringstring2 /","params":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","description":"Name of the SQL collating function to be created or redefined."},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","description":"Callback function that defines the behaviour of a collation. It"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"createFunction","fqn":"Pdo\\Sqlite::createFunction","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":101515,"end":101529}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"function_name","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","phpdoc_type":"callable","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"num_args","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","phpdoc_type":"int","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Registers a user-defined function for use in SQL statements This method allows PHP function to be registered with SQLite as a user-defined function, so that it can be called within SQL queries. The defined function can be used in any SQL query that allows function calls, for example SELECT, UPDATE, or triggers. functions should return a type understood by SQLite (i.e. scalar type). This function need to be defined as: mixedcallback mixedvalue mixedvalues value The first argument passed to the SQL function. values Further arguments passed to the SQL function. parameter is -1, then the SQL function may take any number of arguments. supported, which specifies that the function always returns the same result given the same inputs within a single SQL statement. /","params":[{"name":"function_name","declared_type":"string","description":"The name of the function used in SQL statements."},{"name":"callback","declared_type":"callable","description":"Callback function to handle the defined SQL function. Callback"},{"name":"num_args","declared_type":"int","description":"The number of arguments that the SQL function takes. If this"},{"name":"flags","declared_type":"int","description":"A bitmask of flags. Currently, only Pdo\\Sqlite::DETERMINISTIC is"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"loadExtension","fqn":"Pdo\\Sqlite::loadExtension","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"PDO","location":{"file":"PDO/PDO.php","range":{"start":102024,"end":102037}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","phpdoc_type":"string","optional":false,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"Description Exceptions. /","params":[{"name":"name","declared_type":"string","description":"Description."}],"return_type":"void","var_type":null,"throws":["\\Exception"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"nam