 </p> /","params":[{"name":"filename","declared_type":"string","description":"<p>"}],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":["PharException"],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":true},{"name":"valid","fqn":"PharData::valid","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Phar","location":{"file":"Phar/Phar.php","range":{"start":52299,"end":52304}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[],"declared_return_type":"bool","phpdoc_return_type":"bool"},"documentation":{"description":"Check whether current DirectoryIterator position is a valid file /","params":[],"return_type":"bool","var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"webPhar","fqn":"PharData::webPhar","kind":"Method","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Phar","location":{"file":"Phar/Phar.php","range":{"start":89012,"end":89019}},"declared_type":null,"signature":{"parameters":[{"name":"alias","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"null|string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"index","declared_type":"?string","phpdoc_type":"string|null","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"fileNotFoundScript","declared_type":null,"phpdoc_type":"null|string","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"mimeTypes","declared_type":"array","phpdoc_type":"null|array","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false},{"name":"rewrite","declared_type":"?callable","phpdoc_type":"null|callable","optional":true,"variadic":false,"by_reference":false}],"declared_return_type":"void","phpdoc_return_type":"void"},"documentation":{"description":"(PHP &gt;= 5.3.0, PECL phar &gt;= 2.0.0)<br/> mapPhar for web-based phars. front controller for web applications The alias that can be used in phar:// URLs to refer to this archive, rather than its full path. </p> The location within the phar of the directory index. </p> The location of the script to run when a file is not found. This script should output the proper HTTP 404 headers. </p> An array mapping additional file extensions to MIME type. If the default mapping is sufficient, pass an empty array. By default, these extensions are mapped to these MIME types: <code> $mimes = array( 'phps' => Phar::PHPS, // pass to highlight_file() 'c' => 'text/plain', 'cc' => 'text/plain', 'cpp' => 'text/plain', 'c++' => 'text/plain', 'dtd' => 'text/plain', 'h' => 'text/plain', 'log' => 'text/plain', 'rng' => 'text/plain', 'txt' => 'text/plain', 'xsd' => 'text/plain', 'php' => Phar::PHP, // parse as PHP 'inc' => Phar::PHP, // parse as PHP 'avi' => 'video/avi', 'bmp' => 'image/bmp', 'css' => 'text/css', 'gif' => 'image/gif', 'htm' => 'text/html', 'html' => 'text/html', 'htmls' => 'text/html', 'ico' => 'image/x-ico', 'jpe' => 'image/jpeg', 'jpg' => 'image/jpeg', 'jpeg' => 'image/jpeg', 'js' => 'application/x-javascript', 'midi' => 'audio/midi', 'mid' => 'audio/midi', 'mod' => 'audio/mod', 'mov' => 'movie/quicktime', 'mp3' => 'audio/mp3', 'mpg' => 'video/mpeg', 'mpeg' => 'video/mpeg', 'pdf' => 'application/pdf', 'png' => 'image/png', 'swf' => 'application/shockwave-flash', 'tif' => 'image/tiff', 'tiff' => 'image/tiff', 'wav' => 'audio/wav', 'xbm' => 'image/xbm', 'xml' => 'text/xml', ); </code> </p> The rewrites function is passed a string as its only parameter and must return a string or <b>FALSE</b>. </p> <p> If you are using fast-cgi or cgi then the parameter passed to the function is the value of the $_SERVER['PATH_INFO'] variable. Otherwise, the parameter passed to the function is the value of the $_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'] variable. </p> <p> If a string is returned it is used as the internal file path. If <b>FALSE</b> is returned then webPhar() will send a HTTP 403 Denied Code. </p> /","params":[{"name":"alias","declared_type":"null|string","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"index","declared_type":"string|null","description":"[optional] <p>"},{"name":"fileNotFoundSc