ecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"max_oids","fqn":"SNMP::max_oids","kind":"Property","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":287,"end":296}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"/","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":"int","throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"oid_increasing_check","fqn":"SNMP::oid_increasing_check","kind":"Property","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":3417,"end":3438}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p> Some SNMP agents are known for returning OIDs out of order but can complete the walk anyway. Other agents return OIDs that are out of order and can cause SNMP::walk() to loop indefinitely until memory limit will be reached. PHP SNMP library by default performs OID increasing check and stops walking on OID tree when it detects possible loop with issuing warning about non-increasing OID faced. Set oid_increasing_check to <b>FALSE</b> to disable this check. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":"bool","throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"oid_output_format","fqn":"SNMP::oid_output_format","kind":"Property","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":2729,"end":2747}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>OID .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.3.0 representation for various oid_output_format values <dl> <dt>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_FULL</dt><dd>.iso.org.dod.internet.mgmt.mib-2.system.sysUpTime.sysUpTimeInstance</dd> <dt>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_NUMERIC</dt><dd>.1.3.6.1.2.1.1.3.0</dd> <dt>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_MODULE</dt><dd>DISMAN-EVENT-MIB::sysUpTimeInstance</dd> <dt>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_SUFFIX</dt><dd>sysUpTimeInstance</dd> <dt>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_UCD</dt><dd>system.sysUpTime.sysUpTimeInstance</dd> <dt>SNMP_OID_OUTPUT_NONE</dt><dd>Undefined</dd> </dl> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":"int","throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"quick_print","fqn":"SNMP::quick_print","kind":"Property","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":1659,"end":1671}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<p>Sets the value of quick_print within the NET-SNMP library. When this is set (1), the SNMP library will return 'quick printed' values. This means that just the value will be printed. When quick_print is not enabled (default) the UCD SNMP library prints extra information including the type of the value (i.e. IpAddress or OID). Additionally, if quick_print is not enabled, the library prints additional hex values for all strings of three characters or less. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":"bool","throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"valueretrieval","fqn":"SNMP::valueretrieval","kind":"Property","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"snmp","location":{"file":"snmp/snmp.php","range":{"start":1003,"end":1018}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"<dl> <dt>SNMP_VALUE_LIBRARY</dt><dd>The return values will be as returned by the Net-SNMP library.</dd> <dt>SNMP_VALUE_PLAIN</dt><dd>The return values will be the plain value without the SNMP type hint.</dd> <dt>SNMP_VALUE_OBJECT</dt><dd>The return values will be objects with the properties \"value\" and \"type\", where the latter is one of the SNMP_OCTET_STR, SNMP_COUNTER etc. constants. The way \"value\" is returned is based on which one of SNMP_VALUE_LIBRARY, SNMP_VALUE_PLAIN is set</dd> <dl> /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":"int","throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"nam