flate::STRATEGY_FILT","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"http","location":{"file":"http/http3.php","range":{"start":84881,"end":84894}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Filtered compression strategy. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"STRATEGY_FIXED","fqn":"Deflate::STRATEGY_FIXED","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"http","location":{"file":"http/http3.php","range":{"start":86352,"end":86366}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Encoding with fixed Huffman codes only. > **A note on the compression strategy:** > > The strategy parameter is used to tune the compression algorithm. > > Use the value DEFAULT_STRATEGY for normal data, FILTERED for data produced by a filter (or predictor), HUFFMAN_ONLY to force Huffman encoding only (no string match), or RLE to limit match distances to one (run-length encoding). > > Filtered data consists mostly of small values with a somewhat random distribution. In this case, the compression algorithm is tuned to compress them better. The effect of FILTERED is to force more Huffman coding and less string matching; it is somewhat intermediate between DEFAULT_STRATEGY and HUFFMAN_ONLY. > > RLE is designed to be almost as fast as HUFFMAN_ONLY, but give better compression for PNG image data. > > FIXED prevents the use of dynamic Huffman codes, allowing for a simpler decoder for special applications. > > The strategy parameter only affects the compression ratio but not the correctness of the compressed output even if it is not set appropriately. > >_Source: [zlib Manual](http://www.zlib.net/manual.html)_ /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"STRATEGY_HUFF","fqn":"Deflate::STRATEGY_HUFF","kind":"ClassC