th lots of loop iterations, but usually is not noticeable. This flag setting cannot be overridden or specified in the LIBEV_FLAGS environment variable. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"FLAG_NOENV","fqn":"Ev::FLAG_NOENV","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":699,"end":709}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Flag passed to create a loop: If this flag used(or the program runs setuid or setgid), libev won't look at the environment variable LIBEV_FLAGS. Otherwise(by default), LIBEV_FLAGS will override the flags completely if it is found. Useful for performance tests and searching for bugs. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"FLAG_NOINOTIFY","fqn":"Ev::FLAG_NOINOTIFY","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":1514,"end":1528}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Flag passed to create a loop: When this flag is specified, libev won't attempt to use the inotify API for its ev_stat watchers. The flag can be useful to conserve inotify file descriptors, as otherwise each loop using ev_stat watchers consumes one inotify handle. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"FLAG_NOSIGMASK","fqn":"Ev::FLAG_NOSIGMASK","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":2394,"end":2408}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Flag passed to create a loop: When this flag is specified, libev will avoid to modify the signal mask. Specifically, this means having to make sure signals are unblocked before receiving them. This behaviour is useful for custom signal handling, or handling signals only in specific threads. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"FLAG_SIGNALFD","fqn":"Ev::FLAG_SIGNALFD","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":2015,"end":2028}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Flag passed to create a loop: When this flag is specified, libev will attempt to use the signalfd API for its ev_signal (and ev_child ) watchers. This API delivers signals synchronously, which makes it both faster and might make it possible to get the queued signal data. It can also simplify signal handling with threads, as long as signals are properly blocked in threads. Signalfd will not be used by default. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"IDLE","fqn":"Ev::IDLE","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":5001,"end":5005}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Event bitmask: EvIdle watcher works when there is nothing to do with other watchers. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"MAXPRI","fqn":"Ev::MAXPRI","kind":"ClassConstant","origin":"PhpRuntime","extension":"Ev","location":{"file":"Ev/Ev.php","range":{"start":3982,"end":3988}},"declared_type":null,"signature":null,"documentation":{"description":"Highest allowed watcher priority. /","params":[],"return_type":null,"var_type":null,"throws":[],"deprecated":null},"availability":{"since":null,"until":null},"is_static":false},{"name":"MINPRI","fqn":